		* Method:            UploadFileSbAsync
		* Purpose:           Creates an asynchronous task to call the UploadFileSb
		*                    method with the arguments provided. 
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        toChilkatStringBuilder, a Chilkat StringBuilder object.
		*                    tcFileName, mostly informational.
		*                    tcMimeType, specifies the MIME type, such as "application/pdf" or "text/plain"
		* Returns:           toChilkatTask, a Chilkat Task object.
		* Date Added:        07/23/2026
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 11.4.0.
		**
		** Creates an asynchronous task to call the UploadFileSb method with the arguments provided. 
		** (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		** 
		** Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. 
		** Accessing and updating UI elements existing in the main thread may require special considerations.
		**
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS toChilkatStringBuilder AS [Chilkat.StringBuilder], tcFileName AS Character, tcMimeType AS Character  
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS [Chilkat.Ai], loException AS Exception, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, loChilkatTask AS [Chilkat.Task], ;
		loParkParameterStringBuilder AS [iParkParameter OF ChilkatVFP.VCX], ;
		loChilkatStringBuilder AS [Chilkat.StringBuilder]
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterStringBuilder, m.loChilkatStringBuilder
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(11, 4, 0)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      loParkParameterStringBuilder = ;
		      NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], .ClassLibrary, [], m.oChilkatStringBuilder)
		
		      loChilkatStringBuilder = m.loParkParameterStringBuilder.GetObject()
		
		      TRY
		
		        loChilkatTask = m.loChilkatObject.UploadFileSbAsync(;
		        m.loChilkatStringBuilder, m.tcFileName, m.tcMimeType) 
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		      toChilkatStringBuilder = ;
		      m.loParkParameterStringBuilder.SetObject(m.oChilkatStringBuilder, m.loChilkatStringBuilder)
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterStringBuilder, m.loChilkatStringBuilder
		
		RETURN m.loChilkatTask
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.Ai])
		  toChilkatStringBuilder = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.StringBuilder])
		  loChilkatTask = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.Task])
		  loChilkatStringBuilder = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.StringBuilder])
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE usemcp		&& Introduced in version 11.6.0. Registers the tools provided by the connected MCP (Model Context Protocol) server cMcp so the AI model can call them during a conversation. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            UseMcp
		* Purpose:           Registers the tools provided by the connected MCP (Model Context Protocol) server.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        toChilkatMcp, a Chilkat Mcp object.
		*                    tcNamePrefix - a short schema name.
		* Returns:           Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		* Date Added:        09/06/2026
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 11.6.0.
		**
		** Registers the tools provided by the connected MCP (Model Context Protocol) server cMcp 
		** so the AI model can call them during a conversation. This lists the server's tools 
		** (a network operation) and namespaces each tool name using the prefix in namePrefix 
		** (to avoid collisions between servers and with JavaScript tools).
		**
		** When the model requests one of these tools, Chilkat automatically routes the call 
		** to the MCP server via Mcp.CallTool, adds the result to the conversation, and continues the Ask. 
		** An informational ProgressInfo event named McpToolCall (value = the qualified tool name) 
		** is emitted for each automatic call. MCP tools may be mixed with JavaScript tools 
		** (RegisterJsTools) in the same conversation.
		** 
		** The cMcp Mcp object must already be connected (see Mcp.Connect) and must remain valid 
		** for as long as its tools are in use. Tool use requires a conversation; 
		** it cannot be used with a stateless query.
		** 
		** Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		** 
		
		LPARAMETERS toChilkatMcp AS [Chilkat.Mcp], tcNamePrefix AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS [Chilkat.Ai], loException AS Exception, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, loParkParameterBinData AS [iParkParameter OF ChilkatVFP.VCX], ;
		loChilkatMcp AS [Chilkat.Mcp], liReturn AS Integer, luReturn AS Unknown
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterBinData, m.loChilkatMcp
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(11, 6, 0)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      liStrict = .LogicalToBit(m.tuStrict)
		
		      loParkParameterBinData = ;
		      NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], .ClassLibrary, [], m.oChilkatMcp)
		
		      loChilkatMcp = m.loParkParameterBinData.GetObject()
		
		      TRY
		
		        STORE m.loChilkatObject.UseMcp(m.loChilkatMcp, ;
		        m.tcNamePrefix) TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		      toChilkatMcp = ;
		      m.loParkParameterBinData.SetObject(m.oChilkatMcp, m.loChilkatMcp)
		    
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		  luReturn = .BitToLogical(m.liReturn)
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterBinData, m.loChilkatMcp
		
		RETURN m.luReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.Ai])
		  toChilkatMcp = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.Mcp])
		  loParkParameterBinData = NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], [ChilkatVFP.VCX])
		  loChilkatMcp = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.Mcp])
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE usemcpasync		&& Introduced in version 11.6.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the UseMcp method with the arguments provided. Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            UseMcpAsync
		* Purpose:           Creates an asynchronous task to call the UseMcp
		*                    method with the arguments provided. 
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        toChilkatMcp, a Chilkat Mcp object.
		*                    tcNamePrefix - a short schema name.
		* Returns:           toChilkatTask, a Chilkat Task object.
		* Date Added:        09/06/2026
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 11.6.0.
		**
		** Creates an asynchronous task to call the UseMcp method with the arguments provided. 
		** (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		** 
		** Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. 
		** Accessing and updating UI elements existing in the main thread may require special considerations.
		**
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS toChilkatMcp AS [Chilkat.Mcp], tcNamePrefix AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS [Chilkat.Ai], loException AS Exception, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, loChilkatTask AS [Chilkat.Task], ;
		loParkParameterMcp AS [iParkParameter OF ChilkatVFP.VCX], ;
		loChilkatMcp AS [Chilkat.Mcp]
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterMcp, m.loChilkatMcp
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(11, 6, 0)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      loParkParameterMcp = ;
		      NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], .ClassLibrary, [], m.oChilkatMcp)
		
		      loChilkatMcp = m.loParkParameterMcp.GetObject()
		
		      TRY
		
		        loChilkatTask = m.loChilkatObject.UseMcpAsync(m.loChilkatMcp, m.tcNamePrefix) 
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		      toChilkatMcp = ;
		      m.loParkParameterMcp.SetObject(m.oChilkatMcp, m.loChilkatMcp)
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterMcp, m.loChilkatMcp
		
		RETURN m.loChilkatTask
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.Ai])
		  toChilkatMcp = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.Mcp])
		  loChilkatTask = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.Task])
		  loChilkatMcp = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.Mcp])
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE verboselogging_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat AI VerboseLogging property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            VerboseLogging_Access
		* Purpose:           Assign method used to retrieve 
		*                    the VerboseLogging property of the referenced Chilkat object.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           THIS.VerboseLogging
		* Date Added:        11/03/2025
		*==============================================================================
		
		** 
		** If set to 1, then the contents of LastErrorText (or LastErrorXml, or LastErrorHtml) 
		** may contain more verbose information. The default value is 0. 
		** Verbose logging should only be used for debugging. 
		** The potentially large quantity of logged information may adversely affect peformance.
		** 
		
		LOCAL liStackLevel AS Integer, lcMethod AS Character, ;
		lcProperty AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_Stack[1, 1], la_IntroducedInBuild[3]
		
		STORE [] TO m.lcMethod, m.lcProperty, m.lcMethodToCall, m.la_Stack, m.la_IntroducedInBuild
		
		liStackLevel = ASTACKINFO(la_Stack)
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 11
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 2
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 0
		
		lcMethod = m.la_Stack(m.liStackLevel, 3)
		lcMethod = PROPER(SUBSTRC(m.lcMethod, AT_C([.], m.lcMethod) + 1))
		lcProperty = LEFTC(m.lcMethod, LENC(m.lcMethod) - 7)
		
		lcMethodToCall = [LongBit]
		
		THIS.CallAccessObject(m.lcMethodToCall, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN EVALUATE([THIS.] + m.lcProperty)
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE verboselogging_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the VerboseLogging property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            VerboseLogging_Assign
		* Purpose:           Assign method used to retrieve 
		*                    the VerboseLogging property of the referenced Chilkat object.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tuValue, integer or logical value 
		*                    used to hold a reference to the VerboseLogging property.
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        11/03/2025
		*==============================================================================
		
		LPARAMETERS tuValue AS Unknown
		
		LOCAL lcValidationMethod AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_IntroducedInBuild[3]
		
		lcValidationMethod = []
		lcMethodToCall = [LongBit]
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 11
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 2
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 0
		
		THIS.CallAssignObject(m.tuValue, m.lcMethodToCall, m.lcValidationMethod, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN
	ENDPROC

ENDDEFINE

DEFINE CLASS asn AS ibasechilkat OF "chilkatvfp.vcx" 		&& For creating, loading, parsing, converting, and saving ASN.1
 	*< CLASSDATA: Baseclass="custom" Timestamp="" Scale="Pixels" Uniqueid="" />

	#INCLUDE "foxpro.h"
	*<DefinedPropArrayMethod>
		*m: appendbigint		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Appends an ASN.1 integer, but one that is a big (huge) integer that is too large to be represented by an integer variable. The bytes composing the integer are passed in encoded string format (such as base64, hex, etc.).
		*m: appendbits		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Appends an ASN.1 bit string to the caller's sub-items. The bytes containing the bits are passed in encoded string format (such as base64, hex, etc.). The byte order must be big-endian (MSB first).
		*m: appendbool		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Appends an ASN.1 boolean item to the caller's sub-items. Items may only be appended to constructed data types such as Sequence and Set. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendcontextconstructed		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Appends an ASN.1 context-specific constructed item to the caller's sub-items. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendcontextprimitive		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Appends an ASN.1 context-specific primitive item to the caller's sub-items. The bytes are passed in encoded string format (such as base64, hex, etc.).
		*m: appendint		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Appends an ASN.1 integer item to the caller's sub-items. Items may only be appended to constructed data types such as Sequence and Set. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendnull		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Appends an ASN.1 null item to the caller's sub-items. Items may only be appended to constructed data types such as Sequence and Set. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendoctets		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Appends an ASN.1 octet string to the caller's sub-items. The bytes are passed in encoded string format (such as base64, hex, etc.).
		*m: appendoid		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Appends an ASN.1 OID (object identifier) to the caller's sub-items. The OID is passed in string form, such as "1.2.840.113549.1.9.1". Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendsequence		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Appends an ASN.1 sequence item to the caller's sub-items. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendsequence2		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Appends an ASN.1 sequence item to the caller's sub-items, and updates the internal reference to point to the newly appended sequence item. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendsequencer		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Appends an ASN.1 sequence item to the caller's sub-items, and returns the newly appended sequence item. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: appendset		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Appends an ASN.1 set item to the caller's sub-items. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendset2		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Appends an ASN.1 set item to the caller's sub-items, and updates the internal reference to point to the newly appended set item. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendsetr		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Appends an ASN.1 set item to the caller's sub-items, and returns the newly appended set item. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: appendstring		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Appends a string item to the caller's sub-items. The strType specifies the type of string to be added. It may be "utf8", "ia5", "t61", "printable", "visible", "numeric", "universal", or "bmp".
		*m: appendtime		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Appends a UTCTime item to the caller's sub-items. The timeFormat specifies the format of the dateTimeStr. It should be set to "utc".
		*m: asntoxml		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Converts ASN.1 to XML and returns the XML string. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: boolvalue_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN BoolValue property.
		*m: boolvalue_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the BoolValue property.
		*m: constructed_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN Constructed property.
		*m: constructed_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Constructed property.
		*m: contentstr_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN ContentStr property.
		*m: contentstr_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ContentStr property.
		*m: debuglogfilepath_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN DebugLogFilePath property.
		*m: debuglogfilepath_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the DebugLogFilePath property.
		*m: deletesubitem		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Discards the Nth sub-item. (The 1st sub-item is at index 0.) Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: getbinaryder		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Returns the ASN.1 in binary DER form. Returns a zero-length byte array (as a Variant) on failure. An empty array will have a UBound of -1 meaning 0 elements.
		*m: getencodedcontent		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Returns the content of the ASN.1 item in encoded string form.
		*m: getencodedder		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Returns the binary DER in encoded string form. The encoding indicates the encoding and can be "base64", "hex", "uu", "quoted-printable", "base32", or "modbase64". Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: getlastsubitem		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Returns the last ASN.1 sub-item. This method can be called immediately after any Append* method to access the appended item. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: getsubitem		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Returns the Nth ASN.1 sub-item. The 1st sub-item is at index 0. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: intvalue_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN IntValue property.
		*m: intvalue_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the IntValue property.
		*m: lastbinaryresult_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN LastBinaryResult property.
		*m: lastbinaryresult_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastBinaryResult property.
		*m: lasterrorhtml_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN LastErrorHTML property.
		*m: lasterrorhtml_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastErrorHTML property.
		*m: lasterrortext_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN LastErrorText property.
		*m: lasterrortext_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastErrorText property.
		*m: lasterrorxml_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN LastErrorXML property.
		*m: lasterrorxml_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastErrorXML property.
		*m: lastmethodsuccess_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN LastMethodSuccess property.
		*m: lastmethodsuccess_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastMethodSuccess property.
		*m: laststringresultlen_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN LastStringResultLen property.
		*m: laststringresultlen_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastStringResultLen property
		*m: laststringresult_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN LastStringResult property.
		*m: laststringresult_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastStringResult property
		*m: loadasnxml		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Loads ASN.1 from the XML representation (such as that created by the AsnToXml method). Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: loadbd		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.77. Loads ASN.1 from the binary DER contained in bd. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: loadbinary		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Loads ASN.1 from binary DER. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: loadbinaryfile		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Loads ASN.1 from a binary DER file. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: loadencoded		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Loads ASN.1 from an encoded string. The encoding can be "base64", "hex", "uu", "quoted-printable", "base32", or "modbase64". Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: numsubitems_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN NumSubItems property.
		*m: numsubitems_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the NumSubItems property
		*m: setencodedcontent		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Sets the content of this primitive ASN.1 item.
		*m: tagvalue_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN TagValue property.
		*m: tagvalue_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TagValue property.
		*m: tag_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN Tag property.
		*m: tag_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Tag property.
		*m: verboselogging_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN VerboseLogging property.
		*m: verboselogging_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the VerboseLogging property
		*m: writebd		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.77. Appends the ASN.1 in binary DER format to bd. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: writebinaryder		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Writes the ASN.1 in binary DER form to a file. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*p: boolvalue		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. The ASN.1 item's boolean value if it is a boolean item.
		*p: constructed		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. 1 if this ASN.1 item is a constructed item. Sequence and Set items are constructed and can contain sub-items. All other tags (boolean, integer, octets, utf8String, etc.) are primitive (non-constructed).
		*p: contentstr		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. The ASN.1 item's content if it is an ASN.1 string type (such as Utf8String, BmpString, PrintableString, VisibleString, T61String, IA5String, NumericString, or UniversalString).
		*p: debuglogfilepath		&& If set to a file path, causes each Chilkat method or property call to automatically append it's LastErrorText to the specified log file.
		*p: intvalue		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. The ASN.1 item's integer value if it is a small integer item.
		*p: lastbinaryresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The binary data returned by the last (binary data returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepBinaryResult is set to 1.
		*p: lasterrorhtml		&& Provides information in HTML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrortext		&& Provides information in plain-text format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrorxml		&& Provides information in XML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lastmethodsuccess		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Indicate whether the last method call succeeded or failed. A value of 1 indicates success, a value of 0 indicates failure. This property is automatically set for method calls. It is not modified by property accesses.
		*p: laststringresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The string return value of the last (string returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepStringResult is set to 1.
		*p: laststringresultlen		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.53. The length, in characters, of the string contained in the LastStringResult propert
		*p: numsubitems		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. The number of sub-items contained within this ASN.1 item. Only constructed items, such as Sequence and Set will contain sub-iitems. Primitive items such as OIDs, octet strings, integers, etc. will never contain sub-items
		*p: tagvalue		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. The ASN.1 item's tag as a integer value.
		*p: verboselogging		&& If set to 1, then the contents of LastErrorText (or LastErrorXml, or LastErrorHtml) may contain more verbose information. The default value is 0. Verbose logging should only be used for debugging.
