	PROCEDURE chilkatchangelog
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ChilkatChangeLog
		* Purpose:           Documentation method used to hold 
		*                    the Chilkat class changes per release version.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        02/04/2024
		*==============================================================================
		
		#IF .F.
		
		TEXT
		
		** Version 11.2.0
		
		  Added base62 encoding as an additional encoding choice recognized throughout Chilkat.
		
		** Version 99
		
		  Chilkat’s internal ASN.1 decoder needed an update to correctly handle 
		  0-length ASN.1 bit strings (which is something not normally encountered).
		
		  Added “Base45” to the set of binary encodings supported by Chilkat. 
		  “base45” can now be used in any Chilkat function or property 
		  where a binary encoding such as “base64”, “hex”, “base58”, etc., can be used.
		
		** Version 79
		
		  Encoding: Added ascii85 encoding/decoding to the list of supported binary encoding algorithms.
		  “ascii85” can be used anywhere in the Chilkat API
		  where an encoding such as “base64”, “hex”, “base58”, etc. is used.
		
		** Version 77
		
		  Added LoadBd and WriteBd methods.
		
		** Version 75
		
		  Added the “hexlower” encoding. “hexlower” may be used instead of “hex”
		  to get the hexadecimal encoding using lowercase a-f (“hex” produces uppercase A-F).
		
		** Version 67
		
		  Added the “base64_mime” to the list of possible encodings.
		  This is the same as “base64”, but causes the base64 to be emitted
		  in lines just like it would be found in MIME or in a PEM.
		
		** Version 65
		
		  Added the “eda” encoding for UN/EDIFACT Syntax Level A.
		  See https://www.example-code.com/foxpro/edifact_eda_syntax_level_A_encoding.asp
		  Also see: https://cknotes.com/chilkat-binary-encoding-list/
		
		  ActiveX LastStringResultLen property incorrectly returned the size of the string in bytes (utf-16)
		  rather than in number of characters. This is fixed to return the number of characters.
		  (Note: this is a property that only exists in ActiveX classes, and is only useful
		  for certain programming languages such as SQL Server to help programs determine
		  if temp tables are required.)
		
		** Version 58
		
		  The Windows logged-on username is no longer automatically logged at the top of every LastErrorText.
		  (This was originally done to help w/ support issues so tht Chilkat might notice if the program runs
		  in the context of a Service or IIS, which could be a clue to the cause of certain problems.)
		
		** Version 56
		
		   Added the “base64url” encoding to the list of supported encodings.
		   See https://cknotes.com/chilkat-binary-encoding-list/
		
		** Version 55
		
		  A new Chilkat encoding named “fingerprint” was added. The “fingerprint” encoding
		  is lowercase hex with each byte separated by a colon character.
		  See https://cknotes.com/chilkat-binary-encoding-list/
		
		** Version 53
		
		  The LastStringResultLen property is added to each Chilkat class.
		  This is helpful for certain programming languages such as DataFlex or SQL Server
		  where the size of the string returned may need to be known before using it.
		  Each Chilkat ActiveX object has its own LastStringResult and LastStringResultLen properties.
		  The KeepStringResult is a property of Chilkat.Global only.
		  (It may be confusing that Chilkat.Global also has a LastStringResult property —
		  but this is just like any other object.)
		
		  Therefore, your code would set Global.KeepStringResult once at the beginning of your code.
		
		  Let’s say you have an HttpResult object, and you want the BodyQP.
		  You would access the BodyQP, but ignore the string returned.
		  Then examine the HttpResult.LastStringResultLen, adjust your max string length (in DataFlex) if necessary,
		  and then get the cached string from HttpResult.LastStringResult.
		
		** Version 52
		
		  Added the LastMethodSuccess property.
		
		** Version 49
		
		  Added the new Asn class to provide an ASN.1 API.
		
		ENDTEXT
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE constructed_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ASN Constructed property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            Constructed_Access
		* Purpose:           Access method used to retrieve 
		*                    the Chilkat ASN Constructed property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           THIS.Constructed
		* Date Added:        07/30/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.49
		**
		** 1 if this ASN.1 item is a constructed item. Sequence and Set items 
		** are constructed and can contain sub-items. All other tags 
		** (boolean, integer, octets, utf8String, etc.) are primitive (non-constructed).
		** 
		
		LOCAL liStackLevel AS Integer, lcMethod AS Character, ;
		lcProperty AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_Stack[1, 1], la_IntroducedInBuild[3, 1]
		
		STORE [] TO m.lcMethod, m.lcProperty, m.lcMethodToCall, m.la_Stack, m.la_IntroducedInBuil
		
		liStackLevel = ASTACKINFO(la_Stack)
		
		lcMethod = m.la_Stack(m.liStackLevel, 3)
		lcMethod = PROPER(SUBSTRC(m.lcMethod, AT_C([.], m.lcMethod) + 1))
		lcProperty = LEFTC(m.lcMethod, LENC(m.lcMethod) - 7)
		
		lcMethodToCall = [LongBitReadOnly]
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 9
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 5
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 49
		
		THIS.CallAccessObject(m.lcMethodToCall, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN EVALUATE([THIS.] + m.lcProperty)
	ENDPROC

