	PROCEDURE addelementdatestr		&& Adds a new date-formatted element to the Atom document. The tag is a string such as "created", "modified", "issued", etc. The dateTimeStr should be an RFC822 formatted date/time string such as "Tue, 25 Sep 2012 12:25:32 -0500".
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            AddElementDateStr
		* Purpose:           Adds a new date-formatted element to the Atom document.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcTag -- the tag name to add.
		*                    tcDateTime -- the tag's date time value.
		* Returns:           Returns the index of the element added, or -1 for failure.
		* Date Added:        07/30/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Adds a new date-formatted element to the Atom document. 
		** The tag is a string such as "created", "modified", "issued", etc. 
		** The dateTimeStr should be an RFC822 formatted date/time string such as 
		** "Tue, 25 Sep 2012 12:25:32 -0500". 
		** 
		** Returns the index of the element added, or -1 for failure.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcTag AS Character, tcDateTime AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS [Chilkat_9_5_0.Atom], ;
		loException AS Exception, liElementIndex AS Integer
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		liElementIndex = 0
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
