		*m: percentdone_post		&& Template PercentDone post-processing method.
		*m: percentdone_pre		&& Template PercentDone pre-processing method.
		*m: percentdone_process		&& Template PercentDone processing method.
		*m: progressinfo		&& A general name/value event that provides information about what is happening during a method call. To find out what information is available, write code to handle this event and log the name/value pairs.
		*m: progressinfo_post		&& Template ProgressInfo post-processing method.
		*m: progressinfo_pre		&& Template ProgressInfo pre-processing method.
		*m: progressinfo_process		&& Template ProgressInfo processing method.
		*m: taskcompleted		&& Called in the background thread when an asynchronous task completes.
		*m: taskcompleted_post		&& Template TaskCompleted post-processing method.
		*m: taskcompleted_pre		&& Template TaskCompleted pre-processing method.
		*m: taskcompleted_process		&& Template TaskCompleted processing method.
		*m: textdata		&& Added in version 58 but as of the time of this writing is unused.
		*m: textdata_post		&& Template TextData post-processing method.
		*m: textdata_pre		&& Template TextData pre-processing method.
		*m: textdata_process		&& Template TextData processing method.
	*</DefinedPropArrayMethod>

	*<PropValue>
		Name = "baseeventhandler"
	*</PropValue>
	
	PROCEDURE abortcheck		&& Provides the opportunity for a method call to be aborted. The AbortCheck event is fired periodically based on the value of the HeartbeatMs property. If HeartbeatMs is 0, then no AbortCheck events will fire.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            AbortCheck
		* Purpose:           Provides the opportunity for a method call to be aborted. 
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tiAbort, indicates the abort status. 0 = Not aborting.
		* Returns:           Integer
		* Date Added:        10/18/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Provides the opportunity for a method call to be aborted. 
		** The AbortCheck event is fired periodically based 
		** on the value of the HeartbeatMs property. If HeartbeatMs is 0, 
		** then no AbortCheck events will fire. As an example, 
		** to fire 5 AbortCheck events per second, set the HeartbeatMs property equal to 200.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tiAbort AS Integer
		
		LOCAL liAbort AS Integer
		
		liAbort = m.tiAbort
		
		*!*  ? [AbortCheck Event!]
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  ** Not aborting test+
		  IF m.liAbort = 0
		
		    liAbort = .AbortCheck_Pre(m.liAbort)
		
		    ** Still not aborting test
		    IF m.liAbort = 0
		
		      liAbort = .AbortCheck_Process(m.liAbort)
		
		      ** Still not aborting test
		      IF m.liAbort = 0
		
		        liAbort = .AbortCheck_Post(m.liAbort)
		
		      ENDIF m.liAbort = 0
		      ** End still not aborting test
		
		    ENDIF m.liAbort = 0
		    ** End still not aborting test
		
		  ENDIF m.liAbort = 0
		  ** End not aborting test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		RETURN m.liAbort
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE abortcheck_post		&& Template AbortCheck post-processing method.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            AbortCheck_Post
		* Purpose:           Template AbortCheck post-processing method. 
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tiAbort, indicates the abort status. 0 = Not aborting.
		* Returns:           Integer
		* Date Added:        10/18/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		LPARAMETERS tiAbort AS Integer
		
		RETURN m.tiAbort
		
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE abortcheck_pre		&& Template AbortCheck pre-processing method.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            AbortCheck_Pre
