	PROCEDURE getencoded		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.51. Retrieves the binary data as an encoded string.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            GetEncoded
		* Purpose:           Retrieves the binary data as an encoded string.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcEncoding, the encoding of the string to retrieve.
		* Returns:           The binary data in an encoded string.
		* Date Added:        06/22/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.51
		**
		** Retrieves the binary data as an encoded string. 
		** The encoding may be "Base64", "modBase64", "base64Url", "Base32", "Base58", 
		** "QP" (for quoted-printable), "URL" (for url-encoding), "Hex", 
		** or any of the encodings found at Chilkat Binary Encodings List.
		** 
		** Enhancement for Version 55: A new Chilkat encoding named “fingerprint” was added. 
		** The “fingerprint” encoding is lowercase hex with each byte separated by a colon character.
		** 
		** Enhancement for Version 56: 
		** Added the “base64url” encoding to the list of supported encodings. 
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 65: Added the “eda” encoding for UN/EDIFACT Syntax Level A.
		**
		** Enhancement to Version 67: Added the “base64_mime” to the list of possible encodings. 
		** This is the same as “base64”, but causes the base64 to be emitted 
		** in lines just like it would be found in MIME or in a PEM.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 75: Added the “hexlower” encoding. 
		** “hexlower” may be used instead of “hex” to get the hexadecimal encoding 
		** using lowercase a-f (“hex” produces uppercase A-F).
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 79: 
		** Added ascii85 encoding/decoding to the list of supported binary encoding algorithms.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 99: 
		** Added “Base45” to the set of binary encodings supported by Chilkat. 
		** “base45” can now be used in any Chilkat function or property where a binary encoding 
		** such as “base64”, “hex”, “base58”, etc., can be used.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 11.2.0:
		** Added base62 encoding as an additional encoding choice recognized throughout Chilkat.
		** 
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcEncoding AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_BINDATA_COM_CALL, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		loException AS Exception, lcEncodedString AS Character
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		lcEncodedString = []
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 51
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        lcEncodedString = m.loChilkatObject.GetEncoded(m.tcEncoding)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcEncodedString
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_BINDATA_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE getencodedchunk		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.51. Retrieves a chunk of the binary data and returns it in encoded form.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            GetEncodedChunk
		* Purpose:           Retrieves the binary data contained within the object.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tiOffset, the offset from the beginning of the file.
		*                    tiNumBytes, the number of bytes to retrieve.
		*                    tcEncoding, the encoding of the returned string.
		* Returns:           The string chunk.
		* Date Added:        06/22/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.51
		**
		** Retrieves the binary data contained within the object.
		**
		** Returns a zero-length byte array (as a Variant) on failure.
		** 
		** Enhancement for Version 55: A new Chilkat encoding named “fingerprint” was added. 
		** The “fingerprint” encoding is lowercase hex with each byte separated by a colon character.
		** 
		** Enhancement for Version 56: 
		** Added the “base64url” encoding to the list of supported encodings. 
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 65: Added the “eda” encoding for UN/EDIFACT Syntax Level A.
		**
		** Enhancement to Version 67: Added the “base64_mime” to the list of possible encodings. 
		** This is the same as “base64”, but causes the base64 to be emitted 
		** in lines just like it would be found in MIME or in a PEM.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 75: Added the “hexlower” encoding. 
		** “hexlower” may be used instead of “hex” to get the hexadecimal encoding 
		** using lowercase a-f (“hex” produces uppercase A-F).
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 79: 
		** Added ascii85 encoding/decoding to the list of supported binary encoding algorithms.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 99: 
		** Added “Base45” to the set of binary encodings supported by Chilkat. 
		** “base45” can now be used in any Chilkat function or property where a binary encoding 
		** such as “base64”, “hex”, “base58”, etc., can be used.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 11.2.0:
		** Added base62 encoding as an additional encoding choice recognized throughout Chilkat.
		**
		** An empty array will have a UBound of -1 meaning 0 elements.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tiOffset AS Integer, tiNumBytes AS Integer, tcEncoding AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_BINDATA_COM_CALL, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		loException AS Exception, lcEncodedString AS Character
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		lcEncodedString = []
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 51
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        lcEncodedString = ;
		        m.loChilkatObject.GetEncodedChunk(m.tiOffset, m.tiNumBytes, m.tcEncoding)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcEncodedString
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_BINDATA_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE getencodedsb		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.64. Writes the encoded data to a StringBuilder.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            GetEncodedSb
		* Purpose:           Retrieves the binary data as an encoded string.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcEncoding, the encoding of the string to retrieve.
		*                    toChilkatStringBuilder, a Chilkat String Builder object.
		* Returns:           The binary data in an encoded string.
		* Date Added:        06/22/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.64
		**
		** Retrieves the binary data as an encoded string. 
		** The encoding may be "Base64", "modBase64", "base64Url", "Base32", "Base58", 
		** "QP" (for quoted-printable), "URL" (for url-encoding), "Hex", 
		** or any of the encodings found at Chilkat Binary Encodings List.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 65: Added the “eda” encoding for UN/EDIFACT Syntax Level A.
		**
		** Enhancement to Version 67: Added the “base64_mime” to the list of possible encodings. 
		** This is the same as “base64”, but causes the base64 to be emitted 
		** in lines just like it would be found in MIME or in a PEM.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 75: Added the “hexlower” encoding. 
		** “hexlower” may be used instead of “hex” to get the hexadecimal encoding 
		** using lowercase a-f (“hex” produces uppercase A-F).
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 79: 
		** Added ascii85 encoding/decoding to the list of supported binary encoding algorithms.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 99: 
		** Added “Base45” to the set of binary encodings supported by Chilkat. 
		** “base45” can now be used in any Chilkat function or property where a binary encoding 
		** such as “base64”, “hex”, “base58”, etc., can be used.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 11.2.0:
		** Added base62 encoding as an additional encoding choice recognized throughout Chilkat.
		** 
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcEncoding AS Character, ;
		toChilkatStringBuilder AS CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_BINDATA_COM_CALL, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		loException AS Exception, lcEncodedString AS Character, ;
		loParkParameterStringBuilder AS [iParkParameter OF ChilkatVFP.VCX], ;
		loChilkatStringBuilder AS CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterStringBuilder, m.loChilkatStringBuilder
		
		lcEncodedString = []
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 64
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      loParkParameterStringBuilder = ;
		      NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], .ClassLibrary, [], m.toChilkatStringBuilder)
		
		      loChilkatStringBuilder = m.loParkParameterStringBuilder.GetObject()
		
		      TRY
		
		        lcEncodedString = ;
		        m.loChilkatObject.GetEncodedSb(m.tcEncoding, m.loChilkatStringBuilder)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		      toChilkatStringBuilder = m.loParkParameterStringBuilder.SetObject(;
		      m.toChilkatStringBuilder, m.loChilkatStringBuilder)
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterStringBuilder, m.loChilkatStringBuilder
		
		RETURN m.lcEncodedString
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_BINDATA_COM_CALL)
		  loChilkatStringBuilder = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL)
		  loParkParameterStringBuilder = NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], [ChilkatVFP.VCX])
		  loChilkatStringBuilder = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE gethash		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.91. Returns the hash of the contents of this object.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            GetHash
		* Purpose:           Returns the hash of the contents of this object.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcAlgorithm, the hash algorithm
		*                    tcEncoding, the hash encoding.
		*                    tcCharset, the charset of the hash.
		* Returns:           lcHash, the found (or not) substring.
		* Date Added:        07/15/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.91
		**
		** Returns the hash of the contents of this object. 
		** The algorithm is the hash algorithm, and can be "sha1", "sha256", "sha384", 
		** "sha512", "sha3-224", "sha3-256", "sha3-384", "sha3-512", "md2", "md5", 
		** "ripemd128", "ripemd160","ripemd256", or "ripemd320". 
		** The encoding can be "base64", "modBase64", "base64Url", "base32", "base58", 
		** "qp" (for quoted-printable), "url" (for url-encoding), "hex", "hexLower", 
		** or any of the encodings found at Chilkat Binary Encodings List.
		** 
		** The charset is the character encoding byte representation to hash. 
		** It is typically "utf-8". It can be any of the chacter encodings listed 
		** at Chilkat Character Encodings List.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 99: 
		** Added “Base45” to the set of binary encodings supported by Chilkat. 
		** “base45” can now be used in any Chilkat function or property where a binary encoding 
		** such as “base64”, “hex”, “base58”, etc., can be used.
		**
