	PROCEDURE getasunixtime		&& Returns the date/time as a 32-bit Unix time. bLocal indicates whether the date/time returned is local or UTC. Note: With this format, there is a Y2038 problem that pertains to 32-bit signed integers.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            GetAsUnixTime
		* Purpose:           Returns the date/time as a 32-bit Unix time.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tuLocalTime, whether or not the returned time 
		*                    is local or UTC time.
		* Returns:           An integer representing the current UNIX DateTime value.
		* Date Added:        07/26/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Returns the date/time as a 32-bit Unix time.
		** 
		** bLocal indicates whether the date/time returned is local or UTC.
		** 
		** Note: With this format, there is a Y2038 problem that pertains to 32-bit signed integers. 
		** There are approx 31.5 million seconds per year. The Unix time is number of seconds 
		** since the Epoch, 1970-01-01 00:00:00 +0000 (UTC). In 2012, it's 42 years since 1/1/1970, 
		** so the number of seconds is approx 1.3 billion. A 32-bit signed integer 
		** ranges from -2,147,483,648 to 2,147,483,647 Therefore, if a 32-bit signed integer is used, 
		** it turns negative in 2038.
		** 
		** The GetAsUnixTime64 and GetAsUnixTimeDbl methods are provided as solutions to the Y2038 problem.
		** 
		** (Note: The ActiveX Chilkat implementation omits methods that use 64-bit integers 
		** because there is no means for passing or returning 64-bit integers in ActiveX.)
		** 
		
		LPARAMETERS tuLocalTime AS Unknown
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_CKDATETIME_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, liLocalTime AS Integer, liUnixTime AS Integer
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liLocalTime, m.liUnixTime
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    liLocalTime = .LogicalToBit(m.tuLocalTime)
		
		    TRY
		
		      liUnixTime = m.loChilkatObject.GetAsUnixTime(m.liLocalTime)
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.liUnixTime 
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_CKDATETIME_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

