	PROCEDURE chilkatchangelog
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ChilkatChangeLog
		* Purpose:           Documentation method used to hold 
		*                    the Chilkat class changes per release version.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        02/04/2024
		*==============================================================================
		
		#IF .F.
		
		TEXT
		
		** Version 99
		
		  Fixed a crash problem when appending hex encoded bytes to be interpreted as “gsm”.
		
		** Version 78
		
		  The appendHexData method would terminate with an unnecessary LF
		  if the passed in data was a multiple of 16.
		
		** Version 76
		
		  The saveToFileW and SaveToFile2 methods did not properly
		  write the utf-8 BOM (byte order mark) if the “bom-utf-8” charset was specified.
		
		** Version 75
		
		  Fixed: The saveToFile method did not write a file with no BOM (Byte Order Mark)
		  when passing “no-bom-utf-8” for the charsetEncoding.
		
		** Version 73
		
		  The loadFile method will now recognize Unicode/utf-8 BOMs 
		  and will load files correctly based on the BOM encountered.
		
		** Version 62
		
		  Note: BinData and StringBuilder are consistently the same across all programming languages,
		  whereas CkString and CkByteData are not. CkString and CkByteData will continue to be used in future versions,
		  are still an integral part of Chilkat, and are NOT decremented.
		
		** Version 52
		
		  Added punycode encoding/decoding methods.
		
		ENDTEXT
		
		#ENDIF .F.
	ENDPROC

