	PROCEDURE opaquesignbytesenc		&& Digitally signs a byte array and returns a PKCS7/CMS format signature in encoded string format (such as Base64 or hex). This is a signature that contains both the original data as well as the signature.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            OpaqueSignBytesENC
		* Purpose:           Digitally signs a byte array and returns a PKCS7/CMS 
		*                    format signature in encoded string format.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tqDataBytes -- the bytes to convert. 
		* Returns:           The encoded format string.
		* Date Added:        07/01/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Digitally signs a byte array and returns a PKCS7/CMS format signature in encoded string format 
		** (such as Base64 or hex). This is a signature that contains both the original data 
		** as well as the signature. A certificate must be set by calling SetSigningCert 
		** prior to calling this method. The EncodingMode property controls the output encoding, 
		** which can be "Base64", "QP","Hex", etc. (See the EncodingMode property.)
		**
		** Enhancement to Version 67: Added the “base64_mime” to the list of possible encodings. 
		** This is the same as “base64”, but causes the base64 to be emitted 
		** in lines just like it would be found in MIME or in a PEM.
		**
		** Fixed for Version 72: 
		** Fixed certain cases where creating PKCS7 signatures embedded the same certificate twice.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 75: Added the “hexlower” encoding. 
		** “hexlower” may be used instead of “hex” to get the hexadecimal encoding 
		** using lowercase a-f (“hex” produces uppercase A-F).
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 79: 
		** Added ascii85 encoding/decoding to the list of supported binary encoding algorithms.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 99: 
		** Added “Base45” to the set of binary encodings supported by Chilkat. 
		** “base45” can now be used in any Chilkat function or property where a binary encoding 
		** such as “base64”, “hex”, “base58”, etc., can be used.
		** 
		** Enhancement for Version 10: Added the ability to create and verify 
		** AES-GCM authEnvelopedData. 
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 11.2.0:
		** Added base62 encoding as an additional encoding choice recognized throughout Chilkat.
		** 
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		** 
		
		LPARAMETERS tqDataBytes AS VarBinary
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_CRYPT2_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, lcFormatSignature AS Character
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		lcFormatSignature = []
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      lcFormatSignature = m.loChilkatObject.OpaqueSignBytesENC(m.tqDataBytes)
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcFormatSignature
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_CRYPT2_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

