	PROCEDURE setencryptalgorithm		&& Selects an encryption algorithm. The return value is the key-length of the algorithm. If the algorithm is not available, the return value is 0.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            SetEncryptionAlgorithm
		* Purpose:           Selects an encryption algorithm.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcAlgorithm, the encryption algorithm.
		* Returns:           The key length of the algorithm
		* Date Added:        06/11/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Selects an encryption algorithm. The return value is the key-length of the algorithm. 
		** If the algorithm is not available, the return value is 0. 
		** (There usually is not a need to explicitly select the key length, 
		** because the key length can be part of the name, such as "AES 128", 
		** or it is determined by the CSP. For example, the Microsoft Enhanced CSP 
		** will return a 128-bit key length for RC2, 
		** whereas the Base CSP will return a 40-bit key length.)
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcAlgorithm AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS [Chilkat_9_5_0.Csp], ;
		loException AS Exception, liKeyLength AS Integer
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		liKeyLength = 0
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      liKeyLength = m.loChilkatObject.SetEncryptionAlgorithm(m.tcAlgorithm)
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.liKeyLength
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat_9_5_0.Csp])
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE sethashalgorithm		&& Selects a hash algorithm. The return value is the bit-length of the algorithm. If the algorithm is not available, the return value is 0.
		*==============================================================================
