	PROCEDURE computeglobalkey		&& Decremented function! Use the ComputeGlobalKey2 function if you can.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ComputeGlobalKey
		* Purpose:           Computes a global unique key for the email.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcEncoding -- determines the encoding type.
		*                    tuFold -- if one, the MD5 hash is folded to 8 bytes.
		* Returns:           lcUniqueKey -- the generated unique key. 
		* Date Added:        06/09/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Decremented function! Use the ComputeGlobalKey2 function if you can.
		** 
		** From the 9.5.0.59 update notes: 
		**
		** The ComputeGlobalKey method was decremented and should not be used. 
		** The inputs to the MD5 hash algorithm were not properly canonicalized, 
		** and therefore the computed key could change from version to version 
		** (based on fixes, improvements, etc. in the MIME processing).
		**
		** Added the ComputeGlobalKey2 method, which is properly canonicalized 
		** to avoid the issues of the original ComputeGlobalKey implementation.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcEncoding AS Character, tuFold AS Unknown
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_EMAIL_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, llImplemented AS Logical, liFold AS Integer, ;
		lcUniqueKey AS Character
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liIntroducedInBuild, m.liFold 
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		lcUniqueKey = []
		liIntroducedInBuild = 59
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      liFold = .LogicalToBit(m.tuFold)
		
		      TRY
		
		        lcUniqueKey = m.loChilkatObject.ComputeGlobalKey(m.tcEncoding, m.liFold)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcUniqueKey
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_EMAIL_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE computeglobalkey2		&& Computes a global unique key for the email.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ComputeGlobalKey2
		* Purpose:           Computes a global unique key for the email.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcEncoding -- determines the encoding type.
		*                    tuFold -- if one, the MD5 hash is folded to 8 bytes.
		* Returns:           lcUniqueKey -- the generated unique key. 
		* Date Added:        01/25/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.59
		**
		** Computes a global unique key for the email. 
		** The key is created by a digest-MD5 hash of the concatenation of the following:
		**
		** messageID + CRLF + subject + CRLF + from + CRLF + date + CRLF + recipientAddrs
		**
		** messageID contains the contents of the Message-ID header field.
		** subject contains the contents of the Subject header field, trimmed of whitespace from both ends, 
		**   where TAB chars are converted to SPACE chars, and internal whitespace is trimmed so that 
		**   no more than one SPACE char in a row exists.
		** from contains the lowercase FROM header email address.
		** date contains the contents of the DATE header field.
		** toAddrs contains lowercase TO and CC recipient email addresses, 
		** comma separated, with duplicates removed, and sorted 
		**   in ascending order.  The BCC addresses are NOT included.
		**
		** (After calling this method, the LastErrorText property can be examined to see the string that was hashed.)
		**
		** The 16-byte MD5 hash is returned as an encoded string. 
		** The encoding determines the encoding: base64, hex, url, etc. 
		** If bFold is 1, then the 16-byte MD5 hash is folded to 8 bytes with an XOR to produce a shorter key.
		**
		** Enhancement to Version 67: Added the “base64_mime” to the list of possible encodings. 
		** This is the same as “base64”, but causes the base64 to be emitted 
		** in lines just like it would be found in MIME or in a PEM.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 75: Added the “hexlower” encoding. 
		** “hexlower” may be used instead of “hex” to get the hexadecimal encoding 
		** using lowercase a-f (“hex” produces uppercase A-F).
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 79: 
		** Added ascii85 encoding/decoding to the list of supported binary encoding algorithms.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 99: 
		** Added “Base45” to the set of binary encodings supported by Chilkat. 
		** “base45” can now be used in any Chilkat function or property where a binary encoding 
		** such as “base64”, “hex”, “base58”, etc., can be used.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 11.2.0:
		** Added base62 encoding as an additional encoding choice recognized throughout Chilkat.
		**
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcEncoding AS Character, tuFold AS Unknown
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_EMAIL_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, llImplemented AS Logical, liFold AS Integer, ;
		lcUniqueKey AS Character
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liIntroducedInBuild, m.liFold 
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		lcUniqueKey = []
		liIntroducedInBuild = 59
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      liFold = .LogicalToBit(m.tuFold)
		
		      TRY
		
		        lcUniqueKey = m.loChilkatObject.ComputeGlobalKey2(m.tcEncoding, m.liFold)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcUniqueKey
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_EMAIL_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE convertinlineimages		&& Converts images embedded inline within HTML to multipart/related MIME parts referenced from the HTML by CID. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ConvertInLineImages
		* Purpose:           Converts images embedded inline within HTML to multipart/related 
		*                    MIME parts referenced from the HTML by CID.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		* Date Added:        01/25/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.78
		**
		** Converts images embedded inline within HTML to multipart/related 
		** MIME parts referenced from the HTML by CID.
		**
		** Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		**
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_EMAIL_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liReturn AS Integer, luReturn AS Unknown, ;
		liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn, m.liIntroducedInBuild
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 78
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        STORE m.loChilkatObject.ConvertInLineImages() ;
		        TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		  luReturn = .BitToLogical(m.liReturn)
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.luReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_EMAIL_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE createdsn		&& Creates a new DSN (Delivery Status Notification) email having the format as specified in RFC 3464. See the example (below) for more detailed information.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            CreateDSN
		* Purpose:           Creates a new DSN (Delivery Status Notification) email 
		*                    having the format as specified in RFC 3464.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcHumanReadableMessage -- Email message
		*                    tcXMLStatusFields -- The relative XML name/value pairs.
		*                    tuHeaderOnly -- Indicates whether to include the entire MIME 
		*                    of the calling email object in the DSN, or only the header.
		* Returns:           loChilkatEmail, a Chilkat Email object.
		* Date Added:        01/25/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Creates a new DSN (Delivery Status Notification) email having the format as specified in RFC 3464. 
		** See the example (below) for more detailed information.
		**
		** Update to Version 11.0.0: Method decremented.
		**
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcHumanReadableMessage AS Character, ;
		tcXMLStatusFields AS Character, tuHeaderOnly AS Unknown
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_EMAIL_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		loChilkatEmail AS CHILKAT_EMAIL_COM_CALL, liHeaderOnly AS Integer
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, m.loChilkatEmail
		
		liHeaderOnly = 0
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    liHeaderOnly = .LogicalToBit(m.tuHeaderOnly)
		
		    TRY
		
		      loChilkatEmail = ;
		      m.loChilkatObject.CreateDSN(m.tcHumanReadableMessage, m.tcXMLStatusFields, m.liHeaderOnly)
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
