		** 
		** The combined name and email address of the sender, such as "John Smith". 
		** This is the content that will be placed in the From: header field. 
		** If the actual sender is to be different, then set the Sender property to a different email address.
		**
		** Fixed for Version 49: This property returned the name part undecoded if Q/B encoding was present.
		**
		** Fixed for Version 54: Setting this property *after* setting the BounceAddress property 
		** would have the side-effect of overwriting the BounceAddress property.
