		*m: socksversion_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SOCKSVersion property.
		*m: socksversion_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSVersion property.
		*m: sorcvbuf_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SoRcvBuf property.
		*m: sorcvbuf_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SoRcvBuf property.
		*m: sosndbuf_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SoSndBuf property.
		*m: sosndbuf_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SoSndBuf property.
		*m: sslallowedciphers_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SSLAllowedCiphers property.
		*m: sslallowedciphers_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSLAllowedCiphers property.
		*m: sslprotocol_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SSLProtocol property.
		*m: sslprotocol_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSLProtocol property.
		*m: sslservercertverified_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SSLServerCertVerified property.
		*m: sslservercertverified_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSLServerCertVerified property.
		*m: ssl_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SSL property.
		*m: ssl_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSL property.
		*m: stat		&& Sends a STAT command to the FTP server and returns the server's reply. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: statasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Stat method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: synccreatealllocaldirs_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SyncCreateAllLocalDirs property.
		*m: synccreatealllocaldirs_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SyncCreateAllLocalDirs property.
		*m: syncdeleteremote		&& Delete remote files that do not exist locally. The remote directory tree rooted at the current remote directory is traversed and remote files that have no corresponding local file are deleted.
		*m: syncdeleteremoteasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SyncDeleteRemote method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: syncedfiles_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SyncedFiles property.
		*m: syncedfiles_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SyncedFiles property.
		*m: synclocaldir		&& The same as SyncLocalTree, except the sub-directories are not traversed. The files in the current remote directory are synchronized (downloaded) with the files in localRoot. For possible mode settings, see SyncLocalTree.
		*m: synclocaldirasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SyncLocalDir method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: synclocaltree		&& Downloads files from the FTP server to a local directory tree.
		*m: synclocaltreeasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SyncLocalTree method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: syncmustmatchdir_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SyncMustMatchDir property.
		*m: syncmustmatchdir_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SyncMustMatchDir property.
		*m: syncmustmatch_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SyncMustMatch property.
		*m: syncmustmatch_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SyncMustMatch property.
		*m: syncmustnotmatchdir_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SyncMustNotMatchDir property.
		*m: syncmustnotmatchdir_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SyncMustNotMatchDir property.
		*m: syncmustnotmatch_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SyncMustNotMatch property.
		*m: syncmustnotmatch_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SyncMustNotMatch property.
		*m: syncpreview_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SyncPreview property.
		*m: syncpreview_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SyncPreview property
		*m: syncremotetree		&& Uploads a directory tree from the local filesystem to the FTP server.
		*m: syncremotetree2		&& Same as SyncRemoteTree, except two extra arguments are added to allow for more flexibility.
		*m: syncremotetree2async		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SyncRemoteTree2 method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: syncremotetreeasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SyncRemoteTree method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: syst		&& Sends a SYST command to the FTP server to find out the type of operating system at the server. The method returns the FTP server's response string. Refer to RFC 959 for details. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: systasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Syst method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: tlsciphersuite_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat TLSCipherSuite property.
		*m: tlsciphersuite_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TLSCipherSuite property
		*m: tlspinset_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat TLSPinSet property.
		*m: tlspinset_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TLSPinSet property
		*m: tlsversion_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat TLSVersion property.
		*m: tlsversion_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TLSVersion property
		*m: uncommonoptions_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat UncommonOptions property.
		*m: uncommonoptions_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UncommonOptions property
		*m: unlockcomponent		&& Undocumented function! Appears related to Chilkat licensing.
		*m: uploadtransferrate_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat UploadTransferRate property.
		*m: uploadtransferrate_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UploadTransferRate property
		*m: useepsv_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat UseEPSV property.
		*m: useepsv_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UseEPSV property
		*m: username_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat UserName property.
		*m: username_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UserName property
		*m: verboselogging_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat VerboseLogging property.
		*m: verboselogging_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the VerboseLogging property
		*p: abortcurrent		&& When set to 1, causes the currently running method to abort. Methods that always finish quickly (i.e.have no lengthy file operations or network communications) are not affected.
		*p: account		&& Some FTP servers require an Account name in addition to login/password. This property can be set for those servers with this requirement.
		*p: activeportrangeend		&& When Active (i.e. PORT) mode is used (opposite of Passive), the client-side is responsible for choosing a random port for each data connection.
		*p: activeportrangestart		&& This property, along with ActivePortRangeEnd, allows the client to specify a range of ports for data connections when in Active mode.
		*p: allocatesize		&& If set to a non-zero value, causes an ALLO command, with this size as the parameter, to be automatically sent when uploading files to an FTP server
		*p: allowmlsd		&& If 1, then uses the MLSD command to fetch directory listings when the FTP server supports MLSD. This property is 1 by default.
		*p: asyncbytesreceived		&& The number of bytes received during an asynchronous FTP download. This property is updated in real-time and an application may periodically fetch and display it's value while the download is in progress.
		*p: asyncbytesreceivedstr		&& The number of bytes received during an asynchronous FTP download. This property is updated in real-time and an application may periodically fetch and display it's value while the download is in progress.
		*p: asyncbytessent		&& The number of bytes sent during an asynchronous FTP upload. This property is updated in real-time and an application may periodically fetch and display it's value while the upload is in progress.
		*p: asyncbytessentstr		&& The number of bytes sent during an asynchronous FTP upload. This string property is updated in real-time and an application may periodically fetch and display it's value while the upload is in progress
		*p: asynclog		&& Decremented function! The last-error information for an asynchronous (background) file transfer. This functionality is replaced by the new model for asynchronous programming introduced in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.
		*p: asyncpercentdone		&& Decremented property! The current percentage completed of an asynchronous FTP upload or download.
		*p: authssl		&& Same as AuthTls, except the command sent to the FTP server is "AUTH SSL" instead of "AUTH TLS". Most FTP servers accept either. AuthTls is more commonly used. If a particular server has trouble with AuthTls, try AuthSsl instead.
		*p: authtls		&& Set this to 1 to switch to a TLS encrypted channel. This property should be set prior to connecting. If this property is set, the port typically remains at it's default (21) and the Ssl property should *not* be set.
		*p: autofeat		&& When 1 (which is the default value), a "FEAT" command is automatically sent to the FTP server immediately after connecting.
		*p: autofix		&& If 1, then the following will occur when a connection is made to an FTP server:
		*p: autogetsizeforprogress		&& Forces the component to retrieve each file's size prior to downloading for the purpose of monitoring percentage completion progress. For many FTP servers, this is not required and therefore for performance reasons this property defaults to 0.
		*p: autooptsutf8		&& When 1 (which is the default value), then an "OPTS UTF8 ON" command is automatically sent when connecting/authenticating if it is discovered via the FEAT command that the UTF8 option is supported.
		*p: autosetuseepsv		&& If 1 then the UseEpsv property is automatically set upon connecting to the FTP server. The default value of this property is 0.
		*p: autosyst		&& When 1 (which is the default value), a "SYST" command is automatically sent to the FTP server immediately after connecting.
		*p: autoxcrc		&& Many FTP servers support the XCRC command. The Chilkat FTP component will automatically know if XCRC is supported because it automatically sends a FEAT command to the server immediately after connecting.
		*p: bandwidththrottledown		&& If set to a non-zero value, the FTP2 component will bandwidth throttle all downloads to this value. The default value of this property is 0. The value should be specified in bytes/second.
		*p: bandwidththrottleup		&& If set to a non-zero value, the FTP2 component will bandwidth throttle all uploads to this value. The default value of this property is 0. The value should be specified in bytes/second.
		*p: clientipaddress		&& The IP address to use for computers with multiple network interfaces or IP addresses. For computers with a single network interface (i.e. most computers), this property should not be set.
		*p: commandcharset		&& Indicates the charset to be used for commands sent to the FTP server. The command charset must match what the FTP server is expecting in order to communicate non-English characters correctly. The default value of this property is "ansi".
		*p: connectfailreason		&& If the Connect method fails, this property can be checked to determine the reason for failure.
		*p: connecttimeout		&& Maximum number of seconds to wait when connecting to an FTP server. The default is 30 seconds. A value of 0 indicates the willingness to wait forever.
		*p: connectverified		&& True if the FTP2 component was able to establish a TCP/IP connection to the FTP server after calling Connect.
		*p: crlfmode		&& Used to control CRLF line endings when downloading text files in ASCII mode. The default value is 0.
		*p: curbytesreceived		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. The number of bytes received during an FTP download. This property is updated in real-time and an application may periodically fetch and display it's value while the download is in progress.
		*p: curbytesreceivedstr		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. The number of bytes received during an FTP download. This property is updated in real-time and an application may periodically fetch and display it's value while the download is in progress.
		*p: curbytessent		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. The number of bytes sent during an FTP upload. This property is updated in real-time and an application may periodically fetch and display it's value while the upload is in progress.
		*p: curbytessentstr		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. The number of bytes sent during an FTP upload. This string property is updated in real-time and an application may periodically fetch and display it's value while the upload is in progress.
		*p: dataprotection		&& Controls the data protection level for the data connections. Possible values are "control", "clear", or "private".
		*p: debuglogfilepath		&& If set to a file path, causes each Chilkat method or property call to automatically append it's LastErrorText to the specified log file.
		*p: dirlistingcharset		&& Indicates the charset of the directory listings received from the FTP server. The FTP2 client must interpret the directory listing bytes using the correct character encoding in order to correctly receive non-English characters
		*p: downloadtransferrate		&& The average download rate in bytes/second. This property is updated in real-time during any FTP download (asynchronous or synchronous).
		*p: enablesecrets		&& Introduced in version 11.5.0. This property that automatic resolution of credentials from the operating system’s secure storage. The default value is 0.
		*p: forceportipaddress		&& If set, forces the IP address used in the PORT command for Active mode (i.e. non-passive) data transfers. This string property should be set to the IP address in dotted notation, such as "233.190.65.31".
		*p: greeting		&& The initial greeting received from the FTP server after connecting.
		*p: hasmodez		&& Chilkat FTP2 supports MODE Z, which is a transfer mode implemented by some FTP servers. It allows for files to be uploaded and downloaded using compressed streams (using the zlib deflate algorithm). This is a read-only property.
		*p: heartbeatms		&& This is the number of milliseconds between each AbortCheck event callback. The AbortCheck callback allows an application to abort any FTP operation prior to completion.
		*p: hostname		&& The domain name of the FTP server. May also use the IPv4 or IPv6 address in string format.
		*p: httpproxyauthmethod		&& If an HTTP proxy requiring authentication is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy authentication method name. Valid choices are "Basic" or "NTLM".
		*p: httpproxydomain		&& If an HTTP proxy is used, and it uses NTLM authentication, then this optional property is the NTLM authentication domain.
		*p: httpproxyhostname		&& If an HTTP proxy is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy hostname or IPv4 address (in dotted decimal notation).
		*p: httpproxypassword		&& If an HTTP proxy is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy hostname or IPv4 address (in dotted decimal notation).
		*p: httpproxyport		&& If an HTTP proxy is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy port number. (Two commonly used HTTP proxy ports are 8080 and 3128.)
		*p: httpproxyusername		&& If an HTTP proxy requiring authentication is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy login name.
		*p: idletimeoutms		&& Forces a timeout when a response is expected on the control channel, but no response arrives for this number of milliseconds. Setting IdleTimeoutMs = 0 allows the application to wait indefinitely. The default value is 60000 (i.e. 60 seconds).
		*p: isconnected		&& Important: This property is decremented. Applications should instead call the CheckConnection method. Returns 1 if currently connected and logged into an FTP server, otherwise returns 0.
		*p: keepsessionlog		&& Turns the in-memory session logging on or off. If on, the session log can be obtained via the SessionLog property.
		*p: largefilemeasures		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.66. Enables internal features that can help when uploading or downloading extremely large files.
		*p: lastbinaryresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The binary data returned by the last (binary data returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepBinaryResult is set to 1.
		*p: lasterrorhtml		&& Provides information in HTML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrortext		&& Provides information in plain-text format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrorxml		&& Provides information in XML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lastmethodsuccess		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Indicate whether the last method call succeeded or failed. A value of 1 indicates success, a value of 0 indicates failure. This property is automatically set for method calls.
		*p: lastreply		&& Contains the last control-channel reply. For example: "550 Failed to change directory." or "250 Directory successfully changed." The control channel reply is typically formatted as an integer status code followed by a one-line description.
		*p: laststringresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The string return value of the last (string returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepStringResult is set to 1.
		*p: laststringresultlen		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.53. The length, in characters, of the string contained in the LastStringResult property.
		*p: listoption		&& Introduced in version 11.4.0. This property can be set to an option string, such as -a, which is added to the LIST command when retrieving FTP directory listings.
		*p: listpattern		&& A wildcard pattern, defaulting to "*" that determines the files and directories included in the following properties and methods: GetDirCount, GetCreateTime, GetFilename, GetIsDirectory, GetLastAccessTime, GetModifiedTime, GetSize.
		*p: loginverified		&& True if the FTP2 component was able to login to the FTP server after calling Connect.
		*p: numfilesanddirs		&& Undocumented/decremented property!
		*p: partialtransfer		&& A read-only property that indicates whether a partial transfer was received in the last method call to download a file. Set to 1 if a partial transfer was received. Set to 0 if nothing was received, or if the full file was received.
		*p: passive		&& Set to 1 for FTP to operate in passive mode, otherwise set to 0 for non-passive (.i.e. "active" or "port" mode). The default value of this property is 1.
		*p: passiveusehostaddr		&& This can handle problems that may arise when an FTP server is located behind a NAT router. FTP servers respond to the PASV command by sending the IP address and port where it will be listening for the data connection.
		*p: password		&& Password for logging into the FTP server.
		*p: percentdonescale		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. This property is only valid in programming environment and languages that allow for event callbacks. Sets the value to be defined as 100% complete for the purpose of PercentDone event callbacks.
		*p: port		&& Port number. Automatically defaults to the default port for the FTP service.
		*p: preferipv6		&& If 1, then use IPv6 over IPv4 when both are supported for a particular domain. The default value of this property is 0, which will choose IPv4 over IPv6.
		*p: prefernlst		&& If 1, the NLST command is used instead of LIST when fetching a directory listing. This can help in very rare cases where the FTP server returns truncated filenames.
		*p: progressmonsize		&& Progress monitoring for FTP downloads rely on the FTP server indicating the file size within the RETR response. Some FTP servers however, do not indicate the file size and therefore it is not possible to monitor progress based on percentage completion.
		*p: proxyhostname		&& The hostname of your FTP proxy, if a proxy server is used.
		*p: proxymethod		&& The proxy scheme used by your FTP proxy server. Valid values are 0 to 9. The default value is 0 which indicates that no proxy server is used.
		*p: proxypassword		&& The password for authenticating with the FTP proxy server.
		*p: proxyport		&& If an FTP proxy server is used, this is the port number at which the proxy server is listening for connections.
		*p: proxyusername		&& The username for authenticating with the FTP proxy server.
		*p: readtimeout		&& Forces a timeout when incoming data is expected on a data channel, but no data arrives for this number of seconds. The ReadTimeout is the amount of time that needs to elapse while no additional data is forthcoming.
		*p: requiresslcertverify		&& If 1, then the FTP2 client will verify the server's SSL certificate. The server's certificate signature is verified with its issuer, and the issuer's cert is verified with its issuer, etc. up to the root CA cert.
		*p: restartnext		&& Both uploads and downloads may be resumed by simply setting this property = 1 and re-calling the upload or download method.
		*p: sendbuffersize		&& Undocumented property! This property is now decremented, and has no effect in Chilkat versions 9.5.0.69 and greater. In the past, it affected how often percent completion callbacks were made.
		*p: sessionlog		&& Contains the session log if KeepSessionLog is turned on.
		*p: sockshostname		&& The SOCKS4/SOCKS5 hostname or IPv4 address (in dotted decimal notation). This property is only used if the SocksVersion property is set to 4 or 5).
		*p: sockspassword		&& The SOCKS5 password (if required). The SOCKS4 protocol does not include the use of a password, so this does not apply to SOCKS4
		*p: socksport		&& The SOCKS4/SOCKS5 proxy port. The default value is 1080. This property only applies if a SOCKS proxy is used (if the SocksVersion property is set to 4 or 5).
		*p: socksusername		&& The SOCKS4/SOCKS5 proxy username. This property is only used if the SocksVersion property is set to 4 or 5).
		*p: socksversion		&& SocksVersion May be set to one of the following integer values: 0 - No SOCKS proxy is used. This is the default. 4 - Connect via a SOCKS4 proxy. 5 - Connect via a SOCKS5 proxy.
		*p: sorcvbuf		&& Sets the receive buffer size socket option. Normally, this property should be left unchanged. The default value is 4194304. This property can be increased if download performance seems slow. It is recommended to be a multiple of 4096.
		*p: sosndbuf		&& Sets the send buffer size socket option. Normally, this property should be left unchanged. The default value is 262144. This property can be increased if upload performance seems slow. It is recommended to be a multiple of 4096.
		*p: ssl		&& Use TLS/SSL for FTP connections. You would typically set Ssl = 1 when connecting to port 990 on FTP servers that support TLS/SSL mode. Note: It is more common to use AuthTls.
		*p: sslallowedciphers		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.48. Provides a means for setting a list of ciphers that are allowed for SSL/TLS connections. The default (empty string) indicates that all implemented ciphers are possible.
		*p: sslprotocol		&& Selects the secure protocol to be used for secure (SSL/TLS) implicit and explicit (AUTH TLS / AUTH SSL) connections .
		*p: sslservercertverified		&& Read-only property that returns 1 if the FTP server's digital certificate was verified when connecting via SSL / TLS.
		*p: synccreatealllocaldirs		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.76
		*p: syncedfiles		&& The paths of the files uploaded or downloaded in the last call to SyncDeleteTree, SyncLocalDir, SyncLocalTree, SyncRemoteTree, or SyncRemoteTree2. The paths are listed one per line.
		*p: syncmustmatch		&& Can contain a wildcarded list of file patterns separated by semicolons. For example, "*.xml; *.txt; *.csv".
		*p: syncmustmatchdir		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.76. Can contain a wildcarded list of file patterns separated by semicolons. For example, "xml; txt; data_*".
		*p: syncmustnotmatch		&& Can contain a wildcarded list of file patterns separated by semicolons. For example, "*.xml; *.txt; *.csv". If set, the Sync* upload and download methods will not transfer files that match any one of these patterns.
		*p: syncmustnotmatchdir		&& ntroduced in version 9.5.0.76. Can contain a wildcarded list of file patterns separated by semicolons. For example, "xml; txt; data_*".
		*p: syncpreview		&& Contains the list of files that would be transferred in a call to SyncRemoteTree2 when the previewOnly argument is set to 1. This string property contains one filepath per line, separated by CRLF line endings.
		*p: tlsciphersuite		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Contains the current or last negotiated TLS cipher suite. If no TLS connection has yet to be established, or if a connection as attempted and failed, then this will be empty.
		*p: tlspinset		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.55. Specifies a set of pins for Public Key Pinning for TLS connections. This property lists the expected SPKI fingerprints for the server certificates.
		*p: tlsversion		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Contains the current or last negotiated TLS protocol version. If no TLS connection has yet to be established, or if a connection as attempted and failed, then this will be empty.
		*p: uncommonoptions		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.78. This is a catch-all property to be used for uncommon needs. This property defaults to the empty string and should typically remain empty.
		*p: uploadtransferrate		&& The average upload rate in bytes/second. This property is updated in real-time during any FTP upload (asynchronous or synchronous).
		*p: useepsv		&& If 1, the FTP2 component will use the EPSV command instead of PASV for passive mode data transfers. The default value of this property is 0. (It is somewhat uncommon for FTP servers to support EPSV.)
		*p: username		&& Username for logging into the FTP server. Defaults to "anonymous".
		*p: verboselogging		&& If set to 1, then the contents of LastErrorText (or LastErrorXml, or LastErrorHtml) may contain more verbose information. The default value is 0. Verbose logging should only be used for debugging.
	*</DefinedPropArrayMethod>

