		*m: percentdonescale_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP PercentDoneScale property.
		*m: percentdonescale_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the PercentDoneScale property.
		*m: pfile		&& Sends an HTTP/HTTPS request to the url. The verb can be "POST", "PUT", "PATCH", etc. The url can begin with "http://" or "https://" depending if TLS is desired. The body of the HTTP request is streamed directly from the localFilePath.
		*m: pfileasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the PFile method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: postbinary		&& Sends an HTTP POST request to the url. The body of the HTTP request contains the bytes passed in byteData. The contentType is a content type such as "image/gif", "application/pdf", etc.
		*m: postbinaryasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the PostBinary method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: postjson		&& A simplified way of sending a JSON POST and receiving the JSON response. The HTTP response is returned in an HTTP response object. The content type of the HTTP request is "application/json".
		*m: postjson2		&& The same as PostJson,except it allows for the content type to be explicitly provided. The PostJson method automatically uses "application/jsonrequest".
		*m: postjson2async		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the PostJson2 method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: postjson3		&& The same as PostJson2,except a JSON object is passed in for the request body. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: postjson3async		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the PostJson3 method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: postjsonasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the PostJson method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: posturlencoded		&& Sends a simple URL encoded POST. The form parameters are sent in the body of the HTTP request in x-www-form-urlencoded format. The content-type is "application/x-www-form-urlencoded". Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: posturlencodedasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the PostUrlEncoded method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: postxml		&& A simplified way of posting XML content to a web server. This method is good for making SOAP calls using HTTP POST.
		*m: postxmlasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the PostXml method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: preferipv6_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP PreferIPV6 property.
		*m: preferipv6_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the PreferIPV6 property.
		*m: proxyauthmethod_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP ProxyAuthMethod property.
		*m: proxyauthmethod_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ProxyAuthMethod property.
		*m: proxydirecttls_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP ProxyDirectTLS property.
		*m: proxydirecttls_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ProxyDirectTLS property.
		*m: proxydomain_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP ProxyDomain property.
		*m: proxydomain_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ProxyDomain property.
		*m: proxylogindomain_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP ProxyLoginDomain property.
		*m: proxylogindomain_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ProxyLoginDomain property.
		*m: proxylogin_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP ProxyLogin property.
		*m: proxylogin_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ProxyLogin property.
		*m: proxypassword_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP ProxyPassword property.
		*m: proxypassword_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ProxyPassword property.
		*m: proxyport_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP ProxyPort property.
		*m: proxyport_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ProxyPort property.
		*m: ptext		&& Sends an HTTP request to the url. The verb can be "POST", "PUT", "PATCH", etc. The body of the HTTP request contains the text passed in textData. The contentType is a content type such as "text/xml", "application/json", etc.
		*m: ptextasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the PText method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: ptextsb		&& The same as PText, but the data to be uploaded is passed in textData. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: ptextsbasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the PTextSb method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: putbinary		&& Sends an HTTP PUT request to the url. The body of the HTTP request is byteData. The contentType is a content type such as "image/gif", "application/pdf", etc.
		*m: putbinaryasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the PutBinary method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: puttext		&& Sends an HTTP PUT request to the url. The body of the HTTP request is textData. The charset should be set to a charset name such as "iso-8859-1", "windows-1252", "Shift_JIS", "utf-8", etc. The string "ansi" may also be used as a charset name.
		*m: puttextasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the PutText method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: quickdeletestr		&& Same as QuickGetStr, but uses the HTTP DELETE method instead of the GET method. Note: The HTTP response code is available in the LastStatus property
		*m: quickdeletestrasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the QuickDeleteStr method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: quickget		&& Sends an HTTP GET request for a URL and returns the binary response body. The URL may contain query parameters. If the SendCookies property is 1, matching cookies previously persisted to the CookiesDir are automatically included in the request.
		*m: quickgetasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the QuickGet method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: quickgetbd		&& The same as QuickGet, but returns the content in a Chilkat BinData object. The existing content of binData, if any, is cleared and replaced with the downloaded content.
		*m: quickgetbdasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the QuickGetBd method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: quickgetobj		&& Sends an HTTP GET request for a URL and returns the response object. If the SendCookies property is 1, matching cookies previously persisted to the CookiesDir are automatically included in the request.
		*m: quickgetobjasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the QuickGetObj method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: quickgetsb		&& The same as QuickGetStr, but returns the content in a Chilkat StringBuilder object. The existing content of sbContent, if any, is cleared and replaced with the downloaded content.
		*m: quickgetsbasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the QuickGetSb method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: quickgetstr		&& Sends an HTTP GET request for a URL and returns the response body as a string. The URL may contain query parameters. If the SendCookies property is 1, matching cookies previously persisted to the CookiesDir are automatically included in the request.
		*m: quickgetstrasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the QuickGetStr method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: quickputstr		&& Same as QuickGetStr, but uses the HTTP PUT method instead of the GET method. Note: The HTTP response code is available in the LastStatus property.
		*m: quickputstrasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the QuickPutStr method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: quickrequest		&& Sends an HTTP request with no body for a URL and returns the response object. The verb is typically "GET" or "DELETE". If the SendCookies property is 1, matching cookies previously persisted to the CookiesDir are automatically included in the request.
		*m: quickrequestasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the QuickRequest method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: quickrequestparams		&& This is the same as the QuickRequest method, except query params can be provided as non-URL-encoded name/value members in the json. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: quickrequestparamsasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the QuickRequestParams method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: readtimeout_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP ReadTimeout property.
		*m: readtimeout_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ReadTimeout property.
		*m: receivedcertreq_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP ReceivedCertReq property.
		*m: receivedcertreq_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ReceivedCertReq property.
		*m: redirectverb_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP RedirectVerb property.
		*m: redirectverb_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the RedirectVerb property.
		*m: referer_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP Referer property.
		*m: referer_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Referer property.
		*m: removequickheader		&& Undocumented method! Adds a custom header field to any HTTP request sent by a method that does not use the HTTP request object.
		*m: removerequestheader		&& Removes a header from the internal list of custom header field name/value pairs to be automatically added when HTTP requests are sent via methods that do not use the HTTP request object.
		*m: renderget		&& Same as QuickGet, but does not send the HTTP GET. Instead, it builds the HTTP request that would've been sent and returns it. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: requiredcontenttype_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP RequiredContentType property.
		*m: requiredcontenttype_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the RequiredContentType property.
		*m: requirehostnamematch_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP RequiredHostNameMatch property.
		*m: requirehostnamematch_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the RequiredHostNameMatch property.
		*m: requiresslcertverify_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP RequireSSLCertVerify property.
		*m: requiresslcertverify_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the RequireSSLCertVerify property.
		*m: resumedownload		&& Same as the Download method, except a failed download may be resumed. The targetFilename is automatically checked and if it exists, the download will resume at the point where it previously failed.
		*m: resumedownloadasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ResumeDownload method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: resumedownloadbd		&& Same as the DownloadBd method, except a failed download may be resumed. The download will resume at a point based on the number of bytes already contained in binData
		*m: resumedownloadbdasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ResumeDownloadBd method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3ssl_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP S3SSL property.
		*m: s3ssl_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the S3SSL property.
		*m: s3_createbucket		&& Creates a new Amazon S3 bucket.
		*m: s3_createbucketasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_CreateBucket method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_deletebucket		&& Deletes an Amazon S3 bucket. Note: If the bucket is in a region different than us-east-1, makes sure to set the AwsEndpoint property to the correct region, such as "eu-central-1".
		*m: s3_deletebucketasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_DeleteBucket method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_deletemultipleobjects		&& Deletes multiple objects from a bucket using a single HTTP request. The bucketName contains the names (also known as "keys") of the objects to be deleted.
		*m: s3_deletemultipleobjectsasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_DeleteMultipleObjects method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_deleteobject		&& Deletes a remote file (object) on the Amazon S3 service. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: s3_deleteobjectasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_DeleteObject method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_deleteobjects		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Deletes several objects from a bucket with a single request. objectNames includes the object names (or keys) to be deleted.
		*m: s3_deleteobjectsasync		&& ntroduced in version 11.0.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_DeleteObjects method with the arguments provided. Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: s3_downloadbd		&& The same as DownloadFile, except the downloaded file data is appended to bd. Note: If the bucket is in a region different than us-east-1, makes sure to set the AwsEndpoint property to the correct region, such as "eu-central-1".
		*m: s3_downloadbdasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_DownloadBd method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_downloadbytes		&& The same as DownloadFile, except the file data is returned directly in-memory instead of being written to a local file. Returns a zero-length byte array (as a Variant) on failure.
		*m: s3_downloadbytesasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_DownloadBytes method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_downloadfile		&& Downloads a file from the Amazon S3 service. Note: If the bucket is in a region different than us-east-1, makes sure to set the AwsEndpoint property to the correct region, such as "eu-central-1".
		*m: s3_downloadfileasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_DownloadFile method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_downloadstring		&& Downloads a text file (object) from the Amazon S3 service directly into a string variable. The charset specifies the character encoding, such as "utf-8", of the remote text object.
		*m: s3_downloadstringasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_DownloadString method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_fileexists		&& Determines if a remote object (file) exists. Returns 1 if the file exists, 0 if it does not exist, -1 if there was a failure in checking, or 2 if using in asynchronous mode to indicate that the background task was successfully started.
		*m: s3_fileexistsasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_FileExists method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_generateurl		&& Generates a temporary pre-signed URL for Amazon S3 using AWS Signature V2. (Call S3_GenerateUrlV4 to generate AWS Signature V4 pre-signed URLs.) Requires that the AwsSecretKey and AwsAccessKey be set to valid values prior to calling this method.
		*m: s3_generateurlv4		&& Generates a temporary pre-signed URL for Amazon S3 using AWS Signature V4. (Call S3_GenerateUrl to generate AWS Signature V2 pre-signed URLs.)
		*m: s3_genpresignedurl		&& Generates a temporary pre-signed URL for Amazon S3 using AWS Signature V4. Requires that the AwsSecretKey, AwsAccessKey, and AwsRegion properties be set to valid values prior to calling this method.
		*m: s3_listbucketobjects		&& Retrieves the XML listing of the objects contained within an Amazon S3 bucket. (This is like a directory listing, but in XML format.) The bucketPath name may be qualified with URL-encoded params.
		*m: s3_listbucketobjectsasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_ListBucketObjects method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_listbuckets		&& Retrieves the XML listing of the buckets for an Amazon S3 account. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: s3_listbucketsasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_ListBuckets method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_uploadbd		&& The same as S3_UploadFile, except the contents of the file come from bd instead of a local file. Note: x-amz-* headers, including metadata, can be added to any S3 request by adding each header with a call to SetRequestHeader.
		*m: s3_uploadbdasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_UploadBd method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_uploadbytes		&& The same as S3_UploadFile, except the contents of the file come from contentBytes instead of a local file. Note: x-amz-* headers, including metadata, can be added to any S3 request by adding each header with a call to SetRequestHeader.
		*m: s3_uploadbytesasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_UploadBytes method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_uploadfile		&& Uploads a file to the Amazon S3 service. Note: x-amz-* headers, including metadata, can be added to any S3 request by adding each header with a call to SetRequestHeader. This applies to all S3 methods, even if not explicitly stated.
		*m: s3_uploadfileasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_UploadFile method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: s3_uploadstring		&& Uploads an in-memory string to the Amazon S3 service. This is the same as UploadFile, except that the file contents are from an in-memory string instead of a local file.
		*m: s3_uploadstringasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_UploadString method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: savecookies_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SaveCookies property.
		*m: savecookies_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SaveCookies property.
		*m: sendbuffersize_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SendBufferSize property.
		*m: sendbuffersize_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SendBufferSize property.
		*m: sendcookies_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SendCookies property.
		*m: sendcookies_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SendCookies property.
		*m: sessionlogfilename_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SessionLogFileName property.
		*m: sessionlogfilename_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SessionLogFileName property.
		*m: setauthprivatekey		&& Sets the private key to be used with some forms of authentication. Starting in v9.5.0.89, this is used automatically add the Authorization header (Signature) for Amazon Pay requests. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setauthtokensb		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.95. Sets the AuthToken property. The sb contains the OAuth2 access token to be used. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setcookiexml		&& Restores cookies for a particular domain. It is assumed that the cookie XML was previously retrieved via the GetCookieXml method, and saved to some sort of persistent storage, such as within a database table.
		*m: setdpopkey		&& Introduced in version 11.4.0. Sets the EC private key for automatically adding the DPoP header to HTTP requests. Chilkat will generate a JWT for each request and include the DPoP header. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setoauthrsakey		&& Sets the RSA key to be used with OAuth authentication when the RSA-SHA1 OAuth signature method is used (see the OAuthSigMethod property). Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setrequestheader		&& Adds a custom header field to any HTTP request sent by a method that does not use the HTTP request object.
		*m: setsecurepassword		&& Equivalent to setting the Password property, but provides for a more secure way of passing the password in a secure string object. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setsslcertrequirement		&& Enforces a requirement on the server's certificate. The reqName can be one of the following: SubjectDN - SubjectCN - IssuerDN - IssuerCN - SAN (added in v9.5.0.84)
		*m: setsslclientcert		&& Allows for a client-side certificate to be used for an SSL connection. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure
		*m: setsslclientcertpem		&& Allows for a client-side certificate + private key to be used for the SSL / TLS connection (often called 2-way SSL). Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setsslclientcertpfx		&& Allows for a client-side certificate + private key to be used for the SSL / TLS connection (often called 2-way SSL). Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: seturlvar		&& Sets the value of a variable for substitutions in URLs passed to any method. Variables can appear in URLs in the following format: {$varName}. For example: https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/users/{$id}. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: sharepointonlineauth		&& Authenticates with SharePoint Online, resulting in a cookie being set and used for subsequent SharePoint HTTP requests.
		*m: sharepointonlineauthasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SharePointOnlineAuth method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: sleepms		&& Convenience method to force the calling process to sleep for a number of milliseconds.
		*m: snihostname_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SNIHostName property.
		*m: snihostname_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SNIHostName property.
		*m: sockshostname_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SOCKSHostName property.
		*m: sockshostname_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSHostName property.
		*m: sockspassword_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SOCKSPassword property.
		*m: sockspassword_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSPassword property.
		*m: socksport_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SOCKSPort property.
		*m: socksport_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSPort property.
		*m: socksusername_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SOCKSUserName property.
		*m: socksusername_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSUserName property.
		*m: socksversion_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SOCKSVersion property.
		*m: socksversion_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSVersion property.
		*m: sorcvbuf_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SoRcvBuf property.
		*m: sorcvbuf_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SoRcvBuf property.
		*m: sosndbuf_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SoSndBuf property.
		*m: sosndbuf_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SoSndBuf property.
		*m: sslallowedciphers_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SSLAllowedCiphers property.
		*m: sslallowedciphers_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSLAllowedCiphers property.
		*m: sslprotocol_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP SSLProtocol property.
		*m: sslprotocol_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSLProtocol property.
		*m: streamresponsebodypath_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP StreamResponseBodyPath  property.
		*m: streamresponsebodypath_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the StreamResponseBodyPath property.
		*m: synchronousrequest		&& Sends an explicit HttpRequest to an HTTP server and returns an HttpResponse object. The HttpResponse object provides full access to the response including all headers and the response body.
		*m: synchronousrequestasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SynchronousRequest method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: tlsciphersuite_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP TLSCipherSuite  property.
		*m: tlsciphersuite_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TLSCipherSuite property.
		*m: tlspinset_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP TLSPinSet property.
		*m: tlspinset_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TLSPinSet property.
		*m: tlsversion_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP TLSVersion property.
		*m: tlsversion_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TLSVersion property.
		*m: uncommonoptions_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP UncommonOptions roperty.
		*m: uncommonoptions_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UncommonOptions property.
		*m: unlockcomponent		&& Undocumented function! Appears related to Chilkat licensing.
		*m: updatecache_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP UpdateCache roperty.
		*m: updatecache_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UpdateCache property.
		*m: urldecode		&& URL decodes a string. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: urlencode		&& URL encodes a string. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: usebgthread_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP UseBgThread roperty.
		*m: usebgthread_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UseBgThread property.
		*m: useieproxy_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP UseIEProxy roperty.
		*m: useieproxy_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UseIEProxy property.
		*m: useragent_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP UserAgent roperty.
		*m: useragent_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UserAgent property.
		*m: verboselogging_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP VerboseLogging roperty.
		*m: verboselogging_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the VerboseLogging property.
		*m: verifytimestampreply		&& Verifies a timestamp reply received from a timestamp authority (TSA).
		*m: wasredirected_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HTTP WasRedirected roperty.
		*m: wasredirected_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the WasRedirected property.
		*m: xmlrpc		&& Makes an XML RPC call to a URL endpoint. The XML string is passed in an HTTP POST, and the XML response is returned. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: xmlrpcasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the XmlRpc method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: xmlrpcput		&& Same as XmlRpc, but uses the HTTP PUT method instead of the POST method. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: xmlrpcputasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the XmlRpcPut method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*p: abortcurrent		&& When set to 1, causes the currently running method to abort. Methods that always finish quickly (i.e.have no length file operations or network communications) are not affected.
		*p: accept		&& The Accept header field to be automatically included with GET requests issued by QuickGet or QuickGetStr. The default value is "*/*".
		*p: acceptcharset		&& The Accept-Charset header field to be automatically included with GET requests issued by QuickGet or QuickGetStr. The default value is "ISO-8859-1,utf-8;q=0.7,*;q=0.7".
		*p: acceptlanguage		&& The Accept-Language header field to be automatically included with GET requests issued by QuickGet or QuickGetStr. The default value is "en-us,en;q=0.5".
		*p: allowgzip		&& Controls whether the "Accept-Encoding: gzip" header is added to HTTP requests sent via any method that sends an HTTP request without using the HttpRequest object (such as QuickGetStr).
		*p: allowheaderfolding		&& If this property is set to 0, then no MIME header folding will be automatically applied to any request header. The default is 1.
		*p: authsignature		&& If set, then automatically adds the Authorization: Signature keyId="...", algorithm="...", headers="...", signature="..." header to all requests.
		*p: authtoken		&& If set, then automatically adds the "Authorization: Bearer " header to all requests. (If you have an OAuth2 access token, set this property equal to the OAuth2 access token string. Note: For OAuth1 (older) tokens, use the OAuthTOken property.)
		*p: autoaddhostheader		&& If set to true, the "Host" header field will automatically be added to the request header for any QuickGet or QuickGetStr method calls.
		*p: awsaccesskey		&& The AWS Access Key to be used with the Amazon S3 methods listed below.
		*p: awsendpoint		&& The regional endpoint (domain) to be used for Amazon S3 method calls. The default value is "s3.amazonaws.com".
		*p: awsregion		&& The AWS (S3) region, such as "us-east-1", "us-west-2", "eu-west-1", "eu-central-1", etc. This propery defaults to "us-east-1". It is only used when the AwsSignatureVersion property is set to 4.
		*p: awssecretkey		&& The AWS Secret Key to be used with the Amazon S3 methods listed below.
		*p: awssessiontoken		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.95. This is only used if a set of temporary security credentials were obtained by calling the AssumeRole action of the AWS Security Token Service.
		*p: awssignatureversion		&& Selects the AWS Signature Version algorithm. The default value is 4. May be set to 2 to select AWS Signature Version 2. (The only valid choices are 2 and 4.)
		*p: awssubresources		&& The AWS sub-resources to be used with the Amazon S3 methods listed below. If the S3 request needs to address a sub-resource, like ?versioning, ?policy, ?location, ?acl, or ?torrent, or ?versionid append the sub-resource and its value if it has one.
		*p: bandwidththrottledown		&& If non-zero, limits (throttles) the download bandwidth to approximately this maximum number of bytes per second. The default value of this property is 0.
		*p: bandwidththrottleup		&& If non-zero, limits (throttles) the upload bandwidth to approximately this maximum number of bytes per second. The default value of this property is 0.
		*p: basicauth		&& If HTTP basic authentication is needed, this property must be set to 1.
		*p: bglasterrortext		&& Undocumented property! When a background-enabled method is run asynchronously in a background thread, the last-error information is saved here and not in the LastErrorText property.
		*p: bgpercentdone		&& Undocumented property! The integer percent completed for a background HTTP method call. The value will be between 0 and 100 while a background method call is in progress. Otherwise, the value is meaningless.
		*p: bgresultdata		&& Undocumented method! If a backgrounded method returns a byte array, the returned data is found here.
		*p: bgresultint		&& Undocumented property! If a backgrounded method returns an integer, the return value is found here.
		*p: bgresultstring		&& Undocumented property! If a backgrounded method returns a string, the return value is found here.
		*p: bgtaskfinished		&& Undocumented property! Becomes true when the background method completes. Your application would periodically check for this condition.
		*p: bgtaskrunning		&& Undocumented property! If true then the object instance already has a backgrounded method running. Another backgrounded method cannot be started until the 1st completes.
		*p: bgtasksuccess		&& Undocumented property! This property's value is only meaningful (true or false) after a backgrounded method completes.
		*p: clientipaddress		&& The IP address to use for computers with multiple network interfaces or IP addresses. For computers with a single network interface (i.e. most computers), this property should not be set.
		*p: connectfailreason		&& This property will be set to the status of the last HTTP connection made (or failed to be made) by any HTTP method.
		*p: connection		&& The Connection header field to be automatically included with GET requests issued by QuickGet or QuickGetStr. The default value is "Keep-Alive". To prevent the Connection header from being added to the HTTP header, set this property to the empty string
		*p: connecttimeout		&& The amount of time in seconds to wait before timing out when connecting to an HTTP server. The default ConnectTimeout is 30 seconds.
		*p: cookiedir		&& Specifies a directory where cookies are automatically persisted if the Http.SaveCookies property is turned on. Cookies are stored in XML formatted files, one per domain, to main it easy for other programs to understand and parse.
		*p: debuglogfilepath		&& If set to a file path, causes each Chilkat method or property call to automatically append it's LastErrorText to the specified log file.
		*p: defaultfreshperiod		&& The default freshness period (in minutes) for cached documents when the FreshnessAlgorithm property is set to 0. The default value is 10080 (1 week).
		*p: digestauth		&& Setting this property to 1 causes the HTTP component to use digest authentication. The default value is 0.
		*p: enablesecrets		&& Introduced in version 11.5.0. This property that automatic resolution of credentials from the operating system’s secure storage. The default value is 0.
		*p: eventlogcount		&& Undocumented property! If the KeepEventLog property is set to true, then this property will contain the number of events that have accumulated in the in-memory event log. The events are indexed from 0 to EventLogCount-1.
		*p: fetchfromcache		&& Set to true if pages should be fetched from cache when possible. Only HTTP GET requests are cached. HTTP responses that include Set-Cookie headers are not cached.
		*p: finalredirecturl		&& If an HTTP GET was redirected (as indicated by the WasRedirected property), this property will contain the final redirect URL, assuming the FollowRedirects property is 1.
		*p: followredirects		&& If true, then 301, 302, 303, 307, and 308 redirects are automatically followed when calling QuickGet and QuickGetStr. FollowRedirects is true by default.
		*p: freshnessalgorithm		&& The freshness algorithm to use when determining the freshness of a cached HTTP GET response. A value of 1 causes an LM-factor algorithm to be used. This is the default.
		*p: heartbeatms		&& This property is only valid in programming environment and languages that allow for event callbacks.
		*p: ignoremustrevalidate		&& Some HTTP responses contain a "Cache-Control: must-revalidate" header. If this is present, the server is requesting that the client always issue a revalidate HTTP request instead of serving the page directly from cache.
		*p: ignorenocache		&& Some HTTP responses contain headers of various types that indicate that the page should not be cached. Chilkat HTTP will adhere to this unless this property is set to 1. The default value of this property is 0.
		*p: keepeventlog		&& Undocumented property!
		*p: keepresponsebody		&& If 1, then the response body, if text, is saved to the LastResponseBody property for all methods that do not return an HttpResponse object. The default value of this property is 0.
		*p: lastbinaryresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The binary data returned by the last (binary data returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepBinaryResult is set to 1.
		*p: lastcontenttype		&& The content-type of the last HTTP response received by the HTTP component.
		*p: lasterrorhtml		&& Provides information in HTML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrortext		&& Provides information in plain-text format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrorxml		&& Provides information in XML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lastfromcache		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.91. 1 if the last GET was fetched from cache.
		*p: lastheader		&& The text of the last HTTP header sent by any of this class's methods. The purpose of this property is to allow the developer to examine the exact HTTP header for debugging purposes.
		*p: lastmethodsuccess		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Indicate whether the last method call succeeded or failed. A value of 1 indicates success, a value of 0 indicates failure. This property is automatically set for method calls.
		*p: lastmoddate		&& The value of the Last-Modified header in the last HTTP response received by the HTTP component.
		*p: lastresponsebody		&& The response body of the last HTTP response received by the HTTP component (for methods that do not return an HttpResponse object). The last response body is only saved to this property IF the KeepResponseBody property is set to 1.
		*p: lastresponseheader		&& The entire response header for the last HTTP response received by the HTTP component (for methods that do not return an HttpResponse object).
		*p: laststatus		&& The last HTTP status value received by the HTTP component. This only applies to methods that do not return an HTTP response object.
		*p: laststatustext		&& The last HTTP status text received by the HTTP component. This only applies to methods that do not return an HTTP response object.
		*p: laststringresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The string return value of the last (string returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepStringResult is set to 1.
		*p: laststringresultlen		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.53. The length, in characters, of the string contained in the LastStringResult property.
		*p: lmfactor		&& An integer between 1 and 100 that indicates the percentage of time from the HTTP page's last-modified date that will be used for the freshness period. The default value is 25.
		*p: login		&& The HTTP login for pages requiring a login/password. Chilkat HTTP can do Basic, Digest, and NTLM HTTP authentication. (NTLM is also known as SPA (or Windows Integrated Authentication).
		*p: logindomain		&& The optional domain name to be used with NTLM / Kerberos / Negotiate authentication.
		*p: maxconnections		&& The maximum number of simultaneous open HTTP connections managed by the HTTP component. The Chilkat HTTP component automatically manages HTTP connections.
		*p: maxfreshperiod		&& Limits the amount of time a document can be kept "fresh" in the cache. The MaxFreshPeriod is specified in minutes, and the default value is 525600 which is equal to 1 year.
		*p: maxresponsesize		&& The maximum HTTP response size to be accepted by the calling program. A value of 0 (the default) indicates that there is no maximum value.
		*p: maxurllen		&& The Http class will automatically fail any URL longer than this length. The default MaxUrlLen is 2000 characters.
		*p: mimicfirefox		&& If set to 1, then the appropriate headers to mimic Mozilla/FireFox are automatically added to requests sent via the QuickGet and QuickGetStr methods.
		*p: mimicie		&& If set to 1, then the appropriate headers to mimic Internet Explorer are automatically added to requests sent via the QuickGet and QuickGetStr methods.
		*p: minfreshperiod		&& The freshness period for a document in cache will not be less than this value (in minutes). The default value is 30.
		*p: negotiateauth		&& Set this property equal to 1 for Negotiate authentication. Negotiate authentication will dynamically select Kerberos or NTLM authentication depending on what the server requires.
		*p: ntlmauth		&& Setting this property to 1 causes the HTTP component to use NTLM authentication (also known as IWA -- or Integrated Windows Authentication) when authentication with an HTTP server. The default value is 0.
		*p: numcachelevels		&& The number of directory levels to be used under each cache root. The default is 0, meaning that each cached HTML page is stored in a cache root directory.
		*p: numcacheroots		&& The number of cache roots to be used for the HTTP cache. This allows the disk cache spread out over multiple disk drives. Each cache root is a string indicating the drive letter and directory path.
		*p: oauth1		&& If 1 then causes an OAuth Authorization header to be added to any request sent by the HTTP object.
		*p: oauthbodyhash		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.91. If set to 1, then the oauth_body_hash is automatically added to an OAuth1 Authorization header. The oauth_body_hash contains the SHA-256 hash of the HTTP request body that is sent.
		*p: oauthcallback		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.69. The OAuth 1.0 callback URL. Defaults to "oob".
		*p: oauthconsumerkey		&& The OAuth consumer key to be used in the Authorization header.
		*p: oauthconsumersecret		&& The OAuth consumer secret to be used in computing the contents of the Authorization header.
		*p: oauthrealm		&& The OAuth realm to be used in the Authorization header.
		*p: oauthsigmethod		&& The OAuth signature method, such as "HMAC-SHA1" to be used in the Authorization header. The default is "HMAC-SHA1". It is also possible to choose "HMAC-SHA256", "RSA-SHA1" or "RSA-SHA2".
		*p: oauthtoken		&& The OAuth1 token to be used in the Authorization header. Note: This is for OAuth1. Use the AuthToken property for OAuth2.
		*p: oauthtokensecret		&& The OAuth token secret to be used in computing the Authorization header.
		*p: oauthverifier		&& The OAuth verifier to be used in the Authorization header.
		*p: password		&& The HTTP password for pages requiring a login/password. Chilkat HTTP can do Basic, Digest, and NTLM HTTP authentication. (NTLM is also known as SPA (or Windows Integrated Authentication).
		*p: percentdonescale		&& This property is only valid in programming environment and languages that allow for event callbacks. Sets the value to be defined as 100% complete for the purpose of PercentDone event callbacks.
		*p: preferipv6		&& If 1, then use IPv6 over IPv4 when both are supported for a particular domain. The default value of this property is 0, which will choose IPv4 over IPv6.
		*p: proxyauthmethod		&& Set this to "basic" if you know in advance that Basic authentication is to be used for the HTTP proxy. Otherwise leave this property unset. Note: It is not necessary to set this property.
		*p: proxydirecttls		&& Set to 1 if the proxy server expects a direct TLS connection. (This is where the initial connection to the HTTP proxy server is TLS. See Squid Direct TLS Connection. The default value of this property is 0.
		*p: proxydomain		&& The domain name of a proxy host if an HTTP proxy is used. This can also be set to an IP address.
		*p: proxylogin		&& If an HTTP proxy is used and it requires authentication, this property specifies the HTTP proxy login.
		*p: proxylogindomain		&& The NTLM authentication domain (optional) if NTLM authentication is used.
		*p: proxypassword		&& If an HTTP proxy is used and it requires authentication, this property specifies the HTTP proxy password.
		*p: proxyport		&& The port number of a proxy server if an HTTP proxy is used.
		*p: readtimeout		&& The amount of time in seconds to wait before timing out when reading from an HTTP server. The ReadTimeout is the amount of time that needs to elapse while no additional data is forthcoming.
		*p: receivedcertreq		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.92. Indicates whether the last HTTPS connection received a TLS CertificateRequest handshake message indicating that the server may require a client certificate.
		*p: redirectverb		&& Indicates the HTTP verb, such as GET, POST, PUT, etc. to be used for a redirect when the FollowRedirects property is set to 1. The default value of this property is "GET". This will produce the same behavior as a web browser (such as FireFox).
		*p: referer		&& The Referer header field to be automatically included with GET requests issued by QuickGet or QuickGetStr. The default value is the empty string which causes the Referer field to be omitted from the request header.
		*p: requiredcontenttype		&& If set, then any HTTP response to any POST or GET, including downloads, will be rejected if the content-type in the response header does not match this setting.
		*p: requirehostnamematch		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. If 1, then the hostname/domain in the URL must match at least one of the entries in the server certificate's SAN. The default value is 0.
		*p: requiresslcertverify		&& If 1, then the HTTP client will verify the server's SSL certificate. The certificate is expired, or if the cert's signature is invalid, the connection is not allowed. The default value of this property is 0.
		*p: s3ssl		&& If 1, then all S3_* methods will use a secure SSL/TLS connection for communications. The default value is 1.
		*p: savecookies		&& If this property is 1, cookies are automatically persisted to XML files in the directory specified by the CookiesDir property (or in memory if CookieDir = "memory"). Both CookiesDir and SaveCookies must be set for cookies to be persisted.
		*p: sendbuffersize		&& The buffer size to be used with the underlying TCP/IP socket for sending. The default value is 65535.
		*p: sendcookies		&& If 1, then cookies previously persisted to the CookiesDir are automatically added to all HTTP requests. Only cookies matching the domain and path are added.
		*p: sessionlogfilename		&& Enables file-based session logging. If set to a filename (or relative/absolute filepath), then the exact HTTP requests and responses are logged to a file. The file is created if it does not already exist, otherwise it is appended.
		*p: snihostname		&& Specifies the SNI hostname to be used in the TLS ClientHello. This property is only needed when the domain is specified via a dotted IP address and an SNI hostname is desired.
		*p: sockshostname		&& The SOCKS4/SOCKS5 hostname or IPv4 address (in dotted decimal notation). This property is only used if the SocksVersion property is set to 4 or 5).
		*p: sockspassword		&& The SOCKS5 password (if required). The SOCKS4 protocol does not include the use of a password, so this does not apply to SOCKS4.
		*p: socksport		&& The SOCKS4/SOCKS5 proxy port. The default value is 1080. This property only applies if a SOCKS proxy is used (if the SocksVersion property is set to 4 or 5).
		*p: socksusername		&& The SOCKS4/SOCKS5 proxy username. This property is only used if the SocksVersion property is set to 4 or 5).
		*p: socksversion		&& SocksVersion May be set to one of the following integer values: 0 - No SOCKS proxy is used. This is the default. 4 - Connect via a SOCKS4 proxy. 5 - Connect via a SOCKS5 proxy.
		*p: sorcvbuf		&& Sets the receive buffer size socket option. Normally, this property should be left unchanged. The default value is 4194304. This property can be increased if download performance seems slow. It is recommended to be a multiple of 4096.
		*p: sosndbuf		&& Sets the send buffer size socket option. Normally, this property should be left unchanged. The default value is 262144. This property can be increased if upload performance seems slow. It is recommended to be a multiple of 4096.
		*p: sslallowedciphers		&& Provides a means for setting a list of ciphers that are allowed for SSL/TLS connections. The default (empty string) indicates that all implemented ciphers are possible. The TLS ciphers supported in Chilkat v9.5.0.55 and later are:
		*p: sslprotocol		&& Note: Chilkat v9.5.0.84 supports TLS 1.3. In any TLS connection, during the initial TLS handshake, the client (such as Chilkat) indicates which versions of TLS it supports, and the server selects the version of TLS to be used for the connection.
		*p: streamresponsebodypath		&& Allows for the HTTP response body to be streamed directly into a file. If this property is set, then any method returning an HTTP response object will stream the response body directly to the file path specified.
		*p: tlsciphersuite		&& Contains the current or last negotiated TLS cipher suite. If no TLS connection has yet to be established, or if a connection as attempted and failed, then this will be empty.
		*p: tlspinset		&& Specifies a set of pins for Public Key Pinning for TLS connections. This property lists the expected SPKI fingerprints for the server certificates.
		*p: tlsversion		&& Contains the current or last negotiated TLS protocol version. If no TLS connection has yet to be established, or if a connection as attempted and failed, then this will be empty.
		*p: uncommonoptions		&& This is a catch-all property to be used for uncommon needs. This property defaults to the empty string and should typically remain empty.
		*p: updatecache		&& Controls whether the cache is automatically updated with the responses from HTTP GET requests.
		*p: usebgthread		&& Undocumented property! If true, then background-enabled methods will run in a background thread. Normally, a method will return after its work is completed.
		*p: useieproxy		&& If 1, the proxy address/port used by Internet Explorer will also be used by Chilkat HTTP. Note: This property only pays attention to the proxy address and port, and does not pay attention to additional information such as IE proxy server exceptions.
		*p: useragent		&& The UserAgent header field to be automatically included with GET requests issued by QuickGet or QuickGetStr. The default value is "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.3; WOW64; rv:49.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/49.0".
		*p: verboselogging		&& If set to 1, then the contents of LastErrorText (or LastErrorXml, or LastErrorHtml) may contain more verbose information. The default value is 0. Verbose logging should only be used for debugging.
		*p: wasredirected		&& Indicates whether the last HTTP request was redirected (i.e. the redirect was automatically followed).
	*</DefinedPropArrayMethod>

	*<PropValue>
		abortcurrent = 0
		accept = text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8
		acceptcharset = 
