	PROCEDURE quickget		&& Sends an HTTP GET request for a URL and returns the binary response body. The URL may contain query parameters. If the SendCookies property is 1, matching cookies previously persisted to the CookiesDir are automatically included in the request.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            QuickGet
		* Purpose:           Sends an HTTP GET request for a URL and returns the binary response body. 
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcURL -- the full URL.
		* Returns:           VarBinary
		* Date Added:        02/01/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Sends an HTTP GET request for a URL and returns the binary response body. 
		** The URL may contain query parameters. If the SendCookies property is 1, 
		** matching cookies previously persisted to the CookiesDir are automatically included in the request. 
		** If the FetchFromCache property is 1, the resource may be fetched directly from cache.
		**
		** Note: The HTTP response code is available in the LastStatus property. 
		** Other properties having information include LastResponseHeader, LastResponseBody, 
		** LastModDate, LastContentType, etc.
		**
		** A response code >= 400 is considered a failure. If the error response was textual in nature, 
		** then it will also be available in the LastResponseBody property.
		**
		** Enhancement to Version 66:
		** Improved performance for SFTP, FTP, and HTTP data transfers.
		**
		** Fix for version 82: The method did not properly set the WasRedirected 
		** and FinalRedirectUrl properties when redirects are automatically followed. 
		**
		** Returns a zero-length byte array (as a Variant) on failure.
		**
		** An empty array will have a UBound of -1 meaning 0 elements.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcURL AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_HTTP_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, lqBinData AS VarBinary
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, m.lqBinData
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      lqBinData = m.loChilkatObject.QuickGet(m.tcURL)
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lqBinData
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_HTTP_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

