	PROCEDURE s3_deletemultipleobjects		&& Deletes multiple objects from a bucket using a single HTTP request. The bucketName contains the names (also known as "keys") of the objects to be deleted.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            S3_DeleteMultipleObjects
		* Purpose:           Deletes multiple objects from a bucket using a single HTTP request.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcBucketName -- the bucket name to delete items within.
		* Returns:           Chilkat HTTP Response object or NULL
		* Date Added:        02/01/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.47
		**
		** Deletes multiple objects from a bucket using a single HTTP request. 
		** The bucketName contains the names (also known as "keys") of the objects to be deleted. 
		** To delete a specific version of an object, append a versionId attribute to the object name. 
		** For example: "SampleDocument.txt; VersionId="OYcLXagmS.WaD..oyH4KRguB95_YhLs7""
		**
		** Fixed for Version 66: Fixed AWS Signature V4 issues 
		** for some cases when query params are used with S3.
		**
		** Fixed in Version 69: Fixed problems with pre-signing URLs having to do with 
		** 8bit non-us-ascii chars in the filename, or “.” chars in the bucket name.
		** 
		** Fixed in Version 90: Fixed problems when “:” chars are used in bucket names.
		**
		** Update to Version 11.0.0: Method decremented.
		**
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcBucketName AS Character, toChilkatStringArray AS CHILKAT_STRINGARRAY_COM_CALL
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_HTTP_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, loParkParameterStringArray AS [iParkParameter OF ChilkatVFP.VCX], ;
		loChilkatStringArray AS CHILKAT_STRINGARRAY_COM_CALL, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterStringArray, m.loChilkatStringArray
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 47
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      loParkParameterStringArray = ;
		      NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], .ClassLibrary, [], m.toChilkatStringArray)
		
		      loChilkatStringArray = m.loParkParameterStringArray.GetObject()
		
		      TRY
		
		        loChilkatHTTPResponse = ;
		        m.loChilkatObject.S3_DeleteMultipleObjects(m.tcBucketName, m.loChilkatStringArray)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		      toChilkatStringArray = m.loParkParameterStringArray.SetObject(;
		      m.toChilkatStringArray, m.loChilkatStringArray)
		
		    ELSE
		
