	PROCEDURE s3_fileexists		&& Determines if a remote object (file) exists. Returns 1 if the file exists, 0 if it does not exist, -1 if there was a failure in checking, or 2 if using in asynchronous mode to indicate that the background task was successfully started.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            S3_FileExists
		* Purpose:           Determines if a remote object (file) exists.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcBucketPath -- the Amazon S3 bucket path.
		*                    tcObjectName -- the object to determine exists.
		* Returns:           Returns 1 if the file exists, 0 if it does not exist
		* Date Added:        02/02/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Determines if a remote object (file) exists. 
		** Returns 1 if the file exists, 0 if it does not exist, 
		** -1 if there was a failure in checking, 
		** or 2 if using in asynchronous mode to indicate that the background task was successfully started.
		** 
		** Note: If the bucket is in a region different than us-east-1, 
		** makes sure to set the AwsEndpoint property to the correct region, such as "eu-central-1". 
		** Also, if using an S3 compatible service such as Wasabi, always set the AwsEndpoint property. 
		** For example: "s3.wasabisys.com", "s3.eu-central-1.wasabisys.com".
		**
		** Fixed for Version 66: Fixed AWS Signature V4 issues 
		** for some cases when query params are used with S3.
		**
		** Fixed in Version 69:   Fixed problems with pre-signing URLs having to do with 
		** 8bit non-us-ascii chars in the filename, or “.” chars in the bucket name.
		**
		** Fixed in Version 75: Fixed problems with non-us-ascii chars in x-amz-meta-* headers
		** 
		** Fixed in Version 90: Fixed problems when “:” chars are used in bucket names.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcBucketPath AS Character, tcObjectName AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_HTTP_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, liFileStatus AS Integer
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		liFileStatus = 0
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      liFileStatus = m.loChilkatObject.S3_FileExists(m.tcBucketPath, m.tcObjectName)
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.liFileStatus
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_HTTP_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE s3_fileexistsasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the S3_FileExists method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            S3_FileExistsAsync
