	PROCEDURE setrequestheader		&& Adds a custom header field to any HTTP request sent by a method that does not use the HTTP request object.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            SetRequestHeader
		* Purpose:           Adds a custom header field to any HTTP request.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcHeaderFieldName -- the header field name
		*                    tcHeaderFieldValue -- the value within header field
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        02/02/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Adds a custom header field to any HTTP request 
		** sent by a method that does not use the HTTP request object. 
		** These methods include Download, DownloadAppend, GetHead, PostBinary, 
		** PostXml, PutBinary, PutText, QuickDeleteStr, QuickGet, QuickGetObj, 
		** QuickGetStr, QuickPutStr, XmlRpc, and XmlRpcPut.
		**
		** Cookies may be explictly added by calling this method passing "Cookie" for the headerFieldName.
		**
		** The RemoveRequestHeader method can be called to remove a custom header.
		**
		** Note1: Do not call this method to add Basic authentication, 
		** i.e. "Authorization: Basic ....". Instead, set the Login and Password properties, 
		** and also set the BasicAuth property = 1. 
		** Chilkat will add the "Authorization: Basic ..." header using the correct format automatically.
		**
		** Note 2: Never explicitly set the Content-Length header field. 
		** Chilkat will automatically compute the correct length 
		** and add the Content-Length header to all POST, PUT, 
		** or any other request where the Content-Length needs to be specified. 
		** (GET requests always have a 0 length body, and therefore never need a Content-Length header field.)
		**
		** Note 3: To add more than one header, call this method once per header field.
		**
		** Note 4:: Passing an empty value string causes the header to be removed. 
		** This was the unfortunate behavior of the method from the beginning, 
		** and cannot be changed for backward compatibility reasons. 
		** A workaround exists starting in v9.5.0.82 by adding the "AllowEmptyHeaders" 
		** keyword to the UncommonOptions property.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcHeaderFieldName AS Character, tcHeaderFieldValue AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_HTTP_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      m.loChilkatObject.SetRequestHeader(m.tcHeaderFieldName, m.tcHeaderFieldValue)
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_HTTP_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

