	HIDDEN PROCEDURE debuglogfilepath_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat HttpCurl DebugLogFilePath property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            DebugLogFilePath_Access
		* Purpose:           Access method used to retrieve 
		*                    the Chilkat HttpCurl DebugLogFilePath property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           THIS.DebugLogFilePath
		* Date Added:        05/15/2026
		*==============================================================================
		
		** 
		** If set to a file path, causes each Chilkat method or property call to automatically 
		** append it's LastErrorText to the specified log file. 
		** The information is appended such that if a hang or crash occurs, 
		** it is possible to see the context in which the problem occurred, 
		** as well as a history of all Chilkat calls up to the point of the problem. 
		** The VerboseLogging property can be set to provide more detailed information.
		**
		** This property is typically used for debugging the rare cases where a 
		** Chilkat method call hangs or generates an exception that halts program execution (i.e. crashes). 
		** A hang or crash should generally never happen. The typical causes of a hang are:
		** 
		** 1) a timeout related property was set to 0 to explicitly indicate that an infinite timeout is desired,
		** 2) the hang is actually a hang within an event callback (i.e. it is a hang within the application code), or
		** 3) there is an internal problem (bug) in the Chilkat code that causes the hang.
		** 
		
		LOCAL liStackLevel AS Integer, lcMethod AS Character, ;
		lcProperty AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_Stack[1, 1], la_IntroducedInBuild[3]
		
		STORE [] TO m.lcMethod, m.lcProperty, m.lcMethodToCall, m.la_Stack, m.la_IntroducedInBuild
		
		liStackLevel = ASTACKINFO(la_Stack)
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 11
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 5
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 0
		
		lcMethod = m.la_Stack(m.liStackLevel, 3)
		lcMethod = PROPER(SUBSTRC(m.lcMethod, AT_C([.], m.lcMethod) + 1))
		lcProperty = LEFTC(m.lcMethod, LENC(m.lcMethod) - 7)
		
		lcMethodToCall = [String]
		
		THIS.CallAccessObject(m.lcMethodToCall, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN EVALUATE([THIS.] + m.lcProperty)
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE debuglogfilepath_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the DebugLogFilePath property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            DebugLogFilePath_Assign
		* Purpose:           Assign method used to hold 
		*                    the Chilkat HttpCurl DebugLogFilePath property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcValue, character value 
		*                    used to hold a reference to the DebugLogFilePath property.
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        05/15/2026
		*==============================================================================
		
		LPARAMETERS tcValue AS Character
		
		LOCAL lcValidationMethod AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_IntroducedInBuild[3]
		
		lcValidationMethod = []
		lcMethodToCall = [String]
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 11
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 5
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 0
		
		THIS.CallAssignObject(m.tcValue, m.lcMethodToCall, m.lcValidationMethod, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE doyourthing		&& Introduced in version 11.5.0. Runs a the curl command specified in targetCurl. Returns success (1) if a response was received, in which case the response status code will be available in StatusCode
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            DoYourThing
		* Purpose:           Runs a the curl command specified in targetCurl. 
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcTargetCurl, the Curl command to be run
		* Returns:           Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		* Date Added:        05/15/2026
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 11.5.0
		**
		** Runs a the curl command specified in targetCurl. 
		** Returns success (1) if a response was received,
		** in which case the response status code will be available in StatusCode 
		** and the content of the response body will be available in one of two places:
		**
		**   If ResponseFilePath is non-empty, the response body 
		**   was streamed to the specified file path.
		**
		**   If ResponseFilePath is empty, the response body can be retrieved
		**   via ResponseBodyStr, GetResponseSb, or GetResponseBd. 
		**   Binary responses should only be retrieved via ResponseBodyBd .
		**
		** Assuming the HTTP response is JSON, the target outputs (variables) 
		** specified by prior calls to AddTargetOutput will be populated 
		** by applying each variable's JSON path to the response JSON.
		** 
		** Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		** 
		
		LPARAMETERS tcTargetCurl AS Character 
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS [Chilkat.HttpCurl], loException AS Exception, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liReturn AS Integer, luReturn AS Unknown
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		STORE 0 TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(11, 5, 0)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        STORE m.loChilkatObject.DoYourThing(m.tcTargetCurl) TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		    
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		  luReturn = .BitToLogical(m.liReturn)
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.luReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.HttpCurl])
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
		
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE doyourthingasync		&& Introduced in version 11.5.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the DoYourThing method with the arguments provided. Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            DoYourThingAsync
		* Purpose:           Creates an asynchronous task to call the DoYourThing 
		*                    method with the arguments provided. 
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcTargetCurl, a curl command specified in tcTargetCurl. 
		* Returns:           toChilkatTask, a Chilkat Task object.
		* Date Added:        05/15/2026
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 11.5.0.
		**
		** Creates an asynchronous task to call the DoYourThing method with the arguments provided. 
		** (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		** 
		** Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. 
		** Accessing and updating UI elements existing in the main thread may require special considerations.
		**
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcTargetCurl AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS [Chilkat.HttpCurl], loException AS Exception, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, loChilkatTask AS [Chilkat.Task]
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(11, 5, 0)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        loChilkatTask = m.loChilkatObject.DoYourThingAsync(m.tcTargetCurl)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		    
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.loChilkatTask
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.HttpCurl])
		  loChilkatTask = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.Task])
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

