DEFINE CLASS imap AS ibasechilkat OF "chilkatvfp.vcx" 		&& An IMAP client class for interacting with an IMAP server to read and manage email and IMAP mailboxes.
 	*< CLASSDATA: Baseclass="custom" Timestamp="" Scale="Pixels" Uniqueid="" />

	#INCLUDE "foxpro.h"
	*<DefinedPropArrayMethod>
		*m: abortcurrent_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP AbortCurrent property.
		*m: abortcurrent_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the AbortCurrent property.
		*m: addpfxsourcebd		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Adds a PFX file to the object's list of sources for locating certificates and private keys during decryption or signing. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: addpfxsourcedata		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.46. Returns 1 if the underlying TCP socket is connected to the IMAP server. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: addpfxsourcefile		&& Adds a PFX file to the object's internal list of sources to be searched for certificates and private keys when decrypting. Multiple PFX files can be added by calling this method once for each.
		*m: appendmail		&& Appends an email to an IMAP mailbox. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendmailasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the AppendMail method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: appendmime		&& Appends an email (represented as MIME text) to an IMAP mailbox. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendmimeasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the AppendMime method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: appendmimewithdate		&& Undocumented method! It is implied that the third parameter is a VFP DateTime value (see AppendMIMEWithDateStr).
		*m: appendmimewithdatestr		&& The same as AppendMimeWithDate, except the date/time is provided in RFC822 string format, such as "Wed, 18 Oct 2017 09:08:21 GMT". Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendmimewithdatestrasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the AppendMimeWithDateStr method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: appendmimewithflags		&& Same as AppendMime, but allows the flags associated with the email to be set at the same time. A flag is on if 1, and off if 0. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendmimewithflagsasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the AppendMimeWithFlags method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: appendmimewithflagssb		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.62. Same as AppendMimeWithFlags, but the MIME to be uploaded to the IMAP server is passed in a StringBuilder object. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: appendmimewithflagssbasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.62. Creates an asynchronous task to call the AppendMimeWithFlagsSb method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: appendseen_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP AppendSeen property.
		*m: appendseen_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the AppendfSeen property.
		*m: appenduid_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP AppendUID property.
		*m: appenduid_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the AppendUID property.
		*m: authmethod_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP AuthMethod property.
		*m: authmethod_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the AuthMethod property.
		*m: authzid_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP AuthZID property.
		*m: authzid_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the AuthZID property.
		*m: autodownloadattachments_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP AutoDownloadAttachments property.
		*m: autodownloadattachments_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the AutoDownloadAttachments property.
		*m: autofixsettings		&& Method to run after a connection is made to the server and the AutoFix property is set to 1.
		*m: autofix_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP AutoFix property.
		*m: autofix_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the AutoFix property.
		*m: capability		&& Sends a CAPABILITY command to the IMAP server and returns the raw response. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: capabilityasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Capability method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: checkconnection		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.46. Returns 1 if the underlying TCP socket is connected to the IMAP server. Internally, this method makes a lower-level socket system call to check if the TCP socket is still connected.
		*m: checkfornewemail		&& Checks for new email that has arrived since the mailbox was selected (via the SelectMailbox or ExamineMailbox methods), or since the last call to CheckForNewEmail (whichever was most recent).
		*m: checkfornewemailasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the CheckForNewEmail method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: clearsessionlog		&& Clears the contents of the SessionLog property.
		*m: clientipaddress_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP ClientIPAddress property.
		*m: clientipaddress_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ClientIPAddress property.
		*m: closemailbox		&& Closes the currently selected mailbox. Note: The term "mailbox" and "folder" are synonymous. Whenever the word "mailbox" is used, it has the same meaning as "folder". Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: closemailboxasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the CloseMailbox method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: connect		&& Connects to an IMAP server, but does not login. The domainName is the domain name of the IMAP server. (May also use the IPv4 or IPv6 address in string format.)
		*m: connectasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Connect method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: connectedtohost_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP ConnectedToHost property.
		*m: connectedtohost_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ConnectedToHost property.
		*m: connecttimeout_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP ConnectTimeout property.
		*m: connecttimeout_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ConnectTimeout property.
		*m: copy		&& Copies a message from the selected mailbox to copyToMailbox. If bUid is 1, then msgId represents a UID. If bUid is 0, then msgId represents a sequence number.  Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: copyasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Copy method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: copymultiple		&& Same as the Copy method, except an entire set of emails is copied at once. The set of emails is specified in messageSet. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: copymultipleasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the CopyMultiple method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: copysequence		&& Copies one or more emails from one mailbox to another. The emails are specified as a range of sequence numbers. The 1st email in a mailbox is always at sequence number 1. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: copysequenceasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the CopySequence method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: createmailbox		&& Creates a new mailbox. Note: The term "mailbox" and "folder" are synonymous. Whenever the word "mailbox" is used, it has the same meaning as "folder". Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: createmailboxasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the CreateMailbox method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: debuglogfilepath_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP DebugLogFilePath property.
		*m: debuglogfilepath_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the DebugLogFilePath property.
		*m: deletemailbox		&& Deletes an existing mailbox. Note: The term "mailbox" and "folder" are synonymous. Whenever the word "mailbox" is used, it has the same meaning as "folder". Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: deletemailboxasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the DeleteMailbox method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: disconnect		&& Disconnects cleanly from the IMAP server. A non-success return from this method only indicates that the disconnect was not clean -- and this can typically be ignored. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: disconnectasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Disconnect method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: domain_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP Domain property.
		*m: domain_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Domain property.
		*m: enablesecrets_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP EnableSecrets property.
		*m: enablesecrets_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the EnableSecrets property.
		*m: examinemailbox		&& Selects a mailbox such that only read-only transactions are allowed. This method would be called instead of SelectMailbox if the logged-on user has read-only permission. Note: The term "mailbox" and "folder" are synonymous.
		*m: examinemailboxasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ExamineMailbox method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: expunge		&& Permanently removes from the currently selected mailbox all messages that have the Deleted flag set. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: expungeandclose		&& Permanently removes from the currently selected mailbox all messages that have the Deleted flag set, and closes the mailbox. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: expungeandcloseasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ExpungeAndClose method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: expungeasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Expunge method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchattachment		&& Downloads one of an email's attachments and saves it to a file.
		*m: fetchattachmentasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchAttachment method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchattachmentbd		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.62. Downloads one of an email's attachments and returns the attachment data in a BinData object. ***See the FetchAttachment method description for more information about fetching attachments.
		*m: fetchattachmentbdasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.62. Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchAttachmentBd method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: fetchattachmentbytes		&& Downloads one of an email's attachments and returns the attachment data as in-memory bytes that may be accessed by an application. ***See the FetchAttachment method description for more information about fetching attachments.
		*m: fetchattachmentbytesasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchAttachmentBytes method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchattachmentsb		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.62. Downloads one of an email's attachments and returns the attachment data in a StringBuilder. It only makes sense to call this method for attachments that contain text data.
		*m: fetchattachmentsbasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.62. Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchAttachmentSb method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: fetchattachmentstring		&& Downloads one of an email's attachments and returns the attachment data as a string. It only makes sense to call this method for attachments that contain text data.
		*m: fetchattachmentstringasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchAttachmentString method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchbundle		&& Retrieves a set of messages from the IMAP server and returns them in an email bundle object. If the method fails, it may return a NULL reference. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: fetchbundleasmime		&& Retrieves a set of messages from the IMAP server and returns them in a string array object (NOTE: it does not return a string array, but an object that represents a string array.)
		*m: fetchbundleasmimeasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchBundleAsMime method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchbundleasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchBundle method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchchunk		&& Fetches a chunk of emails starting at a specific sequence number. A bundle of fetched emails is returned. The last two arguments are message sets that are updated with the ids of messages successfully/unsuccessfully fetched.
		*m: fetchchunk2		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Downloads a range of full emails based on a starting sequence number (seqnum) and count. The failed sequence numbers are recorded in failedSet. The fetched sequence numbers are recorded in fetchedSet.
		*m: fetchchunk2async		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchChunk2 method with the arguments provided. Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: fetchchunkasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchChunk method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchemail		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Downloads an email or its header based on provided arguments. If headerOnly is 1, only the email header is downloaded. The email is identified by msgId, which can be either a UID or sequence number.
		*m: fetchemailasync		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchEmail method with the arguments provided. Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchflags		&& Fetches the flags for an email. The bUid argument determines whether the msgId is a UID or sequence number. Returns the SPACE separated list of flags set for the email, such as "\Flagged \Seen $label1".
		*m: fetchflagsasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchFlags method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchheaders		&& Retrieves a set of message headers from the IMAP server and returns them in an email bundle object. If the method fails, it may return a NULL reference.
		*m: fetchheadersasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchHeaders method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchmsgset		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Downloads messages or their headers from the IMAP server based on the given arguments. If headersOnly is 1, only the message headers specified by msgSet are downloaded. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: fetchmsgsetasync		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchMsgSet method with the arguments provided. Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: fetchrange		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Downloads a range of full emails or email headers based on a starting sequence number (seqnum) and count. The downloaded emails are returned in bundle. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: fetchrangeasync		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchRange method with the arguments provided. Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchsequence		&& Downloads email for a range of sequence numbers. The 1st email in a mailbox is always at sequence number 1. The total number of emails in the currently selected mailbox is available in the NumMessages property.
		*m: fetchsequenceasmime		&& Same as FetchSequence, but instead of returning email objects in a bundle, the raw MIME of each email is returned. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: fetchsequenceasmimeasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchSequenceAsMime method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchsequenceasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchSequence method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchsequenceheaders		&& Same as FetchSequence, but only the email headers are returned. The email objects within the bundle will be lacking bodies and attachments.
		*m: fetchsequenceheadersasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchSequenceHeaders method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchsingle		&& Retrieves a single message from the IMAP server, including attachments if the AutoDownloadAttachments property is 1. If bUid is 1, then msgId represents a UID. If bUid is 0, then msgId represents a sequence number. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: fetchsingleasmime		&& Retrieves a single message from the IMAP server and returns a string containing the complete MIME source of the email, including attachments if the AutoDownloadAttachments property is 1.
		*m: fetchsingleasmimeasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchSingleAsMime method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchsingleasmimesb		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.62. Retrieves a single message from the IMAP server into the sbMime object. If bUid is 1, then msgId represents a UID.
		*m: fetchsingleasmimesbasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.62. Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchSingleAsMimeSb method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: fetchsingleasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchSingle method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchsinglebd		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.76. Retrieves a single message from the IMAP server into the mimeData object.. If bUid is 1, then msgId represents a UID. If bUid is 0, then msgId represents a sequence number.
		*m: fetchsinglebdasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.76. Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchSingleBd method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchsingleheader		&& Retrieves a single message header from the IMAP server. If the method fails, it may return a NULL reference.
		*m: fetchsingleheaderasmime		&& Fetches and returns the MIME of a single email header. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: fetchsingleheaderasmimeasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchSingleHeaderAsMime method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: fetchsingleheaderasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the FetchSingleHeader method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: getalluids		&& Returns a message set object containing all the UIDs in the currently selected mailbox. A NULL object reference is returned on failure. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: getalluidsasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the GetAllUids method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: getmailattachfilename		&& Returns the Nth attachment filename. Indexing begins at 0. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: getmailattachsize		&& Returns the Nth attachment size in bytes. Indexing begins at 0.
		*m: getmailboxstatus		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.46. Sends a "Status" command to get the status of a mailbox. Returns an XML string containing the status values as named attributes.
		*m: getmailboxstatusasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.46. Creates an asynchronous task to call the GetMailboxStatus method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: getmailflag		&& Returns the value of a flag (1 = yes, 0 = no) for an email. Both standard system flags as well as custom flags may be set.
		*m: getmailnumattach		&& Returns the number of email attachments.
		*m: getmailsize		&& Returns the size (in bytes) of the entire email including attachments.
		*m: getquota		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. Sends the GETQUOTA command and returns the response in JSON format. This feature is only possible with IMAP servers that support the QUOTA extension/capability.
		*m: getquotaasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. Creates an asynchronous task to call the GetQuota method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: getquotaroot		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. Sends the GETQUOTAROOT command and returns the response in JSON format. This feature is only possible with IMAP servers that support the QUOTA extension/capability. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: getquotarootasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. Creates an asynchronous task to call the GetQuotaRoot method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: getservercert		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Returns the IMAP server's digital certificate (for SSL / TLS connections). Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: getsslservercert		&& Returns the IMAP server's digital certificate (for SSL / TLS connections). Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: hascapability		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. Returns 1 if the capability indicated by name is found in the capabilityResponse. Otherwise returns 0.
		*m: heartbeatms_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP HeartbeatMs property.
		*m: heartbeatms_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the HeartbeatMs property.
		*m: highestmodseq_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP HighestModSeq property.
		*m: highestmodseq_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the HighestModSeq property.
		*m: httpproxyauthmethod_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP HTTPProxyAuthMethod property.
		*m: httpproxyauthmethod_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the HTTPProxyAuthMethod property.
		*m: httpproxydomain_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP HTTPProxyDomain property.
		*m: httpproxydomain_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the HTTPProxyDomain property.
		*m: httpproxyhostname_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP HTTPProxyHostName property.
		*m: httpproxyhostname_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the HTTPProxyHostName property.
		*m: httpproxypassword_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP HTTPProxyPassword property.
		*m: httpproxypassword_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the HTTPProxyPassword property.
		*m: httpproxyport_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP HTTPProxyPort property.
		*m: httpproxyport_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the HTTPProxyPort property.
		*m: httpproxyusername_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP HTTPProxyUserName property.
		*m: httpproxyusername_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the HTTPProxyUserName property.
		*m: idlecheck		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.26. Polls the connection to see if any real-time updates are available. The timeoutMs indicates how long to wait for incoming updates.
		*m: idlecheckasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.26. Creates an asynchronous task to call the IdleCheck method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: idledone		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.26. Sends a command to the IMAP server to stop receiving real-time updates. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: idledoneasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.26. Creates an asynchronous task to call the IdleDone method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: idlestart		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.26. Sends an IDLE command to the IMAP server to begin receiving real-time updates. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: idlestartasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.26. Creates an asynchronous task to call the IdleStart method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: isconnected		&& Returns the last known "connected" state with the IMAP server. IsConnected does not send a message to the IMAP server to determine if it is still connected.
		*m: isloggedin		&& Returns 1 if already logged into an IMAP server, otherwise returns 0.
		*m: isunlocked		&& Undocumented method! Returns true if the class has been unlocked.
		*m: keepsessionlog_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP KeepSessionLog property.
		*m: keepsessionlog_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the KeepSessionLog property.
		*m: lastappendedmime_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LastAppendedMIME property.
		*m: lastappendedmime_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastAppendedMIME property.
		*m: lastbinaryresult_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LastBinaryResult property.
		*m: lastbinaryresult_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastBinaryResult property.
		*m: lastcommand_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LastCommand property.
		*m: lastcommand_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastCommand property.
		*m: lasterrorhtml_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LastErrorHTML property.
		*m: lasterrorhtml_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastErrorHTML property.
		*m: lasterrortext_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LastErrorText property.
		*m: lasterrortext_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastErrorText property.
		*m: lasterrorxml_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LastErrorXML property.
		*m: lasterrorxml_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastErrorXML property.
		*m: lastintermediateresponse_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LastIntermediateResponse property.
		*m: lastintermediateresponse_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastIntermediateResponse property.
		*m: lastmethodsuccess_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LastMethodSuccess property.
		*m: lastmethodsuccess_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastMethodSuccess property.
		*m: lastresponsecode_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LastResponseCode property.
		*m: lastresponsecode_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastResponseCode property.
		*m: lastresponse_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LastResponse property.
		*m: lastresponse_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastResponse property.
		*m: laststringresultlen_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LastStringResultLen propert
		*m: laststringresultlen_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastStringResultLen property.
		*m: laststringresult_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LastStringResult propert
		*m: laststringresult_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastStringResult property.
		*m: listmailboxes		&& Returns a subset of the complete list of mailboxes available on the IMAP server. This method has the side-effect of setting the SeparatorChar property to the correct character used by the IMAP server, which is typically "/" or ".".
		*m: listmailboxesasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ListMailboxes method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: listsubscribed		&& The same as ListMailboxes, but returns only the subscribed mailboxes. (See ListMailboxes for more information.) Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: listsubscribedasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ListSubscribed method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: loadtaskcaller		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.80. Loads the caller of the task's async method. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: loggedinuser_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP LoggedInUser propert
		*m: loggedinuser_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LoggedInUser property.
		*m: login		&& Logs into the IMAP server. The component must first be connected to an IMAP server by calling Connect. If XOAUTH2 authentication is required, pass the XOAUTH2 access token in place of the password.
		*m: loginasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Login method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: loginsecure		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.71. The same as Login, except the login name and password are passed as secure strings. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: loginsecureasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.71. Creates an asynchronous task to call the LoginSecure method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: logout		&& Logs out of the IMAP server. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: logoutasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Logout method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: mbxlist		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Queries the IMAP server to retrieve the mailboxes in mboxes. If subscribed is 1, only subscribed mailboxes are included. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: mbxlistasync		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the MbxList method with the arguments provided. Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: movemessages		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.64. Moves a set of messages from one mailbox to another. Note: This is only possible if the IMAP server supports the "MOVE" extension.
		*m: movemessagesasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.64. Creates an asynchronous task to call the MoveMessages method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: noop		&& Sends a NOOP command to the IMAP server and receives the response. The component must be connected and authenticated for this to succeed.
		*m: noopasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Noop method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: nummessages_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP NumMessages property.
		*m: nummessages_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the NumMessages property.
		*m: peekmode_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP PeekMode property.
		*m: peekmode_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the PeekMode property.
		*m: percentdonescale_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP PercentDoneScale property.
		*m: percentdonescale_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the PercentDoneScale property.
		*m: port_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP Port property.
		*m: port_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Port property.
		*m: preferipv6_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP PreferIPV6 property.
		*m: preferipv6_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the PreferIPV6 property.
		*m: querymbx		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Searches the selected mailbox for messages matching criteria and returns a message set of all matches. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: querymbxasync		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the QueryMbx method with the arguments provided. Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: querythread		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Sends the THREAD command to search the already selected mailbox for messages that match bUid.
		*m: querythreadasync		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the QueryThread method with the arguments provided. Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: rawcommandbd		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Sends the raw command contained in bdCmd and returns the response in bdResp. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: rawcommandbdasync		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the RawCommandBd method with the arguments provided. Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: readtimeout_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP ReadTimeout property.
		*m: readtimeout_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ReadTimeout property.
		*m: refetchmailflags		&& Fetches the flags for an email and updates the flags in the email's header. When an email is retrieved from the IMAP server, it embeds the flags into the header in fields beginning with "ckx-".
		*m: refetchmailflagsasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the RefetchMailFlags method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: renamemailbox		&& Renames a mailbox. Can also be used to move a mailbox from one location to another. For example, from "Inbox.parent.test" to "Inbox.newParent.test", or from "abc.xyz" to "def.qrs". Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: renamemailboxasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the RenameMailbox method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: requiresslcertverify_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP RequireSSLCertVerify property.
		*m: requiresslcertverify_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the RequireSSLCertVerify property.
		*m: search		&& Searches the already selected mailbox for messages that match criteria and returns a message set of all matching messages. If bUid is 1, then UIDs are returned in the message set, otherwise sequence numbers are returned.
		*m: searchasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Search method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: searchcharset_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SearchCharset property.
		*m: searchcharset_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SearchCharset property.
		*m: selectedmailbox_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SelectedMailbox property.
		*m: selectedmailbox_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SelectedMailbox property.
		*m: selectmailbox		&& Selects a mailbox. A mailbox must be selected before some methods, such as Search or FetchSingle, can be called. If the logged-on user does not have write-access to the mailbox, call ExamineMailbox instead.
		*m: selectmailboxasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SelectMailbox method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sendbuffersize_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SendBufferSize property.
		*m: sendbuffersize_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SendBufferSize property.
		*m: sendrawcommand		&& Allows for the sending of arbitrary commands to the IMAP server. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: sendrawcommandasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SendRawCommand method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sendrawcommandb		&& The same as SendRawCommand, but instead of returning the response as a string, the binary bytes of the response are returned. Returns a zero-length byte array (as a Variant) on failure. An empty array will have a UBound of -1 meaning 0 elements.
		*m: sendrawcommandbasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SendRawCommandB method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sendrawcommandc		&& The same as SendRawCommandB, except that the command is provided as binary bytes rather than a string. Returns a zero-length byte array (as a Variant) on failure. An empty array will have a UBound of -1 meaning 0 elements.
		*m: sendrawcommandcasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SendRawCommandC method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: separatorchar_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SeparatorChar property.
		*m: separatorchar_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SeparatorChar property.
		*m: sessionlog_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SessionLog property.
		*m: sessionlog_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SessionLog property.
		*m: setcsp		&& Undocumented method! Accepts a (decremented) Chilkat CSP reference.
		*m: setdecryptcert		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.40. Explicitly specifies the certificate to be used for decrypting encrypted email. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setdecryptcert2		&& Used to explicitly specify the certificate and associated private key to be used for decrypting S/MIME (PKCS7) email. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setflag		&& Sets a flag for a single message on the IMAP server. If value = 1, the flag is turned on, if value = 0, the flag is turned off. Standard system flags such as "\Deleted", "\Seen", "\Answered", "\Flagged", "\Draft", and "\Answered" may be set.
		*m: setflagasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SetFlag method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: setflags		&& Sets a flag for each message in the message set on the IMAP server. If value = 1, the flag is turned on, if value = 0, the flag is turned off.
		*m: setflagsasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SetFlags method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: setmailflag		&& Sets a flag for a single message on the IMAP server. The UID of the email object is used to find the message on the IMAP server that is to be affected. If value = 1, the flag is turned on, if value = 0, the flag is turned off.
		*m: setmailflagasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SetMailFlag method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: setquota		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. Sets the quota for a quotaRoot. The resource should be one of two keywords:"STORAGE" or "MESSAGE". Use "STORAGE" to set the maximum capacity of the combined messages in quotaRoot.
		*m: setquotaasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SetQuota method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: setsslclientcert		&& Specifies a client-side certificate to be used for the SSL / TLS connection. In most cases, servers do not require client-side certificates for SSL/TLS.
		*m: setsslclientcertpem		&& Same as SetSslClientCert, but allows a .pfx/.p12 file to be used directly) Specifies a client-side certificate to be used for the SSL / TLS connection. In most cases, servers do not require client-side certificates for SSL/TLS.
		*m: setsslclientcertpfx		&& (Same as SetSslClientCert, but allows a .pfx/.p12 file to be used directly) Specifies a client-side certificate to be used for the SSL / TLS connection. In most cases, servers do not require client-side certificates for SSL/TLS.
		*m: sockshostname_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SOCKSHostName property.
		*m: sockshostname_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSHostName property.
		*m: sockspassword_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SOCKSPassword property.
		*m: sockspassword_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSPassword property.
		*m: socksport_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SOCKSPort property.
		*m: socksport_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSPort property.
		*m: socksusername_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SOCKSUserName property.
		*m: socksusername_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSUserName property.
		*m: socksversion_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SOCKSVersion property.
		*m: socksversion_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSVersion property.
		*m: sorcvbuf_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SoRcvBuf property.
		*m: sorcvbuf_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SoRcvBuf property.
		*m: sort		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.76. Searches the already selected mailbox for messages that match searchCriteria and returns a message set of all matching messages in the order specified by sortCriteria
		*m: sortasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.76. Creates an asynchronous task to call the Sort method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sortcriteria_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SortCriteria property.
		*m: sortcriteria_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SortCriteria property.
		*m: sosndbuf_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SoSndBuf property.
		*m: sosndbuf_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SoSndBuf property.
		*m: sshauthenticatepk		&& Authenticates with the SSH server using public-key authentication. The corresponding public key must have been installed on the SSH server for the sshLogin. Authentication will succeed if the matching privateKey is provided.
		*m: sshauthenticatepkasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SshAuthenticatePk method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sshauthenticatepw		&& Authenticates with the SSH server using a sshLogin and sshPassword. An SSH tunneling (port forwarding) session always begins by first calling SshTunnel to connect to the SSH server, then calling either AuthenticatePw or AuthenticatePk to authenticate.
		*m: sshauthenticatepwasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SshAuthenticatePw method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sshclosetunnel		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Closes the SSH tunnel previously opened by SshOpenTunnel. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: sshclosetunnelasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SshCloseTunnel method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sshopentunnel		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Connects to an SSH server and creates a tunnel for IMAP. The sshHostname is the hostname (or IP address) of the SSH server. The sshPort is typically 22, which is the standard SSH port number.
		*m: sshopentunnelasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SshOpenTunnel method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sshtunnel		&& Undocumented method!
		*m: sslallowedciphers_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SSLAllowedCiphers property.
		*m: sslallowedciphers_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSLAllowedCiphers property.
		*m: sslprotocol_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SSLProtocol property.
		*m: sslprotocol_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSLProtocol property.
		*m: sslservercertverified_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SSLServerCertVerified property.
		*m: sslservercertverified_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSLServerCertVerified property.
		*m: ssl_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP SSL property.
		*m: ssl_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSL property.
		*m: starttls_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP StartTLS property.
		*m: starttls_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the StartTLS property.
		*m: storeflags		&& Sets one or more flags to a specific value for an email. The email is indicated by either a UID or sequence number, depending on whether bUid is 1 (UID) or 0 (sequence number). flagNames should be a space separated string of flag names.
		*m: storeflagsasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the StoreFlags method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: subscribe		&& Subscribe to an IMAP mailbox. Note: The term "mailbox" and "folder" are synonymous. Whenever the word "mailbox" is used, it has the same meaning as "folder". Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: subscribeasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Subscribe method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: threadcmd		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.77. Sends the THREAD command to search the already selected mailbox for messages that match searchCriteria.
		*m: threadcmdasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.77. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ThreadCmd method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: tlsciphersuite_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP TLSCipherSuite property.
		*m: tlsciphersuite_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TLSCiipherSuite property.
		*m: tlspinset_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP TLSPinSet property.
		*m: tlspinset_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TLSPinSet property.
		*m: tlsversion_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP TLSVersion property.
		*m: tlsversion_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TLSVersion property.
		*m: uidnext_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP UIDNext property.
		*m: uidnext_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UIDNext property.
		*m: uidvalidity_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP UIDValidity property.
		*m: uidvalidity_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UIDValidity property.
		*m: uncommonoptions_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP UncommonOptions property.
		*m: uncommonoptions_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UncommonOptions property.
		*m: unlockcomponent		&& Undocumented method! Appears related to Chilkat licensing.
		*m: unsubscribe		&& Unsubscribe from an IMAP mailbox. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: unsubscribeasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Unsubscribe method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: usecertvault		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.40. Adds an XML certificate vault to the object's internal list of sources to be searched for certificates and private keys when encrypting/decrypting or signing/verifying.
		*m: usessh		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.55. Uses an existing SSH tunnel for the connections to the POP3 andSMTP servers. This method is identical to the UseSshTunnel method, except the SSH connection is obtained from an SSH object instead of a Socket object.
		*m: usesshtunnel		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Uses an existing SSH tunnel. This is useful for sharing an existing SSH tunnel connection wth other objects.
		*m: verboselogging_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat IMAP VerboseLogging property.
		*m: verboselogging_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the VerboseLogging property.
		*p: abortcurrent		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. When set to 1, causes the currently running method to abort. Methods that always finish quickly (i.e.have no length file operations or network communications) are not affected.
		*p: appendseen		&& When 1 (the default) the Append method will mark the email appended to a mailbox as already seen. Otherwise an appended email will be initialized to have a status of unseen.
		*p: appenduid		&& The UID of the last email appended to a mailbox via an Append* method. (Not all IMAP servers report back the UID of the email appended.)
		*p: authmethod		&& Can be set to "XOAUTH2", "CRAM-MD5", "NTLM", "PLAIN", or "LOGIN" to select the authentication method. NTLM is the most secure, and is a synonym for "Windows Integrated Authentication".
		*p: authzid		&& Applies to the PLAIN authentication method. May be set to an authorization ID that is to be sent along with the Login and Password for authentication.
		*p: autodownloadattachments		&& If set to 1, then all Fetch* methods will also automatically download attachments. If set to 0, then the Fetch* methods download the email without attachments. The default value is 1.
		*p: autofix		&& If 1, then the following will occur when a connection is made to an IMAP server: 1) If the Port property = 993, then sets StartTls = 0 and Ssl = 1 2) If the Port property = 143, sets Ssl = 0. The default value of this property is 1.
		*p: clientipaddress		&& The IP address to use for computers with multiple network interfaces or IP addresses. For computers with a single network interface (i.e. most computers), this property should not be set.
		*p: connectedtohost		&& Contains the IMAP server's domain name (or IP address) if currently connected. Otherwise returns an empty string.
		*p: connecttimeout		&& Maximum number of seconds to wait when connecting to an IMAP server. The default value is 30 (units are in seconds).
		*p: debuglogfilepath		&& If set to a file path, causes each Chilkat method or property call to automatically append it's LastErrorText to the specified log file.
		*p: domain		&& The Windows Domain to use for Windows Integrated Authentication (also known as NTLM). This may be empty.
		*p: enablesecrets		&& Introduced in version 11.5.0. This property that automatic resolution of credentials from the operating system’s secure storage. The default value is 0.
		*p: heartbeatms		&& This is the number of milliseconds between each AbortCheck event callback. The AbortCheck callback allows an application to abort any IMAP operation prior to completion. If HeartbeatMs is 0, no AbortCheck event callbacks will occur.
		*p: highestmodseq		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.87. A string containing an integer value that is the HIGHESTMODSEQ of the currently selected mailbox, or 0 if no mailbox is selected.
		*p: httpproxyauthmethod		&& If an HTTP proxy requiring authentication is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy authentication method name. Valid choices are "Basic" or "NTLM".
		*p: httpproxydomain		&& The NTLM authentication domain (optional) if NTLM authentication is used.
		*p: httpproxyhostname		&& If an HTTP proxy is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy hostname or IPv4 address (in dotted decimal notation).
		*p: httpproxypassword		&& If an HTTP proxy requiring authentication is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy password.
		*p: httpproxyport		&& If an HTTP proxy is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy port number. (Two commonly used HTTP proxy ports are 8080 and 3128.)
		*p: httpproxyusername		&& If an HTTP proxy requiring authentication is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy login name.
		*p: keepsessionlog		&& Turns the in-memory session logging on or off. If on, the session log can be obtained via the SessionLog property. The default value is 0.
		*p: lastappendedmime		&& The MIME source of the email last appended during a call to AppendMail, or AppendMime.
		*p: lastbinaryresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The binary data returned by the last (binary data returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepBinaryResult is set to 1.
		*p: lastcommand		&& The last raw command sent to the IMAP server. (This information can be used for debugging if problems occur.)
		*p: lasterrorhtml		&& Provides information in HTML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrortext		&& Provides information in plain-text format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrorxml		&& Provides information in XML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lastintermediateresponse		&& The last intermediate response received from the IMAP server. (This information can be used for debugging if problems occur.)
		*p: lastmethodsuccess		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Indicate whether the last method call succeeded or failed. A value of 1 indicates success, a value of 0 indicates failure. This property is automatically set for method calls. It is not modified by property accesses.
		*p: lastresponse		&& The raw data of the last response from the IMAP server. (Useful for debugging if problems occur.) This property is cleared whenever a command is sent to the IMAP server. If no response is received, then this property will remain empty.
		*p: lastresponsecode		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.44. The response code part of the last command response, if it exists. IMAP status responses MAY include an OPTIONAL "response code".
		*p: laststringresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The string return value of the last (string returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepStringResult is set to 1.
		*p: laststringresultlen		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.53. The length, in characters, of the string contained in the LastStringResult property.
		*p: loggedinuser		&& If logged into an IMAP server, the logged-in username.
		*p: nummessages		&& After selecting a mailbox (by calling SelectMailbox), this property will be updated to reflect the total number of emails in the mailbox.
		*p: peekmode		&& Set to true to prevent the mail flags (such as the "Seen" flag) from being set when email is retrieved. The default value of this property is false.
		*p: percentdonescale		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. This property is only valid in programming environment and languages that allow for event callbacks. Sets the value to be defined as 100% complete for the purpose of PercentDone event callbacks.
		*p: port		&& The IMAP port number. If using SSL, be sure to set this to the IMAP SSL port number, which is typically port 993. (If this is the case, make sure you also set the Ssl property = 1.
		*p: preferipv6		&& If 1, then use IPv6 over IPv4 when both are supported for a particular domain. The default value of this property is 0, which will choose IPv4 over IPv6.
		*p: readtimeout		&& The maximum amount of time (in seconds) that incoming data is allowed to stall while reading any kind of response from an IMAP server. This is the amount of time that needs to elapse while no additional response bytes are forthcoming.
		*p: requiresslcertverify		&& If 1, then the IMAP client will verify the server's SSL certificate. The certificate is expired, or if the cert's signature is invalid, the connection is not allowed. The default value of this property is 0.
		*p: searchcharset		&& The "CHARSET" to be used in searches issued by the Search method. The default value is "UTF-8". (If no 8bit chars are found in the search criteria passed to the Search method, then no CHARSET is needed and this property doesn't apply.)
		*p: selectedmailbox		&& The currently selected mailbox, or an empty string if none.
		*p: sendbuffersize		&& The buffer size to be used with the underlying TCP/IP socket for sending. The default value is 32767.
		*p: separatorchar		&& The separator character used by the IMAP server for the mailbox hierarchy. It is typically "/" or ".", but may vary depending on the IMAP server.
		*p: sessionlog		&& Contains an in-memory log of the raw commands sent to the IMAP server, and the raw responses received from the IMAP server. The KeepSessionLog property must be set to 1 to enable session logging. Call ClearSessionLog to reset the log.
		*p: sockshostname		&& The SOCKS4/SOCKS5 hostname or IPv4 address (in dotted decimal notation). This property is only used if the SocksVersion property is set to 4 or 5).
		*p: sockspassword		&& The SOCKS5 password (if required). The SOCKS4 protocol does not include the use of a password, so this does not apply to SOCKS4.
		*p: socksport		&& The SOCKS4/SOCKS5 proxy port. The default value is 1080. This property only applies if a SOCKS proxy is used (if the SocksVersion property is set to 4 or 5).
		*p: socksusername		&& The SOCKS4/SOCKS5 proxy username. This property is only used if the SocksVersion property is set to 4 or 5).
		*p: socksversion		&& SocksVersion May be set to one of the following integer values: 0 - No SOCKS proxy is used. This is the default. 4 - Connect via a SOCKS4 proxy. 5 - Connect via a SOCKS5 proxy.
		*p: sorcvbuf		&& Sets the receive buffer size socket option. Normally, this property should be left unchanged. The default value is 4194304. This property can be increased if download performance seems slow. It is recommended to be a multiple of 4096.
		*p: sortcriteria		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. This applies to the QueryMbx method to set a sort order for search results. By default, this property is an empty string. Can be set to a string of SPACE separated keywords to indicate sort order (default is ascending).
		*p: sosndbuf		&& Sets the send buffer size socket option. Normally, this property should be left unchanged. The default value is 262144. This property can be increased if upload performance seems slow. It is recommended to be a multiple of 4096.
		*p: ssl		&& 1 if the IMAP connection should be TLS/SSL. Note: The typical IMAP TLS/SSL port number is 993. If you set this property = 1, it is likely that you should also set the Port property = 993.
		*p: sslallowedciphers		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.48. Provides a means for setting a list of ciphers that are allowed for SSL/TLS connections. The default (empty string) indicates that all implemented ciphers are possible.
		*p: sslprotocol		&& Selects the secure protocol to be used for secure (SSL/TLS) connections.
		*p: sslservercertverified		&& Read-only property that returns 1 if the IMAP server's digital certificate was verified when connecting via SSL / TLS.
		*p: starttls		&& If 1, then the Connect method will (internallly) convert the connection to TLS/SSL via the STARTTLS IMAP command. This is called "explict SSL/TLS" because the client explicitly requests the connection be transformed into a TLS/SSL secure channel.
		*p: tlsciphersuite		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Contains the current or last negotiated TLS cipher suite. If no TLS connection has yet to be established, or if a connection as attempted and failed, then this will be empty.
		*p: tlspinset		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.55. Specifies a set of pins for Public Key Pinning for TLS connections. This property lists the expected SPKI fingerprints for the server certificates.
		*p: tlsversion		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Contains the current or last negotiated TLS protocol version. If no TLS connection has yet to be established, or if a connection as attempted and failed, then this will be empty.
		*p: uidnext		&& A positive integer value containing the UIDNEXT of the currently selected folder, or 0 if it's not available or no folder is selected.
		*p: uidvalidity		&& An integer value containing the UIDVALIDITY of the currently selected mailbox, or 0 if no mailbox is selected. A client can save the UidValidity value for a mailbox and then compare it with the UidValidity on a subsequent session.
		*p: uncommonoptions		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.80. This is a catch-all property to be used for uncommon needs. This property defaults to the empty string and should typically remain empty.
		*p: verboselogging		&& If set to 1, then the contents of LastErrorText (or LastErrorXml, or LastErrorHtml) may contain more verbose information. The default value is 0. Verbose logging should only be used for debugging.
	*</DefinedPropArrayMethod>

	*<PropValue>
		abortcurrent = 0
		appendseen = 1
		appenduid = 0
		authmethod = LOGIN
