	PROCEDURE getmailboxstatus		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.46. Sends a "Status" command to get the status of a mailbox. Returns an XML string containing the status values as named attributes.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            GetMailBoxStatus
		* Purpose:           Sends a "Status" command to get the status of a mailbox.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcMailBox, the mailbox to examine.
		* Returns:           The mailbox status
		* Date Added:        06/22/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.46
		**
		** Sends a "Status" command to get the status of a mailbox. 
		** Returns an XML string containing the status values as named attributes. 
		** Possible status values are:
		** 
		**   messages: The number of messages in the mailbox.
		**   recent: The number of messages with the \Recent flag set.
		**   uidnext: The next unique identifier value of the mailbox.
		**   uidvalidity: The unique identifier validity value of the mailbox.
		**   unseen: The number of messages which do not have the \Seen flag set.
		**
		** An example of the string returned by this method is: 
		** <status messages="240" recent="0" uidnext="3674" uidvalidity="3" unseen="213" />
		** 
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcMailBox AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_IMAP_COM_CALL, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		loException AS Exception, lcMailBoxStatus AS Character
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		lcMailBoxStatus = []
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 46
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        lcMailBoxStatus = m.loChilkatObject.GetMailBoxStatus(m.tcMailBox)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcMailBoxStatus
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_IMAP_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
		
	ENDPROC

