	PROCEDURE idlecheck		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.26. Polls the connection to see if any real-time updates are available. The timeoutMs indicates how long to wait for incoming updates.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            IdleCheck
		* Purpose:           Polls the connection to see if any real-time updates are available.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tiTimeoutMs, the millisecond time out value.
		* Returns:           The XML updates
		* Date Added:        06/22/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.26
		**
		** Polls the connection to see if any real-time updates are available. 
		** The timeoutMs indicates how long to wait for incoming updates. 
		** This method does not send a command to the IMAP server, 
		** it simply checks the connection for already-arrived messages 
		** that the IMAP server sent. This method would only be called 
		** after IDLE has already been started via the IdleStart method.
		** 
		** If updates are available, they are returned in an XML string 
		** having the format as shown below. There is one child node for each notification. 
		** The possible notifcations are:
		** 
		**  1) flags -- lists flags that have been set or unset for an email.
		**  2) expunge -- provides the sequence number for an email that has been deleted.
		**  3) exists -- reports the new number of messages in the currently selected mailbox.
		**  4) recent -- reports the new number of messages with the /RECENT flag set.
		**  5) raw -- reports an unanticipated response line that was not parsed by Chilkat. 
		**     This should be reported to support@chilkatoft.com
		** 
		** A sample showing all possible notifications (except for "raw") is shown below.
		** 
		**   <idle>
		**       <flags seqnum="59" uid="11876">
		**           <flag>\Deleted</flag>
		**           <flag>\Seen</flag>
		**       </flags>
		**       <flags seqnum="69" uid="11889">
		**           <flag>\Seen</flag>
		**       </flags>
		**       <expunge>58</expunge>
		**       <expunge>58</expunge>
		**       <expunge>67</expunge>
		**       <exists>115</exists>
		**       <recent>0</recent>
		**   </idle>
		**
		** If no updates have been received, the returned XML string has the following format, 
		** as shown below. The
		** 
		**   <idle></idle>
		** 
		** NOTE:Once IdleStart has been called, this method can and should 
		** be called frequently to see if any updates have arrived. 
		** This is NOT the same as polling the IMAP server 
		** because it does not send any requests to the IMAP server. 
		** It simply checks to see if any messages (i.e. updates) 
		** from the IMAP server are available and waiting to be read.
		** 
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tiTimeoutMs AS Integer
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_IMAP_COM_CALL, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		loException AS Exception, lcXMLUpdates AS Character
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		lcXMLUpdates = []
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 26
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        lcXMLUpdates = m.loChilkatObject.IdleCheck(m.tiTimeoutMs)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcXMLUpdates
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_IMAP_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
		
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE idlecheckasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.26. Creates an asynchronous task to call the IdleCheck method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            IdleCheckAsync
		* Purpose:           Creates an asynchronous task to call the 
		*                    IdleCheck method with the arguments provided.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tiTimeoutMs, the millisecond time out value.
		* Returns:           Chilkat Task Object, or NULL
		* Date Added:        06/22/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Creates an asynchronous task to call the IdleCheck method with the arguments provided. 
		** (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		** Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. 
		** Accessing and updating UI elements existing in the main thread may require special considerations.
		**
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		** 
		
		LPARAMETERS tiTimeoutMs AS Integer
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_IMAP_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		loChilkatTask AS CHILKAT_TASK_COM_CALL
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, m.loChilkatTask
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 52 && 26
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        loChilkatTask = m.loChilkatObject.IdleCheckAsync(m.tiTimeoutMs)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		  
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.loChilkatTask
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_IMAP_COM_CALL)
		  loChilkatTask = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_TASK_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
		
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE idledone		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.26. Sends a command to the IMAP server to stop receiving real-time updates. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            IdleDone
		* Purpose:           Sends a command to the IMAP server to stop receiving real-time updates.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		* Date Added:        06/22/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.26
		**
		** Sends a command to the IMAP server to stop receiving real-time updates.
		**
		** Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		**
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_IMAP_COM_CALL, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		loException AS Exception, liReturn AS Integer, luReturn AS Unknown
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 26
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        STORE m.loChilkatObject.IdleDone() TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		  luReturn = .BitToLogical(m.liReturn)
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.luReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_IMAP_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
		
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE idledoneasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.26. Creates an asynchronous task to call the IdleDone method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*==============================================================================
