	PROCEDURE sshopentunnel		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Connects to an SSH server and creates a tunnel for IMAP. The sshHostname is the hostname (or IP address) of the SSH server. The sshPort is typically 22, which is the standard SSH port number.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            SSHOpenTunnel
		* Purpose:           Connects to an SSH server and creates a tunnel for IMAP.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcSSHHostName -- the SSH Host name.
		*                    tiPort -- the SSH Port number.
		* Returns:           Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		* Date Added:        06/22/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.50
		**
		** Connects to an SSH server and creates a tunnel for IMAP. 
		** The sshHostname is the hostname (or IP address) of the SSH server. 
		** The sshPort is typically 22, which is the standard SSH port number.
		**
		** An SSH tunneling (port forwarding) session always begins by 
		** first calling SshOpenTunnel to connect to the SSH server, 
		** followed by calling either SshAuthenticatePw or SshAuthenticatePk to authenticate. 
		** Your program would then call Connect to connect with the IMAP server 
		** (via the SSH tunnel) and then Login to authenticate with the IMAP server.
		**
		** Note: Once the SSH tunnel is setup by calling SshOpenTunnel and SshAuthenticatePw 
		** (or SshAuthenticatePk), all underlying communcations with the IMAP server 
		** use the SSH tunnel. No changes in programming are required 
		** other than making two initial calls to setup the tunnel.
		**
		** Important: When reporting problems, please send the full contents 
		** of the LastErrorText property to support@chilkatsoft.com.
		** 
		** Fixed for Version 61: Fixed TLS connection issue 
		** with some cipher suites on Big Endian machines.
		**
		** Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		** 
		
		LPARAMETERS tcSSHHostName AS Character, tiPort AS Integer
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_IMAP_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		liReturn AS Integer, luReturn AS Unknown 
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn, m.liIntroducedInBuild
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 50
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        STORE m.loChilkatObject.SSHOpenTunnel(m.tcSSHHostName, m.tiPort) ;
		        TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		  luReturn = .BitToLogical(m.liReturn)
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.luReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_IMAP_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
		
	ENDPROC

