	PROCEDURE fullrequestmultipart		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. Sends a complete multipart REST request (header + multipart body) and receives the full response. It is assumed that the response body is a string (such as JSON or XML). The response body is returned.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            FullRequestMultiPart
		* Purpose:           Sends a complete multipart REST request and receives the full response.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcHTTPVerb, the header name.
		*                    tcURLPath, the URL path within the domain.
		* Returns:           The response body
		* Date Added:        06/07/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.58
		**
		** Sends a complete multipart REST request (header + multipart body) 
		** and receives the full response. It is assumed that the response body is a string 
		** (such as JSON or XML). The response body is returned.
		** 
		** This method is the equivalent of making the following calls in sequence: 
		** SendReqMultipart, ReadResponseHeader, ReadRespBodyString.
		** 
		** Note: If your application wishes to receive percent-done callbacks, 
		** make sure the PercentDoneOnSend property is set to indicate 
		** whether percent-done applies to sending or receiving.
		** 
		** IMPORTANT: The uriPath argument should be just the path part of the URL. 
		** It is NOT the full URL. 
		** If your URL is "https://www.example.com/something/123?xyz=1", 
		** then the uriPath is "/something/123?xyz=1".
		**
		** Fix for version 78:  If connecting with auto-reconnect turned on, 
		** this method did not auto-restore the connection if the request was non-chunked.
		** 
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcHTTPVerb AS Character, tcURLPath AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_REST_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, llImplemented AS Logical, ;
		liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, lcResponseBody AS Character
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		lcResponseBody = []
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 58
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        lcResponseBody = ;
		        m.loChilkatObject.FullRequestMultiPart(m.tcHTTPVerb, m.tcURLPath)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcResponseBody
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_REST_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

