	PROCEDURE readresponseheader		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. Reads the HTTP response header. If the HTTP response includes a body, then the application must call the desired method to read the response body.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ReadRespBodyHeader
		* Purpose:           Reads the HTTP response header.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           The body header
		* Date Added:        06/07/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.58
		**
		** Reads the HTTP response header. If the HTTP response includes a body, 
		** then the application must call the desired method to read the response body. 
		** Otherwise, the HTTP request / response is finished after reading the response header 
		** (such as for a GET request). The contents of the response header 
		** are available in various properties and methods.
		** 
		** The HTTP response status code is returned (such as 200 for a typical success response). 
		** If an error occurred such that no response was received, then a value of -1 is returned.
		**
		** Fix for version 83: Fixed crash bug in method (a rare situation)
		**
		** Fix for version 11.6.0: In the manual request/response pattern 
		** (explicit steps rather than a FullRequest* method), 
		** the response body was not readable after ReadResponseHeader: 
		** the object incorrectly moved to an idle state for *all* verbs, 
		** so every body-read call failed with “not in the state to read the response body.” 
		** Fixed — after a valid status code, the object now correctly enters the body-reading state 
		** for any request that can have a body. A HEAD request (no body) 
		** still correctly stops after the header. FullRequest* methods were never affected.
		**
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_REST_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, llImplemented AS Logical, ;
		liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, lcResponseHeader AS Character
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		lcResponseHeader = []
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 58
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        lcResponseHeader = m.loChilkatObject.ReadRespBodyHeader()
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcResponseHeader
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_REST_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE readresponseheaderasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReadResponseHeader method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ReadResponseHeaderAsync
		* Purpose:           Creates an asynchronous task to call the 
		*                    ReadResponseHeader method with the arguments provided.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
