		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.58
		**
		** Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReadResponseHeader method with the arguments provided. 
		** (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		**
		** Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. 
		** Accessing and updating UI elements existing in the main thread 
		** may require special considerations.
		**
		** Fix for version 83: Fixed crash bug in method (a rare situation)
		**
		** Fix for version 11.6.0: In the manual request/response pattern 
		** (explicit steps rather than a FullRequest* method), 
		** the response body was not readable after ReadResponseHeader: 
		** the object incorrectly moved to an idle state for all verbs, 
		** so every body-read call failed with “not in the state to read the response body.” 
		** Fixed — after a valid status code, the object now correctly enters the body-reading state 
		** for any request that can have a body. A HEAD request (no body) 
		** still correctly stops after the header. FullRequest* methods were never affected.
		**
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_REST_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, llImplemented AS Logical, ;
		liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, loChilkatTask AS CHILKAT_TASK_COM_CALL
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, m.loChilkatTask 
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 58
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        loChilkatTask = m.loChilkatObject.ReadResponseHeaderAsync()
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.loChilkatTask
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
