	PROCEDURE establishcontext		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.87. Creates an Application Context to the PC/SC Resource Manager. This must be the first WinSCard function called in a PC/SC application. The scope can be "user" or "system".
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            EstablishContext
		* Purpose:           Creates an Application Context to the PC/SC Resource Manager.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcScope, the scope value.
		* Returns:           Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		* Date Added:        07/10/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.50.87
		**
		** Creates an Application Context to the PC/SC Resource Manager. 
		** This must be the first WinSCard function called in a PC/SC application. 
		** The scope can be "user" or "system". 
		** After calling, this object will have context and all other methods 
		** will use the established context. The "Context" property will hold the value 
		** "user" or "system" if context was established, 
		** or will be empty if no context was established.
		** 
		** Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcScope AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SCARD_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
