		LOCAL liStackLevel AS Integer, lcMethod AS Character, ;
		lcProperty AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_Stack[1, 1], la_IntroducedInBuild[3, 1]
		
		STORE [] TO m.lcMethod, m.lcProperty, m.lcMethodToCall, m.la_Stack, m.la_IntroducedInBuild
		
		liStackLevel = ASTACKINFO(la_Stack)
		
		lcMethod = m.la_Stack(m.liStackLevel, 3)
		lcMethod = PROPER(SUBSTRC(m.lcMethod, AT_C([.], m.lcMethod) + 1))
		lcProperty = LEFTC(m.lcMethod, LENC(m.lcMethod) - 7)
		
		lcMethodToCall = [Long]
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 9
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 5
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 49
		
		THIS.CallAccessObject(m.lcMethodToCall, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN EVALUATE([THIS.] + m.lcProperty)
		
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE bandwidththrottleup_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the BandwidthThrottleUp property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            BandwidthThrottleUp_Assign
		* Purpose:           Assign method used to hold a reference to the BandwidthThrottleUp property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tiValue, integer value 
		*                    used to hold a reference to the BandwidthThrottleUp property.
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        04/19/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		LPARAMETERS tiValue AS Integer
		
		LOCAL lcValidationMethod AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_IntroducedInBuild[3, 1]
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 9
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 5
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 49
		
		lcValidationMethod = []
		lcMethodToCall = [Long]
		
		THIS.CallAssignObject(m.tiValue, m.lcMethodToCall, m.lcValidationMethod, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE chilkatchangelog
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ChilkatChangeLog
		* Purpose:           Documentation method used to hold 
		*                    the Chilkat class changes per release version.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        02/03/2024
		*==============================================================================
		
		#IF .F.
		
		TEXT
		
		** Version 11.5.0
		
		  In Chilkat classes having SOCKS proxy properties, added the ability 
		  for a SOCKS destination host to be an IPv6 address.
		
		  Added the boolean EnableSecrets property to several Chilkat classes. When set to true, 
		  it provides the ability to pass a secret name rather than the actual value of a sensitive item. 
		  For example, a password for Ftp2, or a client_secret for OAuth2 client credentials. 
		  The value (such as client_secret) would’ve been previously stored via the Chilkat.Secrets API 
		  to the local manager, which on Windows is the Window Credentials Manager, 
		  and on Apple is the Apple Keychain.
		
		  Secrets Conceptual Overview — See Chilkat Secrets API for a refresher on the Secrets API.
		
		  When EnableSecrets is true, certain Chilkat methods and properties are secrets-aware. 
		  A passed-in value having the format “!!part1|part2|part3|part4” where a secret name 
		  is specified by providing 2 to 4 parts will get auto-resolved by looking up the secret 
		  in the local manager and found value will be used instead. 
		  This makes it easier for applications to avoid embedding sensitive information in source code.
		  For more information, see Chilkat EnableSecrets
		  
		  Fixed a problem with downloading files from a server that did not behave well 
		  according to the SFTP protocol specification. 
		  (In other words, a workaround for a badly behaving server.)
		
		** Version 11.4.0
		
		  GetHostKeyFP — Fixed: There was a problem in the coalescing of SSH curve names 
		  to the standard curve names used by OpenSSH in the creation of the blob 
		  that is hashed to create the fingerprint. Also, the trailing “=” chars are now automatically stripped. 
		  (Stripping the “=” padding in SSH SHA256 fingerprints 
		  is now the de-facto standard behavior across SSH implementations.)
		
		  UncommonOptions(“+chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com”) — Fixed: Explicitly allowing 
		  the chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com cipher algorithm was not working.
		
		** Version 11.2.0
		
		  Many classes have a GetLastJsonData method. This method was fixed 
		  to avoid clearing the contents of the LastErrorText.
		
		** Version 11.1.0
		
		   Fixed the Failed to parse FXP message data length error that sometimes occurred 
		   only with the SSH-2.0-AWS_SFTP_1.2 server.
		
		** Version 11.0.0
		
		  Removed the UnlockComponent method.
		
		  Removed the SyncedFiles property.
		
		  Added the GetLastJsonData, ReadDirListing and ReadDirListingAsync methods.
		
		  Decremented the GetFileCreateDt, GetFileCreateDtAsync, 
		  GetFileLastAccessDt, GetFileLastAccessDtAsync, GetFileLastModifiedDt, GetFileLastModifiedDtAsync,
		  LastJsonData, ReadDir and ReadDirAsync methods.
		
		** Version 10.0.0
		
		  Added the GetSyncedFiles method.
		
		** Version 99
		
		  The default client identifier for SSH connections is changed to 
		  “SSH-2.0-Chilkat_{version}, where {version} is a string such as “9.5.0.99”.  
		
		  The AuthFailReason was not getting set when authentication failed. This is fixed.
		
		  In some cases, Chilkat failed to establish connections trying to use aes-gcm. 
		  This was fixed. (It was not common.)
		
		  Added the SetAllowedAlgorithms method. This allows an application to explicitly set 
		  the set of allowed connection algorithms (cipher, mac, key exchange, etc.). 
		  Note: It’s best to NOT explicitly set the algorithms. Chilkat already prioritizes algorithms 
		  according to security and other factors. By explicitly setting algorithms, 
		  you may be creating a vulnerability (such as w/ the SSH Terrapin attack), 
		  or you might create a situation where the client and server cannot establish a connection 
		  because no mutually supported algorithms are possible.
		
		** Version 97
		
		  Mitigated vulnerability to the Terrapin attack.
		  See https://cknotes.com/chilkat-v9-5-0-97-mitigates-vulnerability-to-the-ssh-terrapin-attack/
		
		** Version 96
		
		  Fixed possible RSA public key authentication problem for the Azure SSH server.
		
		** Version 95
		
		  The HostKeyFingerprint property will now correctly return the ssh-ed25519 fingerprint,
		  such as “ssh-ed25519 256 da:7b:ce:4f:d7:56:5e:11:a1:a0:fc:74:dd:4d:50:da”,
		  for cases when an Ed25519 host key is used in the connection.
		
		  Fixed rare connection problem with certain SSH servers.
		
		  Added support for SHA224 in all places where a hash algorithm might be specified.
		
		  Fixed uncommon public-key authentication problems where the client and server
		  are not agreeing on the choice of userauth key algorithm if RSA is used
		  and the server supports the rsa-sha2-256 and rsa-sha2-512 host key algorithms.
		
		** Version 94
		
		  Fixed problem where Chilkat may not have honored the max_packet_size
		  limit imposed by some servers for SFTP uploads.
		
		  Fixed login/authentication problems encountered w/ some SSH servers
		  when password + private key authentication is required (AuthenticatePwPk).
		
		  The internal name for curve25519-sha256@libssh.org was changed by newer servers to curve25519-sha256.
		  Chilkat is now modified to automatically work with both old or new servers.
		
		** Version 93
		
		  Fixed problems with “Window size is running low” when communicating with old SSH-2.0-CoreFTP-0.3.2 servers.
		
		** Version 92
		
		  Added the GetHostKeyFP method to both Ssh and SFtp.
		
		  Updated the SetOwnerAndGroup method to correctly handle decimal string owner/group values for SFTP v3 servers.
		
		** Version 91
		
		  Fixed: SyncTreeUpload did not pay attention to the SyncMustMatchDir property.
		
		  Fixed the HostKeyFingerprint property for cases where the SSH server’s host key is ED25519.
		
		** Version 90
		
		  Added support for new algorithms:
		  Key Exchange: diffie-hellman-group14-sha256, diffie-hellman-group16-sha512, diffie-hellman-group18-sha512
		  Host Key: rsa-sha2-256, rsa-sha2-512
		
		  Updated to make Chilkat work better with certain problematic (older) servers.
		
		** Version 88
		
		  Added the ability to authenticate with keyboard authentication in the same way as for SSH.
		  The StartKeyboardAuth and ContinueKeyboardAuth methods are added,
		  and the UserAuthBanner property is added.
		
		  Added support for the “ecdsa-sha2-nistp521” and “ecdsa-sha2-nistp384” host key algorithms.
		
		** Version 87
		
		  Added support for the ecdh-sha2-nistp384 and ecdh-sha2-nistp521 key exchange algorithms.
		  This fixed the “Unable to agree upon host key algorithm.” seen with a few SSH servers.
		
		  Added the “NoHomeAutoFix” keyword to UncommonOptions. Programmers often mistakenly pass
		  a remote path beginning with “/” when they really want a path relative to their SSH account HOME directory.
		  If SFTP encounters a “permission denied” error, it will internally retry using “./”
		  to make the path relative to HOME, unless the “NoHomeAutoFix” keyword is present in UncommonOptions.  
		
		** Version 85
		
		  Added the LastStatusCode and LastStatusMessage properties.
		
		** Version 83
		
		  Improved support for ECDSA certs.
		
		  Improved support for Ed25519 private keys.
		
		  (Fixed) The ReadFileBytes64 method, if reading past the end of the file,
		  did not cause the Eof(handle) function to subsequently return True.
		
		** Version 82
		
		  Default for EnableCompression is changed to false because some servers fail with compression enabled,
		  and in other cases performance is slower with compression enabled.
		  (Yet in other cases, it’s possible that performance is better with compression enabled —
		  it entirely has to do with the compressibility of the data being sent/received.)
		
		** Version 79
		
		  Added the LastJsonData method. This provides the ability
		  to get additional information for some method calls.
		  For example, after calling Connect the LastJsonData will list
		  the algorithms used to establish the SSH connection.
		  Also, authentication failure reason information is available for each of the Authenticate* methods.
		
		** Version 77
		
		  The SFtp.SyncedFiles property contains a list of files (one per line)
		  uploaded or downloaded in the last call to SyncTreeUpload or SyncTreeDownload.
		  For SyncTreeDownload, this list can also include local directories that were created.
		  Starting in v9.5.0.77, the local directory entries will end with “/” to signify a directory.
		
		  Fixed a problem in InitializedSftp for some servers.
		  The InitializeSftp method would timeout and fail.
		  It was caused when a server sent unanticipated “extended data”,
		  which was incorrectly processed as a response to a different message.
		
		  Found and fixed a rare case where corrupt incoming compressed data caused infinite logging to LastErrorText.
		
		  Added new methods: ReadFileBd, WriteFileBd.
		
		** Version 76
		
		  Added the SyncMustMatchDir and SyncMustNotMatchDir properties.
		
		  If preserving the last-mod date/time is the only error for the UploadFileByName,
		  then the method will still return success (rather than failure).
		
		** Version 75
		
		  Fixed the LastReadNumBytes method which always returned 0.
		
		  Downloading to a file (DownloadFileByName) will check to see if the local target file already exists.
		  If so, it will try to delete it prior to downloading. If it is not possible to delete,
		  then the DownloadFileByName will return failure before trying to download the file.
		
		** Version 73
		
		  Fixed: The SyncTreeDownload method was not firing the DownloadRate callback.
		
		  Fixed problems with IPv6 addresses when using SOCKS5 proxies.
		
		  Fixed a host key signature verification failure for certain situations.
		
		  Added the UncommonOptions property, which will be a place to specify
		  future unforeseen workarounds that may be required for particular SSH servers (old or new).
		
		** Version 71
		
		  Added the XferByteCount property to allow for applications to access
		  the current upload or download transfer byte count for ongoing asynchronous transfers.
		
		  Added the ServerIdentifier property.
		
		  Added AuthenticateSecPw and AuthenticateSecPwPk methods.
		
		  Added the following methods: SymLink,HardLink, ReadLink, and FSync.
		
		** Version 70
		
		  Added internal re-try functionality to cope with various situations
		  for IPv4-only and IPv6-only networks.
		
		** Version 69
		
		  In rare cases, when aborting a high-speed download, the LastErrorText would become filled
		  with a repeated message “Socket recv aborted by application.”. This was fixed.
		
		  Added a workaround for a glitch in the “SSH-2.0-Connect:Enterprise_UNIX_2.4.04 Build 00” SSH server.
		
		  Fixed (rare) problem such that on some downloads, an unexpected message is received
		  from the server after the download is completed and when closing the handle.
		
		** Version 67
		
		  Added the FileExists method.
		  
		  Fixed the ReadFileBytes method for the case where one tries
		  to read more bytes than what exists in the remote file.
		
		** Version 66
		
		  Added SFtp.SendIgnore method.
		
		  Improved performance for SFTP, FTP, and HTTP data transfers.
		
		** Version 65
		
		  ActiveX LastStringResultLen property incorrectly returned the size of the string in bytes (utf-16)
		  rather than in number of characters. This is fixed to return the number of characters.
		  (Note: this is a property that only exists in ActiveX classes, and is only useful
		  for certain programming languages such as SQL Server to help programs determine
		  if temp tables are required.)
		
		** Version 62
		
		  Note: One use of BinData and StringBuilder is in use of new methods ending in “Sb” and “Bd”.
		  These methods are for returning or passing text or binary data, especially large amounts of text or data.
		  For example, imagine one Chilkat method is used to retrieve a large amount of data,
		  and then that data is passed to another Chilkat method. A large waste of time and memory is consumed
		  in returning the string (or binary bytes) to the programming language,
		  and then immediately passing it back to Chilkat.
		  If it is .NET, then the data must be marshaled from unmanaged to managed, and then,
		  to pass back to Chilkat it is marshaled from managed to unmanaged.
		  The same applies when using the ActiveX (with BSTR’s and Variants).
		  By retrieving results directly into a BinData or StringBuilder,
		  and then passing the data by passing the object, the data stays on the native side.
		  For example, the new Rest.ReadRespSb method reads the REST response directly in to a StringBuilder.
		  If it is JSON, this can be loaded directly into a JsonObject via the JsonObject.LoadSb.
		  In the future, new “Sb” and “Bd” methods will be added in places
		  where large amounts of data are likely to be encountered.
		  This will create pathways allowing data to stay native as much as possible.
		  Version 9.5.0.62 adds the following initial set of Sb/Bd methods:
		
		    JsonObject.LoadSb
		    JsonObject.EmitSb
		    Xml.LoadSb
		    Xml.GetXmlSb
		
		    Email.GetMimeBd
		    Email.GetMimeSb
		    Email.SetFromMimeSb
		    Email.SetFromMimeBd
		
		    Mime.LoadMimeSb
		    Mime.LoadMimeBd
		    Mime.GetMimeSb
		    Mime.GetMimeBd
		    MailMan.RenderToMimeBd
		    MailMan.RenderToMimeSb
		    Rest.FullRequestSb
		    Rest.ReadRespSb
		    Rest.SendReqSb
		    Rest.SetMultipartBodySb
		    Rest.AddQueryParam
		    Rest.ReadRespBd
		    Rest.SendReqBd
		    Rest.SetMultipartBodyBd
		    Imap.FetchAttachmentSb
		    Imap.FetchAttachmentBd
		    Imap.AppendMimeWithFlagsSb
		    SFtp.UploadSb
		    SFtp.DownloadSb
		    SFtp.UploadBd
		    SFtp.DownloadBd
		    Ftp2.GetFileSb
		    Ftp2.GetFileBd
		
		    Ftp2.PutFileSb
		    Ftp2.PutFileBd
		
		** Version 61
		
		  The ReadFileBytes method could hang for duration of IdleTimeoutMs
		  if file size was smaller than number of bytes requested. This was fixed.
		
		** Version 59
		
		  Added the hmac-sha1-96 algorithm to what is supported in the internal SSH connection protocol.
		
		  Worked around problems with the Devart SSH server.
		
		** Version 58
		
		  The Windows logged-on username is no longer automatically logged at the top of every LastErrorText.
		  (This was originally done to help w/ support issues so tht Chilkat might notice if the program runs
		  in the context of a Service or IIS, which could be a clue to the cause of certain problems.)
		
		  Fixed problems with certain SSH/SFTP servers where certain downloads would hang.
		
		  Added the SyncDirectives property.
		
		  Added the AbortCurrent property to classes that can have event callbacks.
		
		** Version 56
		
		  Added the EnableCompression property. An old server was discovered that did not correctly handle compression.
		  Chilkat automatically disables compression when the problematic servers are encountered,
		  but if undiscovered old servers have the same problem, this property can be set to work around the problem.
		
		  Fixed: The ReadDirMustMatch and ReadDirMustNotMatch properties did not work correctly.
		
		** Version 55
		
		  The ResumeUploadFileByName method was improved. When the remote file does not already exist,
		  then Chilkat will open with writeOnly/createTruncate instead of readWrite/openOrCreate.
		  This avoids problems with some servers. (On most servers, the original behavior posed no problem.)
		
		** Version 54
		
		  Fixed rarely encountered flow problems with a particular SSH server.
		
		** Version 53
		
		  The LastStringResultLen property is added to each Chilkat class.
		  This is helpful for certain programming languages such as DataFlex or SQL Server
		  where the size of the string returned may need to be known before using it.
		  Each Chilkat ActiveX object has its own LastStringResult and LastStringResultLen properties.
		  The KeepStringResult is a property of Chilkat.Global only.
		  (It may be confusing that Chilkat.Global also has a LastStringResult property —
		  but this is just like any other object.)
		
		  Therefore, your code would set Global.KeepStringResult once at the beginning of your code.
		
		  Let’s say you have an HttpResult object, and you want the BodyQP.
		  You would access the BodyQP, but ignore the string returned.
		  Then examine the HttpResult.LastStringResultLen, adjust your max string length (in DataFlex) if necessary,
		  and then get the cached string from HttpResult.LastStringResult.
		
		** Version 52
		
		  Added asynchronous functionality for all qualifying methods
		  across all programming languages, operating systems, and architectures.
		  Each Chilkat method that can potentially be time-consuming or involve network communications,
		  now has a corresponding asynchronous version of the method with the name ending in “Async”.
		
		  Added the LastMethodSuccess property.
		
		  Added the AuthFailReason property.
		
		** Version 51
		
		  Applies to any Chilkat class with HTTP proxy capabilities:
		  Fixed issues related to using HTTP proxes for non-HTTP protocols where SSL/TLS is not used.
		
		  Added the SyncedFiles property to allow applications to get a list of files
		  that were transferred during the last directory synchronization method call.
		
		** Version 50
		
		  Fixed certain problems relating to the download of large files for some types of SSH servers.
		
		** Version 49
		
		  Added the BandwidthThrottleUp/Down properties to HTTP, SFTP, Socket, and Upload.
		
		  Added PercentDoneScale property to FTP2, Http, Tar, Zip, SFtp, MailMan, Imap, Upload.
		
		  Non-SSL/TLS HTTP proxy connections were trying to use CONNECT.
		
		  Fixed mode 99 for the SyncDownloadTree method.
		
		  Fixed the SyncDownloadTree method regarding certain decisions about whether to download newer files.
		
		  The internal automatic retry from EHLO to HELO did not work.
		  If the SMTP server did not support EHLO, then EHLO
		  was mistakenly tried a 2nd time instead of HELO.
		
		** Version 46
		
		  Added the CheckConnection method, which returns true if the underlying TCP socket is connected to the server.
		
		** Version 41
		
		  Improved SFTP behavior when the PreserveDate property is turned on.
		  Some SSH/SFTP servers did not allow for setting the last-mod date/time
		  using an open file handle until the file is actually closed.
		  Internally, Chilkat automatically handles this problem
		  by setting the last-mod date/time after the file is closed using the remote file path.
		
		** Version 40
		
		  The PreserveDate property now affects both uploads and downloads.
		  Starting in v9.5.0.40, the UploadFileByName method
		  will preserve the last-mod date/time for the file that is uploaded
		  Note: The SyncTreeUpload/Download methods already preserve the last-mod date/times
		  regardless of the PreserveDate property setting.
		
		** Version 27
		
		  Added support for the hmac-sha2-512, hmac-sha2-256, hmac-ripemd160 algorithms to SSH/SFTP internal transport.
		
		** Version 23
		
		  A minor fix to SFtp.ResumeDownloadFileByName: 
		  If the complete file already exists locally such that nothing needed to be downloaded,
		  the method incorrectly returned a failed status. This has been fixed.
		
		ENDTEXT
		
		#ENDIF .F.
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE clearaccumulatebuffer		&& Clears the contents of the AccumulateBuffer property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClearAccumulateBuffer
		* Purpose:           Clears the contents of the AccumulateBuffer property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        04/20/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Clears the contents of the AccumulateBuffer property.
		**
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SFTP_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      m.loChilkatObject.ClearAccumulateBuffer()
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SFTP_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE clearcache		&& Clears the internal file attribute cache. (Please refer to the EnableCache property for more information about the file attribute cache.)
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClearCache
		* Purpose:           Clears the internal file attribute cache.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        04/20/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Clears the internal file attribute cache. ;
		** (Please refer to the EnableCache property for more information about the file attribute cache.)
		**
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SFTP_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      m.loChilkatObject.ClearCache()
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SFTP_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE clearsessionlog		&& Clears the contents of the SessionLog property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClearSessionLog
		* Purpose:           Clears the contents of the SessionLog property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        04/20/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Clears the contents of the SessionLog property.
		**
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SFTP_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      m.loChilkatObject.ClearSessionLog()
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SFTP_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE clientidentifier_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SFTP ClientIdentifier property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClientIdentifier_Access
		* Purpose:           Access method used to retrieve 
		*                    the Chilkat SFTP ClientIdentifier property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           THIS.ClientIdentifier
		* Date Added:        04/19/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Specifies the SSH client-identification string sent when a connection is established. 
		** The default begins with SSH-2.0-Chilkat_ followed by the Chilkat version, for example SSH-2.0-Chilkat_11.6.0.
		** 
		** (This string is used to mimic PuTTY because some servers 
		** are known to disconnect from clients with unknown client identifiers.)
		**
		** Updated description in version 99:
		** The client-identifier string to be used when connecting to an SSH/SFTP server. 
		** Starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.99, the default is "SSH-2.0-Chilkat_" 
		** + the Chilkat version number, such as "SSH-2.0-Chilkat_9.5.0.99".
		**
		** Note: The client identifier should always begin with "SSH-2.0-". SSH servers may disconnect if it does not.
		**
		** Changed in version 99: The default client identifier for SSH connections 
		** is changed to “SSH-2.0-Chilkat_{version}, where {version} 
		** is a string such as “9.5.0.99”.
		**
		
		LOCAL liStackLevel AS Integer, lcMethod AS Character, lcProperty AS Character, ;
		lcMethodToCall AS Character, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_Stack[1, 1]
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liStackLevel, m.liIntroducedInBuild
		STORE [] TO m.lcMethod, m.lcProperty, m.lcMethodToCall, m.la_Stack
		
		liStackLevel = ASTACKINFO(la_Stack)
		
		lcMethod = m.la_Stack(m.liStackLevel, 3)
		lcMethod = PROPER(SUBSTRC(m.lcMethod, AT_C([.], m.lcMethod) + 1))
		lcProperty = LEFTC(m.lcMethod, LENC(m.lcMethod) - 7)
		
		lcMethodToCall = [String]
		
		THIS.CallAccessObject(m.lcMethodToCall, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN EVALUATE([THIS.] + m.lcProperty)
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE clientidentifier_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ClientIdentifier property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClientIdentifier_Assign
