	PROCEDURE realpath		&& This method can be used to have the server canonicalize any given path name to an absolute path. This is useful for converting path names containing ".." components or relative pathnames without a leading slash into absolute paths.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            RealPath
		* Purpose:           This method can be used to have the server canonicalize 
		*                    any given path name to an absolute path.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcOriginalPath -- the original path of the file.
		*                    tcComposePath -- the composed path to form the new path.
		* Returns:           The absolute path.
		* Date Added:        04/22/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** This method can be used to have the server canonicalize 
		** any given path name to an absolute path. 
		** This is useful for converting path names containing ".." components 
		** or relative pathnames without a leading slash into absolute paths. 
		** The absolute path is returned by this method.
		**
		** originalPath is the first component of the path which the client wishes 
		** resolved into a absolute canonical path. This may be the entire path.
		**
		** The composePath is a path which the client wishes the server 
		** to compose with the original path to form the new path. 
		** This field is optional and may be set to a zero-length string.
		**
		** The server will take the originalPath 
		** and apply the composePath as a modification to it. 
		** composePath may be relative to originalPath or may be an absolute path, 
		** in which case originalPath will be discarded. 
		** The composePath may be zero length.
		** 
		** Note: Servers running SFTP v4 and below do not support composePath.
		** 
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcOriginalPath AS Character, tcComposePath AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SFTP_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, lcAbsolutePath AS Character
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		lcAbsolutePath = []
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      lcAbsolutePath = m.loChilkatObject.RealPath(m.tcOriginalPath, m.tcComposePath)
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcAbsolutePath
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SFTP_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

