		*m: listenport_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ListenPort property.
		*m: loadtaskcaller		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.80. Loads the caller of the task's async method. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: loadtaskresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Loads the socket object from a completed asynchronous task. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: localipaddress_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket LocalIPAddress property.
		*m: localipaddress_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LocalIPAddress property.
		*m: localport_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket LocalPort property.
		*m: localport_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LocalPort property.
		*m: maxreadidlems_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket MaxReadIdleMs property.
		*m: maxreadidlems_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the MaxReadIdleMs property.
		*m: maxsendidlems_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket MaxSendIdleMs property.
		*m: maxsendidlems_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the MaxSendIdleMs property.
		*m: myipaddress_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket MyIPAddress property.
		*m: myipaddress_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the MyIPAddress property.
		*m: numbytesavailable_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket NumBytesAvailable property.
		*m: numbytesavailable_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the NumBytesAvailable property.
		*m: numreceivedclientcerts_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket NumReceivedClientCerts property.
		*m: numreceivedclientcerts_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the NumReceivedClientCerts property.
		*m: numsocketsinset_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket NumSocketsInSet property.
		*m: numsocketsinset_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the NumSocketsInSet property.
		*m: numsslacceptableclientcas_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket NumSSLAcceptableCAs property.
		*m: numsslacceptableclientcas_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the NumSSLAcceptableCAs property.
		*m: objectid_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket ObjectID property.
		*m: objectid_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ObjectID property.
		*m: percentdonescale_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket PercentDoneScale property.
		*m: percentdonescale_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the PercentDoneScale property.
		*m: polldataavailable		&& Check to see if data is available for reading on the socket. Returns 1 if data is waiting and 0 if no data is waiting to be read.
		*m: polldataavailableasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the PollDataAvailable method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: preferipv6_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket PreferIPV6 property.
		*m: preferipv6_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the PreferIPV6 property.
		*m: rcvbytespersec_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket RcvBytesPerSec property.
		*m: rcvbytespersec_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the RcvBytesPerSec property.
		*m: receivebd		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.65. Receives as much data as is immediately available on a connected TCP socket and appends the incoming data to binData. If no data is immediately available, it waits up to MaxReadIdleMs milliseconds for data to arrive.
		*m: receivebdasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.65. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveBd method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receivebdn		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.65. Reads exactly numBytes bytes from the connection. This method blocks until numBytes bytes are read or the read times out.
		*m: receivebdnasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.65. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveBdN method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receivebyte		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Receives a single byte. The received byte will be available in the ReceivedInt property. If bUnsigned is 1, then a value from 0 to 255 is returned in ReceivedInt.
		*m: receivebyteasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveByte method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receivebytes		&& Receives as much data as is immediately available on a connected TCP socket. If no data is immediately available, it waits up to MaxReadIdleMs milliseconds for data to arrive. Returns a zero-length byte array (as a Variant) on failure.
		*m: receivebytesasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveBytes method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receivebytesenc		&& The same as ReceiveBytes, except the bytes are returned in encoded string form according to encodingAlg.
		*m: receivebytesencasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveBytesENC method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receivebytesn		&& Reads exactly numBytes bytes from a connected SSL or non-SSL socket. This method blocks until numBytes bytes are read or the read times out. The timeout is specified by the MaxReadIdleMs property (in milliseconds).
		*m: receivebytesnasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveBytesN method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receivebytestofile		&& Receives as much data as is immediately available on a connected TCP socket. If no data is immediately available, it waits up to MaxReadIdleMs milliseconds for data to arrive. The received data is appended to the file specified by appendFilename.
		*m: receivebytestofileasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveBytesToFile method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread
		*m: receivecount		&& Receives a 4-byte signed integer and returns the value received. Returns -1 on error.
		*m: receivecountasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveCount method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receivedcount_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket ReceivedCount property.
		*m: receivedcount_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ReceivedCount property.
		*m: receivedint_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket ReceivedInt property.
		*m: receivedint_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ReceivedInt property.
		*m: receivefailreason_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket ReceiveFailReason property.
		*m: receivefailreason_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ReceiveFailReason property.
		*m: receiveint16		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Receives a 16-bit integer (2 bytes). The received integer will be available in the ReceivedInt property. Set bigEndian equal to 1 if the incoming 16-bit integer is in big-endian byte order.
		*m: receiveint16async		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveInt16 method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receiveint32		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Receives a 32-bit integer (4 bytes). The received integer will be available in the ReceivedInt property. Set bigEndian equal to 1 if the incoming 32-bit integer is in big-endian byte order.
		*m: receiveint32async		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveInt32 method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receivenbytesenc		&& The same as ReceiveBytesN, except the bytes are returned in encoded string form using the encoding specified by numBytes.
		*m: receivenbytesencasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveNBytesENC method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread
		*m: receivepacketsize_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket ReceivePacketSize property.
		*m: receivepacketsize_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ReceivePacketSize property.
		*m: receivesb		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.65. Receives as much data as is immediately available on the connection. If no data is immediately available, it waits up to MaxReadIdleMs milliseconds for data to arrive.
		*m: receivesbasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.65. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveSb method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread
		*m: receivestring		&& Receives as much data as is immediately available on a TCP/IP or SSL socket. If no data is immediately available, it waits up to MaxReadIdleMs milliseconds for data to arrive.
		*m: receivestringasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveString method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receivestringmaxn		&& Same as ReceiveString, but limits the amount of data returned to a maximum of maxByteCount bytes. (Receives as much data as is immediately available on the TCP/IP or SSL socket.
		*m: receivestringmaxnasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveStringMaxN method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receivestringuntilbyte		&& Receives bytes on a connected SSL or non-SSL socket until a specific 1-byte value is read. Returns a string containing all the bytes up to but excluding the lookForByte. Returns Nothing on failure
		*m: receivestringuntilbyteasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveStringUntilByte method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receivetocrlf		&& Reads text from the connected TCP/IP or SSL socket until a CRLF is received. Returns the text up to and including the CRLF. The incoming bytes are interpreted according to the charset specified by the StringCharset property. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: receivetocrlfasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveToCRLF method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receiveuntilbyte		&& Receives bytes on the TCP/IP or SSL socket until a specific 1-byte value is read. Returns all the bytes up to and including the lookForByte. Returns a zero-length byte array (as a Variant) on failure.
		*m: receiveuntilbyteasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveUntilByte method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receiveuntilbytebd		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.76. Receives bytes on the TCP/IP or SSL socket until a specific 1-byte value is read. Returns all the bytes up to and including the lookForByte. The received bytes are appended to bd.
		*m: receiveuntilbytebdasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveUntilByteBd method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: receiveuntilmatch		&& Reads text from the connected TCP/IP or SSL socket until a matching string (matchStr) is received. Returns the text up to and including the matching string.
		*m: receiveuntilmatchasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveUntilMatch method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread
		*m: receiveuntilmatchsb		&& Introduced in version 10.1.0. The same as ReceiveUntilMatch, but returns the received string appended to the contents of sb. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: receiveuntilmatchsbasync		&& Introduced in version 10.1.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReceiveUntilMatchSb method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: remoteipaddress_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket ReceiveIPAddress property.
		*m: remoteipaddress_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ReceiveIPAddress property.
		*m: remoteport_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket RemotePort property.
		*m: remoteport_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the RemotePort property.
		*m: requiresslcertverify_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket RequireSSLCertVerify property.
		*m: requiresslcertverify_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the RequireSSLCertVerify property.
		*m: resetperf		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.78. Resets the performance measurements for either receiving or sending. If rcvPerf is 1, then the receive performance monitoring is reset. If rcvPerf is 0, then the sending performance monitoring is reset.
		*m: selectforreading		&& Waits a maximum of timeoutMs milliseconds. If maxWaitMs = 0, then it is effectively a poll. Returns the number of sockets with data available for reading. If no sockets have data available for reading, then a value of 0 is returned.
		*m: selectforreadingasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SelectForReading method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: selectforwriting		&& Waits until it is known that data can be written to one or more sockets without it blocking.
		*m: selectforwritingasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SelectForWriting method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: selectorindex_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SelectorIndex property.
		*m: selectorindex_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SelectorIndex property.
		*m: selectorreadindex_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SelectorReadIndex property.
		*m: selectorreadindex_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SelectorReadIndex property.
		*m: selectorwriteindex_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SelectorWriteIndex property.
		*m: selectorwriteindex_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SelectorWriteIndex property.
		*m: sendbd		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.65. Sends bytes from binData over a connected SSL or non-SSL socket. If transmission halts for more than MaxSendIdleMs milliseconds, the send is aborted. This is a blocking (synchronous) method.
		*m: sendbdasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.65. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SendBd method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sendbyte		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Sends a single byte. The integer must have a value from 0 to 255. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: sendbyteasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SendByte method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread
		*m: sendbytes		&& Sends bytes over a connected SSL or non-SSL socket. If transmission halts for more than MaxSendIdleMs milliseconds, the send is aborted. This is a blocking (synchronous) method. It returns only after the bytes have been sent.
		*m: sendbytesasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SendBytes method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sendbytesenc		&& The same as SendBytes, except the bytes are provided in encoded string form as specified by encodingAlg.
		*m: sendbytesencasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SendBytesENC method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sendbytespersec_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SendBytesPerSec property.
		*m: sendbytespersec_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SendBytesPerSec property.
		*m: sendcount		&& Sends a 4-byte signed integer on the connection. The receiver may call ReceiveCount to receive the integer. The SendCount and ReceiveCount methods are handy for sending byte counts prior to sending data.
		*m: sendcountasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SendCount method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sendfailreason_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SendFailReason property.
		*m: sendfailreason_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SendFailReason property.
		*m: sendint16		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Sends a 16-bit integer (2 bytes). Set bigEndian equal to 1 to send the integer in big-endian byte order (this is the standard network byte order). Otherwise set bigEndian equal to 0 to send in little-endian byte order.
		*m: sendint16async		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SendInt16 method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread
		*m: sendint32		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Sends a 32-bit integer (4 bytes). Set bigEndian equal to 1 to send the integer in big-endian byte order (this is the standard network byte order). Otherwise set bigEndian equal to 0 to send in little-endian byte order.
		*m: sendint32async		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SendInt32 method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sendpacketsize_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SendPacketSize property.
		*m: sendpacketsize_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SendPacketSize property.
		*m: sendsb		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.65. Sends the contents of sb over the connection. If transmission halts for more than MaxSendIdleMs milliseconds, the send is aborted. The string is sent in the charset encoding specified by the StringCharset property.
		*m: sendsbasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.65. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SendSb method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sendstring		&& Sends a string over a connected SSL or non-SSL (TCP/IP) socket. If transmission halts for more than MaxSendIdleMs milliseconds, the send is aborted. The string is sent in the charset encoding specified by the StringCharset property.
		*m: sendstringasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the SendString method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread
		*m: sendwakeonlan		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.69. Sends a "Wake on Lan" magic packet to a computer. A Wake on Lan is a way to power on a computer remotely by sending a data packet known as a magic packet.
		*m: sendwakeonlan2		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.77. The same as SendWakeOnLan, but includes an additional argument to specify a SecureOn password. The password should be a hexidecimal string representing 4 or 6 bytes.
		*m: sessionlogencoding_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SessionLogEncoding property.
		*m: sessionlogencoding_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SessionLogEncoding property.
		*m: sessionlog_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SessionLog property.
		*m: sessionlog_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SessionLog property.
		*m: setsslclientcert		&& A client-side certificate for SSL/TLS connections is optional. It should be used only if the server demands it. This method allows the certificate to be specified using a certificate object. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setsslclientcertpem		&& A client-side certificate for SSL/TLS connections is optional. It should be used only if the server demands it. This method allows the certificate to be specified using a PEM file. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setsslclientcertpfx		&& A client-side certificate for SSL/TLS connections is optional. It should be used only if the server demands it. This method allows the certificate to be specified using a PFX file. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: sleepms		&& Convenience method to force the calling thread to sleep for a number of milliseconds.
		*m: snihostname_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SNIHostName property.
		*m: snihostname_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SNIHostName property.
		*m: sockshostname_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SOCKSHostName property.
		*m: sockshostname_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSHostName property.
		*m: sockspassword_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SOCKSPassword property.
		*m: sockspassword_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSPassword property.
		*m: socksport_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SOCKSPort property.
		*m: socksport_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSPort property.
		*m: socksusername_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SOCKSUserName property.
		*m: socksusername_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSUserName property.
		*m: socksversion_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SOCKSVersion property.
		*m: socksversion_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SOCKSVersion property.
		*m: sorcvbuf_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SoRcvBuf property.
		*m: sorcvbuf_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SoRcvBuf property.
		*m: soreuseaddr_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SoReuseAddr property.
		*m: soreuseaddr_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SoReuseAddr property.
		*m: sosndbuf_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SoSndBuf property.
		*m: sosndbuf_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SoSndBuf property.
		*m: sshauthenticatepk		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Authenticates with the SSH server using public-key authentication. The corresponding public key must have been installed on the SSH server for the sshLogin.
		*m: sshauthenticatepkasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SshAuthenticatePk method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: sshauthenticatepw		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Authenticates with the SSH server using a sshLogin and sshPassword. This method is only used for SSH tunneling.
		*m: sshauthenticatepwasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SshAuthenticatePw method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: sshclosetunnel		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Closes the SSH tunnel previously opened by SshOpenTunnel. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: sshclosetunnelasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SshCloseTunnel method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sshnewchannel		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Opens a new channel within an SSH tunnel and provides the socket connected to the specified destination host:port through SSH port forwarding in channel. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: sshnewchannelasync		&& Introduced in version 11.0.0. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SshNewChannel method with the arguments provided. Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: sshopenchannel		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Opens a new channel within an SSH tunnel. Returns the socket that is connected to the destination host:port through the SSH tunnel via port forwarding.
		*m: sshopenchannelasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SshOpenChannel method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sshopentunnel		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Connects to an SSH server and creates a tunnel for port forwarding. The sshHostname is the hostname (or IP address) of the SSH server. The sshPort is typically 22, which is the standard SSH port number.
		*m: sshopentunnelasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Creates an asynchronous task to call the SshOpenTunnel method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: sslallowedciphers_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SSLAllowedCiphers property.
		*m: sslallowedciphers_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSLAllowedCiphers property.
		*m: sslprotocol_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SSLProtocol property.
		*m: sslprotocol_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSLProtocol property.
		*m: ssl_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket SSL property.
		*m: ssl_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SSL property.
		*m: starttiming		&& Used in combination with the ElapsedSeconds property, which will contain the number of seconds since the last call to this method. (The StartTiming method and ElapsedSeconds property is provided for convenience.)
		*m: stringcharset_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket StringCharset property.
		*m: stringcharset_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the StringCharset property.
		*m: takeconnection		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.77. Takes the connection from sock. If the caller of this method had an open connection, then it will be closed. This method is different than the TakeSocket method because the caller does not become a "socket set".
		*m: takesocket		&& Takes ownership of the sock. sock is added to the internal set of connected sockets. The caller object is now effectively a "socket set", i.e. a collection of connected and/or listener sockets.
		*m: tcpnodelay_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket TCPNoDelay property.
		*m: tcpnodelay_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TCPNoDelay property.
		*m: tlsciphersuite_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket TLSCipherSuite property.
		*m: tlsciphersuite_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TLSCipherSuite property.
		*m: tlspinset_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket TLSPinSet property.
		*m: tlspinset_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TLSPinSet property.
		*m: tlsrenegotiate		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.55. Initiates a renegotiation of the TLS security parameters. This sends a ClientHello to re-do the TLS handshake to establish new TLS security params. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: tlsrenegotiateasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.55. Creates an asynchronous task to call the TlsRenegotiate method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: tlsversion_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket TLSVersion property.
		*m: tlsversion_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TLSVersion property.
		*m: uncommonoptions_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket UncommonOptions property.
		*m: uncommonoptions_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Uncommoptions property.
		*m: unlockcomponent		&& Undocumented method! Unlocks the component allowing for the full functionality to be used. An arbitrary string can be passed to initiate a fully-functional 30-day trial.
		*m: userdata_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket UserData property.
		*m: userdata_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UserData property.
		*m: usessh		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.55. Uses an existing SSH tunnel for the connection. This is an alternative way of establishing a socket connection through an SSH tunnel.
		*m: verboselogging_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket VerboseLogging property.
		*m: verboselogging_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the VerboseLogging property.
		*p: abortcurrent		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. When set to 1, causes the currently running method to abort. Methods that always finish quickly (i.e.have no length file operations or network communications) are not affected.
		*p: acceptfailreason		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. If a AcceptNextConnection method fails, this property can be checked to determine the reason for failure.
		*p: alpnprotocol		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.82. For TLS connections. Can be set to the name of an application layer protocol. This causes the ALPN extension to be added to the TLS ClientHello with the given ALPN protocol name.
		*p: asyncacceptfinished		&& Undocumented Property!  Set to true when an asynchronous accept operation completes.
		*p: asyncacceptlog		&& Undocumented property! Contains the last-error information for an asynchronous accept operation. This functionality is replaced by the new model for asynchronous programming introduced in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.
		*p: asyncacceptsuccess		&& Undocumented property! Set to true when an asynchronous accept operation completes and is successful. This functionality is replaced by the new model for asynchronous programming introduced in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.
		*p: asyncdnsfinished		&& Undocumented property! Set to true when an asynchronous DNS query completes. The success status is available in the AsyncDnsSuccess property. This functionality is replaced by the new model for asynchronous programming introduced in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.
		*p: asyncdnslog		&& Undocumented property? Contains the last-error information for an asynchronous DNS query. This functionality is replaced by the new model for asynchronous programming introduced in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.
		*p: asyncdnsresult		&& Undocumented property! The IP address of the last asynchronous DNS query completed. The IP address is in nnn.nnn.nnn.nnn string form. This functionality is replaced by the new model for asynchronous programming introduced in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.
		*p: asyncdnssuccess		&& Undocumented property! Set to true when an asynchronous DNS query completes and is successful. This functionality is replaced by the new model for asynchronous programming introduced in Chilkat v9.5.0.52..
		*p: asyncreceivedbytes		&& Undocumented function! Contains the data received in an asynchronous receive operation (when receiving bytes asynchronously). This functionality is replaced by the new model for asynchronous programming introduced in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.
		*p: asyncreceivedstring		&& Undocumented property! Contains the string received in an asynchronous receive operation (when receiving a string asynchronously). This functionality is replaced by the new model for asynchronous programming introduced in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.
		*p: asyncreceivefinished		&& Undocumented property! Set to true when an asynchronous receive operation completes. Once the  asynchronous receive has finished, the success/failure is available in the AsyncReceiveSuccess boolean property.
		*p: asyncreceivelog		&& Undocumented property! Contains the last-error information for an asynchronous receive operation. This functionality is replaced by the new model for asynchronous programming introduced in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.
		*p: asyncreceivesuccess		&& Undocumented property! Set to true when an asynchronous receive operation completes and is successful.  This functionality is replaced by the new model for asynchronous programming introduced in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.
		*p: asyncsendfinished		&& Undocumented property! Set to true when an asynchronous send operation completes. Once the asynchronous send has finished, the success/failure is available in the AsyncSendSuccess boolean property.
		*p: asyncsendlog		&& Undocumented property! Contains the last-error information for an asynchronous send operation. This functionality is replaced by the new model for asynchronous programming introduced in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.
		*p: asyncsendsuccess		&& Undocumented property! Set to true when an asynchronous send operation completes. Once the asynchronous send has finished, the success/failure is available in the AsyncSendSuccess boolean property.
		*p: bandwidththrottledown		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. If non-zero, limits (throttles) the receiving bandwidth to approximately this maximum number of bytes per second. The default value of this property is 0.
		*p: bandwidththrottleup		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. If non-zero, limits (throttles) the sending bandwidth to approximately this maximum number of bytes per second. The default value of this property is 0.
		*p: bigendian		&& Applies to the SendCount and ReceiveCount methods. If BigEndian is set to 1 (the default) then the 4-byte count is in big endian format. Otherwise it is little endian.
		*p: clientipaddress		&& The IP address to use for computers with multiple network interfaces or IP addresses.
		*p: clientport		&& Normally left at the default value of 0, in which case a unique port is assigned with a value between 1024 and 5000.
		*p: connectfailreason		&& If the Connect method fails, this property can be checked to determine the reason for failure.
		*p: debugconnectdelayms		&& Undocumented property! Used to simulate a long wait when connecting to a remote server.
		*p: debugdnsdelayms		&& Undocumented property! Used to simulate a long wait when doing a DNS lookup. If your application wishes to test for the handling of timeouts, you may set this value to a number of milliseconds greater than max-wait specified in the DnsLookup method cal
		*p: debuglogfilepath		&& If set to a file path, causes each Chilkat method or property call to automatically append it's LastErrorText to the specified log file.
		*p: elapsedseconds		&& Contains the number of seconds since the last call to StartTiming, otherwise contains 0. (The StartTiming method and ElapsedSeconds property is provided for convenience.)
		*p: heartbeatms		&& The number of milliseconds between periodic heartbeat callbacks for blocking socket operations (connect, accept, dns query, send, receive). Set this to 0 to disable heartbeat events. The default value is 1000 (i.e. 1 heartbeat callback per second).
		*p: httpproxyauthmethod		&& If an HTTP proxy requiring authentication is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy authentication method name. Valid choices are "Basic" or "NTLM".
		*p: httpproxydomain		&& The NTLM authentication domain (optional) if NTLM authentication is used.
		*p: httpproxyforhttp		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.70. If this connection is effectively used to send HTTP requests, then set this property to 1 when using an HTTP proxy. The default value of this property is 0.
		*p: httpproxyhostname		&& If an HTTP proxy is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy hostname or IPv4 address (in dotted decimal notation).
		*p: httpproxypassword		&& If an HTTP proxy requiring authentication is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy password.
		*p: httpproxyport		&& If an HTTP proxy is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy port number. (Two commonly used HTTP proxy ports are 8080 and 3128.)
		*p: httpproxyusername		&& If an HTTP proxy requiring authentication is to be used, set this property to the HTTP proxy login name.
		*p: isconnected		&& Returns 1 if the socket is connected. Otherwise returns 0. Note: In general, this property indicates the last known state of the socket.
		*p: keepalive		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Controls whether the SO_KEEPALIVE socket option is used for the underlying TCP/IP socket. The default value is 1.
		*p: keepsessionlog		&& Controls whether socket (or SSL) communications are logged to the SessionLog string property. To turn on session logging, set this property = 1, otherwise set to 0 (which is the default value).
		*p: lastbinaryresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The binary data returned by the last (binary data returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepBinaryResult is set to 1.
		*p: lasterrorhtml		&& Provides information in HTML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrortext		&& Provides information in plain-text format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrorxml		&& Provides information in XML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lastmethodfailed		&& 1 if the last method called on this object failed. This provides an easier (less confusing) way of determining whether a method such as ReceiveBytes succeeded or failed.
		*p: lastmethodsuccess		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Indicate whether the last method call succeeded or failed. A value of 1 indicates success, a value of 0 indicates failure. This property is automatically set for method calls.
		*p: laststringresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The string return value of the last (string returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepStringResult is set to 1.
		*p: laststringresultlen		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.53. The length, in characters, of the string contained in the LastStringResult property.
		*p: listenipv6		&& If set to 1, then a socket that listens for incoming connections (via the BindAndList and AcceptNextConnection method calls) will use IPv6 and not IPv4. The default value is 0 for IPv4.
		*p: listenport		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.59. The BindAndListen method will find a random unused port to listen on if you bind to port 0. This chosen listen port is available via this property.
		*p: localipaddress		&& The local IP address for a bound or connected socket.
		*p: localport		&& The local port for a bound or connected socket.
		*p: maxreadidlems		&& The maximum number of milliseconds to wait on a socket read operation while no additional data is forthcoming. To wait indefinitely, set this property to 0. The default value is 0.
		*p: maxsendidlems		&& The maximum number of milliseconds to wait for the socket to become writeable on a socket write operation. To wait indefinitely, set this property to 0. The default value is 0.
		*p: myipaddress		&& The local IP address of the local computer. For multi-homed computers (i.e. computers with multiple IP adapters) this property returns the default IP address.
		*p: numbytesavailable		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.94. Returns the number of bytes that are immediately available for reading on a connected socket. For TLS connections, this includes the overhead for TLS protocol records.
		*p: numreceivedclientcerts		&& If the socket is the server-side of an SSL/TLS connection, the property represents the number of client-side certificates received during the SSL/TLS handshake (i.e. connection process).
		*p: numsocketsinset		&& If this socket is a "socket set", then NumSocketsInSet returns the number of sockets contained in the set. A socket object can become a "socket set" by calling the TakeSocket method on one or more connected sockets.
		*p: numsslacceptableclientcas		&& If connected as an SSL/TLS client to an SSL/TLS server where the server requires a client-side certificate for authentication, then this property contains the number of acceptable certificate authorities sent by the server during handshake.
		*p: objectid		&& Each socket object is assigned a unique object ID. This ID is passed in event callbacks to allow your application to associate the event with the socket object.
		*p: percentdonescale		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. This property is only valid in programming environment and languages that allow for event callbacks. Sets the value to be defined as 100% complete for the purpose of PercentDone event callbacks
		*p: preferipv6		&& If 1, then use IPv6 over IPv4 when both are supported for a particular domain. The default value of this property is 0, which will choose IPv4 over IPv6.
		*p: rcvbytespersec		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.78. Returns the cumulative receive rate in bytes per second. The measurement includes the overhead bytes for protocols such as TLS or SSH tunneling
		*p: receivedcount		&& Any method that receives data will increase the value of this property by the number of bytes received. The application may reset this property to 0 at any point.
		*p: receivedint		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.50. Contains the last integer received via a call to ReceiveByte, ReceiveInt16, or ReceiveInt32.
		*p: receivefailreason		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. If a Receive method fails, this property can be checked to determine the reason for failure.
		*p: receivepacketsize		&& The number of bytes to receive at a time (internally). This setting has an effect on methods such as ReadBytes and ReadString where the number of bytes to read is not explicitly specified. The default value is 4096.
		*p: remoteipaddress		&& When a socket is connected, the remote IP address of the connected peer is available in this property.
		*p: remoteport		&& When a socket is connected, the remote port of the connected peer is available in this property.
		*p: requiresslcertverify		&& If 1, then the SSL/TLS client will verify the server's SSL certificate. The certificate is expired, or if the cert's signature is invalid, the connection is not allowed. The default value of this property is 0.
		*p: selectorindex		&& If this socket contains a collection of connected sockets (i.e. it is a "socket set") then method calls and property gets/sets are routed to the contained socket indicated by this property. Indexing begins at 0.
		*p: selectorreadindex		&& When SelectForReading returns a number greater than 0 indicating that 1 or more sockets are ready for reading, this property is used to select the socket in the "ready set" for reading.
		*p: selectorwriteindex		&& When SelectForWriting returns a number greater than 0 indicating that one or more sockets are ready for writing, this property is used to select the socket in the "ready set" for writing.
		*p: sendbytespersec		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.78. Returns the cumulative send rate in bytes per second. The measurement includes the overhead bytes for protocols such as TLS or SSH tunneling.
		*p: sendfailreason		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. If a Send method fails, this property can be checked to determine the reason for failure.
		*p: sendpacketsize		&& The number of bytes to send at a time (internally). This can also be though of as the "chunk size". If a large amount of data is to be sent, the data is sent in chunks equal to this size in bytes. The default value is 65535.
		*p: sessionlog		&& Contains a log of the bytes sent and received on this socket. The KeepSessionLog property must be set to 1 for logging to occur.
		*p: sessionlogencoding		&& Controls how the data is encoded in the SessionLog. Possible values are "esc" and "hex". The default value is "esc".
		*p: snihostname		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.82. Specifies the SNI hostname to be used in the TLS ClientHello. This property is only needed when the domain is specified via a dotted IP address and an SNI hostname is desired.
		*p: sockshostname		&& The SOCKS4/SOCKS5 hostname or IPv4 address (in dotted decimal notation). This property is only used if the SocksVersion property is set to 4 or 5).
		*p: sockspassword		&& The SOCKS5 password (if required). The SOCKS4 protocol does not include the use of a password, so this does not apply to SOCKS4.
		*p: socksport		&& The SOCKS4/SOCKS5 proxy port. The default value is 1080. This property only applies if a SOCKS proxy is used (if the SocksVersion property is set to 4 or 5).
		*p: socksusername		&& The SOCKS4/SOCKS5 proxy username. This property is only used if the SocksVersion property is set to 4 or 5).
		*p: socksversion		&& SocksVersion may be set to one of the following integer values: 0 - No SOCKS proxy is used. This is the default. 4 - Connect via a SOCKS4 proxy. 5 - Connect via a SOCKS5 proxy.
		*p: sorcvbuf		&& Sets the receive buffer size socket option. Normally, this property should be left unchanged. The default value is 4194304. This property can be increased if download performance seems slow. It is recommended to be a multiple of 4096.
		*p: soreuseaddr		&& Sets the SO_REUSEADDR socket option for a socket that will bind to a port and listen for incoming connections. The default value is 1, meaning that the SO_REUSEADDR socket option is set.
		*p: sosndbuf		&& Sets the send buffer size socket option. Normally, this property should be left unchanged. The default value is 262144. This property can be increased if upload performance seems slow. It is recommended to be a multiple of 4096.
		*p: ssl		&& Set this property to 1 if SSL/TLS is required for accepted connections (AcceptNextConnection). The default value is 0. Note: This property should have been more precisely named "RequireSslClient".
		*p: sslallowedciphers		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.48. Provides a means for setting a list of ciphers that are allowed for SSL/TLS connections. The default (empty string) indicates that all implemented ciphers are possible.
		*p: sslprotocol		&& Selects the secure protocol to be used for secure (SSL/TLS) connections.The default value is "default" which will choose the, which allows for the protocol to be selected dynamically at runtime based on the requirements of the server.
		*p: stringcharset		&& A charset such as "utf-8", "windows-1252", "Shift_JIS", "iso-8859-1", etc. Methods for sending and receiving strings will use this charset as the encoding. Strings sent on the socket are first converted (if necessary) to this encoding.
		*p: tcpnodelay		&& Controls whether the TCP_NODELAY socket option is used for the underlying TCP/IP socket. The default value is 0.
		*p: tlsciphersuite		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Contains the current or last negotiated TLS cipher suite. If no TLS connection has yet to be established, or if a connection as attempted and failed, then this will be empty.
		*p: tlspinset		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.55. Specifies a set of pins for Public Key Pinning for TLS connections. This property lists the expected SPKI fingerprints for the server certificates.
		*p: tlsversion		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.49. Contains the current or last negotiated TLS protocol version. If no TLS connection has yet to be established, or if a connection as attempted and failed, then this will be empty.
		*p: uncommonoptions		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.80. This is a catch-all property to be used for uncommon needs. This property defaults to the empty string and should typically remain empty. Can be set to a list of the following comma separated keywords:
		*p: userdata		&& Provides a way to store text data with the socket object. The UserData is purely for convenience and is not involved in the socket communications in any way. An application might use this property to keep extra information associated with the socket.
		*p: verboselogging		&& If set to 1, then the contents of LastErrorText (or LastErrorXml, or LastErrorHtml) may contain more verbose information. The default value is 0. Verbose logging should only be used for debugging.
	*</DefinedPropArrayMethod>

	*<PropValue>
