	HIDDEN PROCEDURE receivefailreason_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Socket ReceiveFailReason property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ReceiveFailReason_Access
		* Purpose:           Access method used to retrieve 
		*                    the Chilkat Socket ReceiveFailReason property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           THIS.ReceiveFailReason
		* Date Added:        05/28/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.49
		** 
		** If a Receive method fails, this property can be checked to determine the reason for failure.
		** 
		** Possible values are:
		** 
		** 0 = Success
		** 1 = An async receive operation is already in progress.
		** 2 = The socket is not connected, such as if it was never connected, 
		**     or if the connection was previously lost.
		** 3 = An unspecified internal failure, perhaps out-of-memory, caused the failure.
		** 4 = Invalid parameters were passed to the receive method call.
		** 5 = Timeout.  Data stopped arriving for more than the amount 
		**     of time specified by the MaxReadIdleMs property.
		** 6 = The receive was aborted by the application in an event callback.
		** 7 = The connection was lost -- the remote peer reset the connection. 
		**     (The connection was forcibly closed by the peer.)
		** 8 = An established connection was aborted by the software in your host machine. 
		**     (See https://www.chilkatsoft.com/p/p_299.asp )
		** 9 = An unspecified fatal socket error occurred (less common).
		** 10 = The connection was closed by the peer.
		** 
		
		LOCAL liStackLevel AS Integer, lcMethod AS Character, ;
		lcProperty AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_Stack[1, 1], la_IntroducedInBuild[3, 1]
		
		STORE [] TO m.lcMethod, m.lcProperty, m.lcMethodToCall, m.la_Stack, m.la_IntroducedInBuild
		
		liStackLevel = ASTACKINFO(la_Stack)
		
		lcMethod = m.la_Stack(m.liStackLevel, 3)
		lcMethod = PROPER(SUBSTRC(m.lcMethod, AT_C([.], m.lcMethod) + 1))
		lcProperty = LEFTC(m.lcMethod, LENC(m.lcMethod) - 7)
		
		lcMethodToCall = [LongReadOnly]
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 9
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 5
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 49
		
		THIS.CallAccessObject(m.lcMethodToCall, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN EVALUATE([THIS.] + m.lcProperty)
		
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE receivefailreason_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ReceiveFailReason property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ReceiveFailReason_Assign
		* Purpose:           Assign method used to hold 
		*                    the ReceiveFailReason property of the referenced Chilkat object.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
