	PROCEDURE getbasedomain		&& To be documented soon. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            GetBaseDomain
		* Purpose:           Returns the second-level + top-level domain of the domain.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcDomain, the URL domain.
		* Returns:           The base domain
		* Date Added:        06/13/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Returns the second-level + top-level domain of the domain. For example, 
		** if domain is "xyz.example.com", this returns "example.com". For some domains, 
		** such as "xyz.example.co.uk", the top 3 levels are returned, such as "example.co.uk".
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		** 
		** The GetBaseDomain method is a utility function that converts 
		** a domain into a "domain base", which is useful for grouping URLs. 
		** For example: abc.chilkatsoft.com, xyz.chilkatsoft.com, and blog.chilkatsoft.com 
		** all have the same base domain: chilkatsoft.com. Things get more complicated 
		** when considering country domains (.au, .uk, .se, .cn, etc.) and government, 
		** state, and .us domains. Also, domains such as blogspot, wordpress, etc, 
		** are treated specially so that "xyz.blogspot.com" has a base domain of "xyz.blogspot.com". 
		** Note: If you find other domains that should be treated similarly to blogspot.com, 
		** send a request to support@chilkatsoft.com.
		** 
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcDomain AS Integer
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS [Chilkat.Spider], ;
		loException AS Exception, lcBaseDomain AS Character
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		lcBaseDomain = []
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      lcBaseDomain = m.loChilkatObject.GetBaseDomain(m.tcDomain)
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcBaseDomain
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT([Chilkat.Spider])
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

