	PROCEDURE channelpoll		&& Polls for incoming data on an open channel. This method will read a channel, waiting at most pollTimeoutMs milliseconds for data to arrive. Return values are as follows:
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ChannelPoll
		* Purpose:           Polls for incoming data on an open channel.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tiChannel, the channel number.
		*                    tiPollTimeout, the timeout value, in milliseconds.
		* Returns:           Returns number of bytes, or error code.
		* Date Added:        04/09/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Polls for incoming data on an open channel. 
		** This method will read a channel, waiting at most 
		** pollTimeoutMs milliseconds for data to arrive. Return values are as follows:
		**
		** -1 -- Error. Check the IsConnected property to see if the connection 
		** to the SSH server is still valid. 
		** Also, call ChannelIsOpen to see if the channel remains open. 
		** The LastErrorText property will contain more detailed information regarding the error.
		**
		** -2 -- No additional data was received prior to the poll timeout.
		**
		** >0 -- Additional data was received and the return value 
		** indicates how many bytes are available to be "picked up". 
		** Methods that read data on a channel do not return the received data directly. 
		** Instead, they return an integer to indicate how many bytes 
		** are available to be "picked up". An application picks up the available data 
		** by calling GetReceivedData or GetReceivedText.
		**
		** =0 -- A zero can be returned if the channel EOF has already been received, 
		** or if the channel had already been closed.
		**
		** Fixed for Version 59: Fixed a performance problem w/ this method for very small timeouts.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tiChannel AS Integer, tiPollTimeout AS Integer
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, liReturn AS Integer
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      liReturn = m.loChilkatObject.ChannelPoll(m.tiChannel, m.tiPollTimeout)
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
