	PROCEDURE channelread		&& Reads incoming data on an open channel. This method will read a channel, waiting at most IdleTimeoutMs milliseconds for data to arrive.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ChannelRead
		* Purpose:           Reads incoming data on an open channel.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tiChannel, the channel number.
		* Returns:           Returns number of bytes, or error code.
		* Date Added:        04/10/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Reads incoming data on an open channel. This method will read a channel, 
		** waiting at most IdleTimeoutMs milliseconds for data to arrive. 
		** Return values are as follows:
		**
		** -1 -- Error. Check the IsConnected property to see if the connection 
		** to the SSH server is still valid. Also, call ChannelIsOpen to see 
		** if the channel remains open. The LastErrorText property will contain more 
		** detailed information regarding the error.
		**
		** -2 -- No additional data was received prior to the IdleTimeoutMs timeout.
		**
		** >0 -- Additional data was received and the return value indicates 
		** how many bytes are available to be "picked up". 
		** Methods that read data on a channel do not return the received data directly. 
		** Instead, they return an integer to indicate how many bytes 
		** are available to be "picked up". An application picks up the available data 
		** by calling GetReceivedData or GetReceivedText.
		**
		** =0 -- A zero can be returned if the channel EOF has already been received, 
		** or if the channel had already been closed.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tiChannel AS Integer
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, liReturn AS Integer
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		liReturn = 0
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      liReturn = m.loChilkatObject.ChannelRead(m.tiChannel)
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.liReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE channelreadandpoll		&& Reads incoming data on an open channel and continues reading until no data arrives for pollTimeoutMs milliseconds. The first read will wait a max of IdleTimeoutMs milliseconds before timing out.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ChannelReadAndPoll
		* Purpose:           Reads incoming data on an open channel and continues reading 
		*                    until no data arrives for pollTimeoutMs milliseconds.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tiChannel, the channel number.
		*                    tiPollTimeout, the timeout value, in milliseconds.
		* Returns:           Returns number of bytes, or error code.
		* Date Added:        04/10/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Reads incoming data on an open channel and continues reading 
		** until no data arrives for pollTimeoutMs milliseconds. 
		** The first read will wait a max of IdleTimeoutMs milliseconds before timing out. 
		** Subsequent reads wait a max of pollTimeoutMs milliseconds before timing out.
		**
		** The idea behind ChannelReadAndPoll is to capture the output of a shell command. 
		** One might imagine the typical sequence of events when executing a shell command 
		** to be like this: (1) client sends command to server, 
		** (2) server executes the command (i.e. it's computing...), 
		** potentially taking some amount of time, 
		** (3) output is streamed back to the client. 
		** It makes sense for the client to wait a longer period of time for the first data to arrive, 
		** but once it begins arriving, the timeout can be shortened. 
		** This is exactly what ChannelReadAndPoll does -- the first timeout is controlled 
		** by the IdleTimeoutMs property, while the subsequent reads (once output starts flowing) 
		** is controlled by pollTimeoutMs.
		**
		** Return values are as follows:
		**
		** -1 -- Error. Check the IsConnected property to see 
		** if the connection to the SSH server is still valid. 
		** Also, call ChannelIsOpen to see if the channel remains open. 
		** The LastErrorText property will contain more detailed information regarding the error.
		**
		** -2 -- No additional data was received prior to the IdleTimeoutMs timeout.
		**
		** >0 -- Additional data was received and the return value indicates 
		** how many bytes are available to be "picked up". 
		** Methods that read data on a channel do not return the received data directly. 
		** Instead, they return an integer to indicate how many bytes 
		** are available to be "picked up". An application picks up the available data 
		** by calling GetReceivedData or GetReceivedText.
		**
		** =0 -- A zero can be returned if the channel EOF has already been received, 
		** or if the channel had already been closed.
		**
		** Fixed for Version 91: The method incorrectly returned the number of bytes available 
		** to be “picked up” (from previous reads) instead of the value -2 
		** if the method call timed out before receiving additional data.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tiChannel AS Integer, tiPollTimeout AS Integer
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, liReturn AS Integer
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      liReturn = m.loChilkatObject.ChannelReadAndPoll(m.tiChannel, m.tiPollTimeout)
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.liReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

