	PROCEDURE channelreceiveuntilmatch		&& Reads incoming text data on an open channel until the received data matches the matchPattern. For example, to receive data until the string "Hello World" arrives, set matchPattern equal to "*Hello World*".
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ChannelReceiveUntilMatch
		* Purpose:           Reads incoming text data on an open channel 
		*                    until the received data matches the matchPattern.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tiChannel, the channel number.
		*                    tcMatchPattern, the pattern to match
		*                    tcCharset, the character set of the matching pattern
		*                    tuCaseSensitive -- Set to 1 to make the search case sensitive.
		* Returns:           Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		* Date Added:        04/10/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Reads incoming text data on an open channel until the received data matches the matchPattern. 
		** For example, to receive data until the string "Hello World" arrives, 
		** set matchPattern equal to "*Hello World*". 
		** charset indicates the character encoding 
		** of the text being received ("iso-8859-1" for example). 
		** caseSensitive may be set to 1 for case sensitive matching, 
		** or 0 for case insensitive matching.
		** 
		** Returns 1 if text data matching matchPattern was received 
		** and is available to be picked up by calling GetReceivedText (or GetReceivedTextS). 
		**
		** IMPORTANT: This method may read beyond the matching text. 
		** Call GetReceivedTextS to extract only the data up-to and including the matching text.
		**
		** Important Notes:
		**
		** It's wise to set the ReadTimeoutMs property to a non-zero value 
		** to prevent an infinite wait if the matchPattern never arrives.
		**
		** If using a shell session and SendReqPty was called, set the termType = "dumb". 
		** If terminal control codes get mixed into the output stream, it could disrupt matching.
		**
		** Be aware of the StderrToStdout property setting. The default value is true, 
		** which means that stderr is mixed with stdout in the output stream. 
		** This could disrupt matching. Set StderrToStdout to false to prevent this possibility.
		**
		** Fixed for Version 59: This method did not work for some cases with wildcard (*) match patterns.
		**
		** Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tiChannel AS Integer, tcMatchPattern AS Character, ;
		tcCharset AS Character, tuCaseSensitive AS Unknown
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		liReturn AS Integer, luReturn AS Unknown, liCaseSensitive AS Integer
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn, m.liCaseSensitive
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    liCaseSensitive = .LogicalToBit(m.tuCaseSensitive)
		
		    TRY
		
		      STORE ;
		      m.loChilkatObject.ChannelReceiveUntilMatch(m.tiChannel, ;
		      m.tcMatchPattern, m.tcCharset, m.liCaseSensitive) TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		  luReturn = .BitToLogical(m.liReturn)
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.luReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

