	PROCEDURE chilkatchangelog
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ChilkatChangeLog
		* Purpose:           Documentation method used to hold 
		*                    the Chilkat class changes per release version.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        02/03/2024
		*==============================================================================
		
		#IF .F.
		
		TEXT
		
		** Version 11.5.0
		
		  In Chilkat classes having SOCKS proxy properties, added the ability 
		  for a SOCKS destination host to be an IPv6 address.
		
		  Added the boolean EnableSecrets property to several Chilkat classes. When set to true, 
		  it provides the ability to pass a secret name rather than the actual value of a sensitive item. 
		  For example, a password for Ftp2, or a client_secret for OAuth2 client credentials. 
		  The value (such as client_secret) would’ve been previously stored via the Chilkat.Secrets API 
		  to the local manager, which on Windows is the Window Credentials Manager, 
		  and on Apple is the Apple Keychain.
		
		  Secrets Conceptual Overview — See Chilkat Secrets API for a refresher on the Secrets API.
		
		  When EnableSecrets is true, certain Chilkat methods and properties are secrets-aware. 
		  A passed-in value having the format “!!part1|part2|part3|part4” where a secret name 
		  is specified by providing 2 to 4 parts will get auto-resolved by looking up the secret 
		  in the local manager and found value will be used instead. 
		  This makes it easier for applications to avoid embedding sensitive information in source code.
		  For more information, see Chilkat EnableSecrets
		
		** Version 11.4.0
		
		  Added the GetReceivedBd method to append received data to a BinData object.
		
		  GetHostKeyFP — Fixed: There was a problem in the coalescing of SSH curve names 
		  to the standard curve names used by OpenSSH in the creation of the blob 
		  that is hashed to create the fingerprint. Also, the trailing “=” chars are now automatically stripped. 
		  (Stripping the “=” padding in SSH SHA256 fingerprints 
		  is now the de-facto standard behavior across SSH implementations.)
		
		  UncommonOptions(“+chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com”) — Fixed: Explicitly allowing 
		  the chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com cipher algorithm was not working.
		
		** Version 11.0.0
		
		  Removed the UnlockComponent method.
		
		  Decremented the LastJsonData method.
		
		** Version 99
		
		  The default client identifier for SSH connections is changed to 
		  “SSH-2.0-Chilkat_{version}, where {version} is a string such as “9.5.0.99”.  
		  
		  In some cases, Chilkat failed to establish connections trying to use aes-gcm. 
		  This was fixed. (It was not common.)
		
		  Added the SetAllowedAlgorithms method. This allows an application to explicitly set 
		  the set of allowed connection algorithms (cipher, mac, key exchange, etc.). 
		  Note: It’s best to NOT explicitly set the algorithms. Chilkat already prioritizes algorithms 
		  according to security and other factors. By explicitly setting algorithms, 
		  you may be creating a vulnerability (such as w/ the SSH Terrapin attack), 
		  or you might create a situation where the client and server cannot establish a connection 
		  because no mutually supported algorithms are possible.
		
		** Version 98
		
		  Restored the UncommonOption keyword “ForceUserAuthRsaSha1” for the rare cases 
		  where an SSH server supports rsa-sha2-256, rsa-sha2-512, 
		  but still requires SHA1 for the userauth algorithm.
		
		  Fixed a rare problem that can occur when the SSH client and server 
		  negotiate to the ssh-dss host key algorithm, which caused the connection to fail.
		
		** Version 97
		
		  Mitigated vulnerability to the Terrapin attack.
		  See https://cknotes.com/chilkat-v9-5-0-97-mitigates-vulnerability-to-the-ssh-terrapin-attack/
		
		** Version 96
		
		  Fixed possible RSA public key authentication problem for the Azure SSH server.
		
		** Version 95
		
		  Fixed rare connection problem with certain SSH servers.
		
		  Added support for SHA224 in all places where a hash algorithm might be specified.
		
		  Fixed uncommon public-key authentication problems where the client and server
		  are not agreeing on the choice of userauth key algorithm if RSA is used
		  and the server supports the rsa-sha2-256 and rsa-sha2-512 host key algorithms.
		
		** Version 94
		
		  Fixed login/authentication problems encountered w/ some SSH servers
		  when password + private key authentication is required (AuthenticatePwPk).
		
		  The internal name for curve25519-sha256@libssh.org was changed by newer servers to curve25519-sha256.
		  Chilkat is now modified to automatically work with both old or new servers.
		
		** Version 93
		
		  Programs that called ssh.QuickCommand many times in a loop would accumulate memory.
		  The memory would be deallocated if the Chilkat SSH object was destructed,
		  so it wasn’t technically a leak. This was fixed so that memory consumption does not accumulate.
		
		** Version 92
		
		  Added the GetHostKeyFP method to both Ssh and SFtp.
		
		** Version 91
		
		  Fixed: The ChannelReadAndPoll method incorrectly returned the number of bytes available
		  to be “picked up” (from previous reads) instead of the value -2
		  if the method call timed out before receiving additional data.
		
		  Fixed the HostKeyFingerprint property for cases where the SSH server’s host key is ED25519.
		
		** Version 90
		
		  Added support for new algorithms:
		  Key Exchange: diffie-hellman-group14-sha256, diffie-hellman-group16-sha512, diffie-hellman-group18-sha512
		  Host Key: rsa-sha2-256, rsa-sha2-512
		
		** Version 88
		
		  Added support for the “ecdsa-sha2-nistp521” and “ecdsa-sha2-nistp384” host key algorithms.
		
		** Version 87
		
		  Added support for the ecdh-sha2-nistp384 and ecdh-sha2-nistp521 key exchange algorithms.
		  This fixed the “Unable to agree upon host key algorithm.” seen with a few SSH servers.
		
		** Version 83
		
		  Improved support for ECDSA certs.
		
		  Improved support for Ed25519 private keys.
		
		** Version 82
		
		  Default for EnableCompression is changed to false because some servers fail with compression enabled,
		  and in other cases performance is slower with compression enabled.
		  (Yet in other cases, it’s possible that performance is better with compression enabled —
		  it entirely has to do with the compressibility of the data being sent/received.)
		
		** Version 79
		
		  Added the LastJsonData method. This provides the ability
		  to get additional information for some method calls.
		  For example, after calling Connect the LastJsonData will list
		  the algorithms used to establish the SSH connection.
		  Also, authentication failure reason information is available for each of the Authenticate* methods.
		
		** Version 79
		
		  Added the GetAuthMethods method to query an SSH server for the list of authentication methods it supports.
		
		** Version 75
		
		  Added the ClientPort property.
		
		  Fixed the HostKeyFingerprint property for ECDSA keys.
		
		** Version 73
		
		  Fixed a rarely encountered “handshake” problem.
		
		  Fixed: After doing a ReadDir, the SFtpFile.IsDirectory property was not correct for some types of SSH servers.
		
		  Fixed problems with IPv6 addresses when using SOCKS5 proxies.
		
		  Fixed slowness for SSH commands the emit a large amount of output.
		
		  Fixed a host key signature verification failure for certain situations.
		
		  Added the UncommonOptions property, which will be a place to specify
		  future unforeseen workarounds that may be required for particular SSH servers (old or new).
		
		** Version 71
		
		  Added the ServerIdentifier property.
		
		  Added AuthenticateSecPw and AuthenticateSecPwPk methods.
		
		** Version 70
		
		  Added internal re-try functionality to cope with various situations
		  for IPv4-only and IPv6-only networks.
		
		** Version 69
		
		  Fixed: calling the method QuickShell() generates an Access Violation when the LAN connection has been severed.
		
		** Version 67
		
		  Added the StripColorCodes property.
		
		** Version 66
		
		  Added support for chacha20 ciphers in TLS and SSH.
		
		** Version 65
		
		  ActiveX LastStringResultLen property incorrectly returned the size of the string in bytes (utf-16)
		  rather than in number of characters. This is fixed to return the number of characters.
		  (Note: this is a property that only exists in ActiveX classes, and is only useful
		  for certain programming languages such as SQL Server to help programs determine
		  if temp tables are required.)
		
		  Added the following methods: QuickShell, QuickCommand, QuickCmdSend, and QuickCmdCheck.
		  These methods help simplify executing remote commands running shell sessions.
		
		** Version 59
		
		  Fixed: ChannelReceiveUntilMatch did not work for some cases with wildcard (*) match patterns.
		
		  Fixed a performance problem w/ the ChannelPoll method for very small timeouts.
		
		** Version 58
		
		  The Windows logged-on username is no longer automatically logged at the top of every LastErrorText.
		  (This was originally done to help w/ support issues so tht Chilkat might notice if the program runs
		  in the context of a Service or IIS, which could be a clue to the cause of certain problems.)
		
		  Added the AbortCurrent property to classes that can have event callbacks.
		
		** Version 56
		
		  Added the EnableCompression property. An old server was discovered that did not correctly handle compression.
		  Chilkat automatically disables compression when the problematic servers are encountered,
		  but if undiscovered old servers have the same problem, this property can be set to work around the problem.
		
		** Version 53
		
		  The LastStringResultLen property is added to each Chilkat class.
		  This is helpful for certain programming languages such as DataFlex or SQL Server
		  where the size of the string returned may need to be known before using it.
		  Each Chilkat ActiveX object has its own LastStringResult and LastStringResultLen properties.
		  The KeepStringResult is a property of Chilkat.Global only.
		  (It may be confusing that Chilkat.Global also has a LastStringResult property —
		  but this is just like any other object.)
		
		  Therefore, your code would set Global.KeepStringResult once at the beginning of your code.
		
		  Let’s say you have an HttpResult object, and you want the BodyQP.
		  You would access the BodyQP, but ignore the string returned.
		  Then examine the HttpResult.LastStringResultLen, adjust your max string length (in DataFlex) if necessary,
		  and then get the cached string from HttpResult.LastStringResult.
		
		  The SSH Rekey handling for certain host key algorithms was fixed.
		
		** Version 52
		
		  Added asynchronous functionality for all qualifying methods
		  across all programming languages, operating systems, and architectures.
		  Each Chilkat method that can potentially be time-consuming or involve network communications,
		  now has a corresponding asynchronous version of the method with the name ending in “Async”.
		
		  Added the LastMethodSuccess property.
		
		  Added the AuthFailReason property.
		
		** Version 51
		
		  Applies to any Chilkat class with HTTP proxy capabilities:
		  Fixed issues related to using HTTP proxes for non-HTTP protocols where SSL/TLS is not used.
		
		** Version 49
		
		  Non-SSL/TLS HTTP proxy connections were trying to use CONNECT.
		
		  The internal automatic retry from EHLO to HELO did not work.
		  If the SMTP server did not support EHLO, then EHLO
		  was mistakenly tried a 2nd time instead of HELO
		
		** Version 48
		
		  Improved performance through the automatic (internal) use of pipelining.
		
		  Added the WaitForChannelMessage method. (See online reference documentation.)
		
		** Version 47
		
		  Added the SendReqCharset property.
		
		** Version 46
		
		  Added the CheckConnection method, which returns true if the underlying TCP socket is connected to the server.
		
		  Added the UserAuthBanner property.
		
		  Added the StartKeyboardAuth and ContinueKeyboardAuth methods to allow for explicit keyboard authenication.
		
		** Version 44
		
		  New: Added the SSH ChannelRelease method. Old channels will accumulate in memory,
		  even after being closed because a program may still need to retrieve data from an already-closed channel.
		  The ChannelRelease method allows for a program to specifically release the internal memory for a channel.
		  It is not required to call ChannelRelease.
		  When the SSH object itself is deleted/disposed/garbage collected, etc., then all internal memory
		  (including for all internal channels) is automatically deleted.
		  The only reason to call ChannelRelease is if an exceptionally large number of channels
		  is opened/used/closed within the same Chilkat SSH object instance.
		  The ChannelRelease method provides a means to prevent the accumulation of memory usage for this case.
		
		** Version 27
		
		  Added support for the hmac-sha2-512,hmac-sha2-256,hmac-ripemd160 algorithms to SSH/SFTP internal transport.
		
		ENDTEXT
		
		#ENDIF .F.
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE clearttymodes		&& Clears the collection of TTY modes that are sent with the SendReqPty method.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClearTTYModes
		* Purpose:           Clears the collection of TTY modes that are sent with the SendReqPty method.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        04/10/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Clears the collection of TTY modes that are sent with the SendReqPty method.
		**
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      m.loChilkatObject.ClearTTYModes()
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE clientidentifier_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SSH ClientIdentifier property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClientIdentifier_Access
		* Purpose:           Access method used to retrieve 
		*                    the Chilkat SSH ClientIdentifier property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           THIS.ClientIdentifier
		* Date Added:        04/08/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Specifies the SSH client-identification string sent when a connection is established. 
		** The default is SSH-2.0-Chilkat_ followed by the Chilkat version, for example SSH-2.0-Chilkat_11.6.0.
		**
		** The value should begin with SSH-2.0-. A server may disconnect if the identification string is not valid.
		**
		** Updated description in version 99:
		** The client-identifier string to be used when connecting to an SSH/SFTP server. 
		** Starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.99, the default is "SSH-2.0-Chilkat_" 
		** + the Chilkat version number, such as "SSH-2.0-Chilkat_9.5.0.99".
		**
		** Note: The client identifier should always begin with "SSH-2.0-". SSH servers may disconnect if it does not.
		**
		** Changed in version 99: The default client identifier for SSH connections 
		** is changed to “SSH-2.0-Chilkat_{version}, where {version} 
		** is a string such as “9.5.0.99”.
		**
		
		LOCAL liStackLevel AS Integer, lcMethod AS Character, lcProperty AS Character, ;
		lcMethodToCall AS Character, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_Stack[1, 1]
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liStackLevel, m.liIntroducedInBuild
		STORE [] TO m.lcMethod, m.lcProperty, m.lcMethodToCall, m.la_Stack
		
		liStackLevel = ASTACKINFO(la_Stack)
		
		lcMethod = m.la_Stack(m.liStackLevel, 3)
		lcMethod = PROPER(SUBSTRC(m.lcMethod, AT_C([.], m.lcMethod) + 1))
		lcProperty = LEFTC(m.lcMethod, LENC(m.lcMethod) - 7)
		
		lcMethodToCall = [String]
		
		THIS.CallAccessObject(m.lcMethodToCall, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN EVALUATE([THIS.] + m.lcProperty)
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE clientidentifier_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ClientIdentifier property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClientIdentifier_Assign
		* Purpose:           Assign method used to hold a reference to the ClientIdentifier property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcValue, character value used to hold 
		*                    a reference to the ClientIdentifier property.
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        04/08/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		LPARAMETERS tcValue AS Character
		
		LOCAL lcValidationMethod AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		lcValidationMethod = []
		lcMethodToCall = [String]
		
		THIS.CallAssignObject(m.tcValue, m.lcMethodToCall, m.lcValidationMethod)
		
		RETURN
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE clientipaddress_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SSH ClientIPAddress property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClientIPAddress_Access
		* Purpose:           Access method used to retrieve 
		*                    the Chilkat SSH ClientIPAddress property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           THIS.ClientIPAddress
		* Date Added:        04/08/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** The IP address to use for computers with multiple network interfaces or IP addresses. 
		** For computers with a single network interface (i.e. most computers), 
		** this property should not be set. For multihoming computers, 
		** the default IP address is automatically used if this property is not set.
		**
		** The IP address is a string such as in dotted notation using numbers, 
		** not domain names, such as "165.164.55.124".
		**
		
		LOCAL liStackLevel AS Integer, lcMethod AS Character, lcProperty AS Character, ;
		lcMethodToCall AS Character, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_Stack[1, 1]
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liStackLevel, m.liIntroducedInBuild
		STORE [] TO m.lcMethod, m.lcProperty, m.lcMethodToCall, m.la_Stack
		
		liStackLevel = ASTACKINFO(la_Stack)
		
		lcMethod = m.la_Stack(m.liStackLevel, 3)
		lcMethod = PROPER(SUBSTRC(m.lcMethod, AT_C([.], m.lcMethod) + 1))
		lcProperty = LEFTC(m.lcMethod, LENC(m.lcMethod) - 7)
		
		lcMethodToCall = [String]
		
		THIS.CallAccessObject(m.lcMethodToCall, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN EVALUATE([THIS.] + m.lcProperty)
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE clientipaddress_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ClientIPAddress property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClientIPAddress_Assign
		* Purpose:           Assign method used to hold a reference to the ClientIPAddress property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcValue, character value used to hold 
		*                    a reference to the ClientIPAddress property.
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        04/08/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		LPARAMETERS tcValue AS Character
		
		LOCAL lcValidationMethod AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		lcValidationMethod = []
		lcMethodToCall = [String]
		
		THIS.CallAssignObject(m.tcValue, m.lcMethodToCall, m.lcValidationMethod)
		
		RETURN
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE clientport_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat SSH ClientPort property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClientPort_Access
		* Purpose:           Access method used to retrieve 
		*                    the Chilkat SSH ClientPort property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           THIS.ClientPort
		* Date Added:        04/08/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.75
		**
		** This property is normally left at its default value of 0. In this case, 
		** the operating system automatically chooses an unused local port from its ephemeral-port range. 
		** Applications should set a specific local port only when a remote system 
		** or network policy requires the connection to originate from that port.
		**
		** When set to a nonzero value, Chilkat requests that exact local port. 
		** The connection fails if the port is already in use or is otherwise unavailable. 
		** A specifically chosen port might also be temporarily unavailable for reuse 
		** after a connection closes because of operating-system TCP connection management. 
		** These port-reuse concerns do not normally apply when this property remains 0.
		**
		** This property applies to all connection paths, including direct SSH connections, 
		** HTTP and SOCKS proxy connections, ConnectThroughSsh, and multi-hop SSH connections.
		**
		** Starting in Chilkat v11.6.0, assigned values must be in the range 0 through 65535. 
		** If a negative value or a value greater than 65535 is assigned, 
		** it is ignored and the existing property value remains unchanged.
		** 
		
		LOCAL liStackLevel AS Integer, lcMethod AS Character, ;
		lcProperty AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_Stack[1, 1], la_IntroducedInBuild[3, 1]
		
		STORE [] TO m.lcMethod, m.lcProperty, m.lcMethodToCall, m.la_Stack, m.la_IntroducedInBuild
		
		liStackLevel = ASTACKINFO(la_Stack)
		
		lcMethod = m.la_Stack(m.liStackLevel, 3)
		lcMethod = PROPER(SUBSTRC(m.lcMethod, AT_C([.], m.lcMethod) + 1))
		lcProperty = LEFTC(m.lcMethod, LENC(m.lcMethod) - 7)
		
		lcMethodToCall = [Long]
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 9
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 5
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 75
		
		THIS.CallAccessObject(m.lcMethodToCall, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN EVALUATE([THIS.] + m.lcProperty)
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE clientport_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ClientPort property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClientPort_Assign
		* Purpose:           Assign method used to hold a reference to the ClientPort property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tiValue, integer value used to hold 
		*                    a reference to the ClientPort property.
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        04/08/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		LPARAMETERS tiValue AS Integer
		
		LOCAL lcValidationMethod AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_IntroducedInBuild[3, 1]
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 9
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 5
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 75
		
		lcValidationMethod = [ClientPort]
		lcMethodToCall = [Long]
		
		THIS.CallAssignObject(m.tiValue, m.lcMethodToCall, m.lcValidationMethod, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE connect		&& Connects to the SSH server at domainName:port The domainName may be a domain name or an IPv4 or IPv6 address in string format.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            Connect
		* Purpose:           Connects to the SSH server at domainName:port
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcDomainName -- the login domain
		*                    tiPort, the port number
		* Returns:           Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		* Date Added:        04/10/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Connects to the SSH server at domainName:port
		**
		** The domainName may be a domain name or an IPv4 or IPv6 address in string format.
		**
		** Internally, the following SSH connection protocol algorithms are supported:
		**
		** Hostkey Types: ssh-rsa, ssh-dsa, ecdsa-sha2-nistp256, rsa-sha2-256, rsa-sha2-512, ssh-ed25519
		** Key Exchange Methods: curve25519-sha256@libssh.org, ecdh-sha2-nistp256, ecdh-sha2-nistp384, 
		** ecdh-sha2-nistp521, diffie-hellman-group-exchange-sha256, diffie-hellman-group-exchange-sha1, 
		** diffie-hellman-group14-sha1, diffie-hellman-group1-sha1
		**
		** Ciphers: chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com, aes256-ctr, aes192-ctr, aes128-ctr, aes256-cbc,
		** aes192-cbc, aes128-cbc, twofish256-cbc, twofish128-cbc, blowfish-cbc, 3des-cbc,
		** arcfour128, arcfour256
		**
		** MAC Algorithms: hmac-sha2-256, hmac-sha2-512, hmac-sha1, hmac-md5, hmac-ripemd160, hmac-sha1-96
		** Compression: none, zlib, zlib@openssh.com
		** Important: All TCP-based Internet communications, regardless of the protocol 
		** (such as HTTP, FTP, SSH, IMAP, POP3, SMTP, etc.), and regardless of SSL/TLS, 
		** begin with establishing a TCP connection to a remote host:port. 
		**
		** External security-related infrastructure such as software firewalls (Windows Firewall), 
		** hardware firewalls, anti-virus, at either source or destination (or both) 
		** can block the connection. If the connection fails, 
		** make sure to check all potential external causes of blockage.
		**
		** Fixed for Version 48: 
		** Improved performance through the automatic (internal) use of pipelining.
		**
		** Enhancement for version 87: Added support for the ecdh-sha2-nistp384 and ecdh-sha2-nistp521 
		** key exchange algorithms. This fixed the “Unable to agree upon host key algorithm.” 
		** seen with a few SSH servers.
		**
		** Enhancement for version 88: Added support for the “ecdsa-sha2-nistp521” 
		** and “ecdsa-sha2-nistp384” host key algorithms. 
		**
		** Fixed for version 97: chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com is no longer included by default. 
		** (Due to the Terrapin Attack, see https://terrapin-attack.com/)
		** It can be re-added by specifying “+chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com” in the UncommonOptions property.
		**
		** Fixed for version 97: hmac-sha1-etm@openssh.com, hmac-sha2-256-etm@openssh.com 
		** hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com are no longer included by default. 
		** (Due to the Terrapin Attack, see https://terrapin-attack.com/)
		** It can be re-added by specifying “+ssh-hmac-etm” in the UncommonOptions property.
		**
		** Fixed in version 99: In some cases, Chilkat failed to establish connections 
		** trying to use aes-gcm. This was fixed. (It was not common.)
		**
		** Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcDomainName AS Character, tiPort AS Integer
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		liReturn AS Integer, luReturn AS Unknown
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      STORE m.loChilkatObject.Connect(m.tcDomainName, m.tiPort) ;
		      TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		  luReturn = .BitToLogical(m.liReturn)
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.luReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
		
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE connectasync		&& Creates an asynchronous task to call the Connect method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ConnectAsync
		* Purpose:           Creates an asynchronous task to call the 
		*                    Connect method with the arguments provided.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcDomainName -- the domain name.
		*                    tiPort, the port number.
		* Returns:           toChilkatTask, a Chilkat Task object.
		* Date Added:        04/10/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Creates an asynchronous task to call the Connect method with the arguments provided. 
		** (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		**
		** Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread. 
		** Accessing and updating UI elements existing in the main thread may require special considerations.
		**
		** Enhancement for version 87: Added support for the ecdh-sha2-nistp384 and ecdh-sha2-nistp521 
		** key exchange algorithms. This fixed the “Unable to agree upon host key algorithm.” 
		** seen with a few SSH servers.
		**
		** Enhancement for version 88: Added support for the “ecdsa-sha2-nistp521” 
		** and “ecdsa-sha2-nistp384” host key algorithms. 
		**
		** Fixed for version 97: chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com is no longer included by default. 
		** (Due to the Terrapin Attack, see https://terrapin-attack.com/)
		** It can be re-added by specifying “+chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com” in the UncommonOptions property.
		**
		** Fixed for version 97: hmac-sha1-etm@openssh.com, hmac-sha2-256-etm@openssh.com 
		** hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com are no longer included by default. 
		** (Due to the Terrapin Attack, see https://terrapin-attack.com/)
		** It can be re-added by specifying “+ssh-hmac-etm” in the UncommonOptions property.
		**
		** Fixed in version 99: In some cases, Chilkat failed to establish connections 
		** trying to use aes-gcm. This was fixed. (It was not common.)
		**
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcDomainName AS Character, tiPort AS Integer
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		loChilkatTask AS CHILKAT_TASK_COM_CALL, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, m.loChilkatTask
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 52
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        loChilkatTask = m.loChilkatObject.ConnectAsync(m.tcDomainName, m.tiPort)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.loChilkatTask
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		  loChilkatTask = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_TASK_COM_CALL)
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
		
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE connectthroughssh		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.55. Connects to an SSH server through an existing SSH connection. The ssh is an existing connected and authenticated SSH object. The connection to hostname:port is made through the existing SSH connection via port-forwarding.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ConnectThroughSSH
		* Purpose:           Connects to an SSH server through an existing SSH connection.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        toChilkatSSH -- a Chilkat SSH object.
		*                    tcHostName -- the host name.
		*                    tiPort -- the port number.
		* Returns:           Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		* Date Added:        04/10/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.55
		**
		** Connects to an SSH server through an existing SSH connection. 
		** The ssh is an existing connected and authenticated SSH object. 
		** The connection to hostname:port is made through the existing SSH connection 
		** via port-forwarding. If successful, the connection is as follows: 
		** application => ServerSSH1 => ServerSSH2. 
		** (where ServerSSH1 is the ssh and ServerSSH2 is the SSH server at hostname:port) 
		** Once connected in this way, all communications are routed through ServerSSH1 to ServerSSH2. 
		** This includes authentication -- which means the application 
		** must still call one of the Authenticate* methods to authenticate with ServerSSH2.
		**
		** Fixed in version 99: In some cases, Chilkat failed to establish connections 
		** trying to use aes-gcm. This was fixed. (It was not common.)
		**
		** Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS toChilkatSSH AS CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL, tcHostName AS Character, tiPort AS Integer
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		liReturn AS Integer, luReturn AS Unknown, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		loParkParameterSsh AS [iParkParameter OF ChilkatVFP.VCX], ;
		loChilkatSsh AS CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL, llImplemented AS Logical
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn, m.liIntroducedInBuild
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterSsh, m.loChilkatSsh
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 55
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      loParkParameterSsh = ;
		      NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], .ClassLibrary, [], m.toChilkatSsh)
		
		      loChilkatSsh = m.loParkParameterSsh.GetObject()
		
		      TRY
		
		        STORE m.loChilkatObject.ConnectThroughSSH(m.loChilkatSSH, m.tcHostName, m.tiPort) ;
		        TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		      toChilkatSsh = m.loParkParameterSsh.SetObject(m.toChilkatSsh, m.loChilkatSsh)
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		  luReturn = .BitToLogical(m.liReturn)
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterSsh, m.loChilkatSsh
		
		RETURN m.luReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL)
		  toChilkatSSH = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL)
		  loParkParameterSsh = NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], [ChilkatVFP.VCX])
		  loChilkatSsh = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

