	PROCEDURE opensessionchannel		&& Opens a new session channel. Almost everything you will do with the Chilkat SSH component will involve opening a session channel.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            OpenSessionChannel
		* Purpose:           Opens a new session channel.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           The new session channel.
		* Date Added:        04/10/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Opens a new session channel. 
		** Almost everything you will do with the Chilkat SSH component 
		** will involve opening a session channel. 
		** The normal sequence of operation is typically this:
		** 
		** 1) Connect to the SSH server. 
		** 2) Authenticate. 
		** 3) Open a session channel. 
		** 4) do something on the channel such as opening a shell, execute a command, etc.
		** 
		** If successful, the channel number is returned. 
		** This is the number that should be passed to any method requiring a channel number. 
		** A -1 is returned upon failure.
		** 
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, liChannel AS Integer
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		liChannel = 0
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		  ** Have a good object test
		  IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		    TRY
		
		      liChannel = m.loChilkatObject.OpenSessionChannel()
		
		    CATCH TO m.loException
		
		      .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		    ENDTRY
		
		  ELSE
		
		    .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		  ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		  AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		  ** End have a good object test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.liChannel
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SSH_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

