	PROCEDURE continuekeyboardauth		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.78. Continues keyboard-interactive authentication with the SSH server. The response is typically the password.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ContinueKeyboardAuth
		* Purpose:           Continues keyboard-interactive authentication with the SSH server. 
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcResponse -- the server response.
		* Returns:           Character
		* Date Added:        07/08/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.78
		**
		** Continues keyboard-interactive authentication with the SSH server. 
		** The response is typically the password. If multiple responses are required 
		** (because there were multiple prompts in the infoRequest XML returned by StartKeyboardAuth), 
		** then the response should be formatted as XML (as shown below) 
		** otherwise the response simply contains the single response string.
		**
		**   <response>
		**       <response1>response to first prompt</response1>
		**       <response2>response to second prompt</response2>
		**       ...
		**       <responseN>response to Nth prompt</responseN>
		**   </response>
		** 
		** If the interactive authentication completed with success or failure, 
		** the XML response will be:
		** 
		**   <success>success_message</success>
		** 
		** or
		** 
		**   <error>error_message</error>
		** 
		** If additional steps are required to complete the interactive authentication, 
		** then an XML string that provides the name, instruction, and prompts is returned. 
		** 
		** The XML has the following format:
		**
		**   <infoRequest numPrompts="N">
		**         <name>name_string</name>
		**         <instruction>instruction_string</instruction>
		**         <prompt1 echo="1_or_0">prompt_string</prompt1>
		**         ...
		**         <promptN echo="1_or_0">prompt_string</promptN>
		**     </infoRequest>
		** 
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcResponse AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_SSHTUNNEL_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		lcPostResponse AS Character, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		lcPostResponse = []
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 78
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        lcPostResponse = m.loChilkatObject.ContinueKeyboardAuth(m.tcResponse)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcPostResponse
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_SSHTUNNEL_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE continuekeyboardauthasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.78. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ContinueKeyboardAuth method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ContinueKeyboardAuthAsync
		* Purpose:           Creates an asynchronous task to call the 
		*                    ContinueKeyboardAuth method with the arguments provided.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
