		*m: defaultchunksize_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the DefaultChunkSize property.
		*m: endofstream_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream EndOfStream property.
		*m: endofstream_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the EndOfStream property.
		*m: heartbeatms_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream HeartbeatMs property.
		*m: heartbeatms_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the HeartbeatMs property.
		*m: iswriteclosed_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream IsWriteClosed property.
		*m: iswriteclosed_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the IsWriteClosed property.
		*m: lastbinaryresult_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream LastBinaryResult property.
		*m: lastbinaryresult_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastBinaryResult property.
		*m: lasterrorhtml_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream LastErrorHTML property.
		*m: lasterrorhtml_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastErrorHTML property.
		*m: lasterrortext_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream LastErrorText property.
		*m: lasterrortext_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastErrorText property.
		*m: lasterrorxml_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream LastErrorXML property.
		*m: lasterrorxml_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastErrorXML property.
		*m: lastmethodsuccess_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream LastMethodSuccess property.
		*m: lastmethodsuccess_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastMethodSuccess property.
		*m: laststringresultlen_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream LastStringResultLen property.
		*m: laststringresultlen_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastStringResultLen property.
		*m: laststringresult_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream LastStringResult property.
		*m: laststringresult_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastStringResult property
		*m: length32_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream Length32 property.
		*m: length32_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Length32 property
		*m: length_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream Length property.
		*m: length_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Length property.
		*m: loadtaskcaller		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.80. Loads the caller of the task's async method. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: numreceived_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream NumReceived property.
		*m: numreceived_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the NumReceived property.
		*m: numsent_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream NumSent property.
		*m: numsent_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the NumSent property.
		*m: readbd		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.67. Read as much data as is immediately available on the stream. If no data is immediately available, it waits up to ReadTimeoutMs milliseconds for data to arrive. The incoming data is appended to binData.
		*m: readbdasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.67. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReadBd method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: readbytes		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Read as much data as is immediately available on the stream. If no data is immediately available, it waits up to ReadTimeoutMs milliseconds for data to arrive. Returns a zero-length byte array (as a Variant) on failure.
		*m: readbytesasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReadBytes method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: readbytesenc		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. The same as ReadBytes, except returns the received bytes in encoded string form. The encoding argument indicates the encoding, which can be "base64", "hex", or any of the multitude of encodings indicated in the link below.
		*m: readbytesencasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReadBytesENC method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: readfailreason_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream ReadFailReason property.
		*m: readfailreason_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ReadFailReason property.
		*m: readnbytes		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Reads exactly numBytes bytes from the stream. If no data is immediately available, it waits up to ReadTimeoutMs milliseconds for data to arrive. Returns a zero-length byte array (as a Variant) on failure.
		*m: readnbytesasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReadNBytes method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.)
		*m: readnbytesenc		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. The same as ReadNBytes, except returns the received bytes in encoded string form. The encoding argument indicates the encoding, which can be "base64", "hex", or any of the multitude of encodings indicated in the link below.
		*m: readnbytesencasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReadNBytesENC method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: readsb		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.67. Read as much data as is immediately available on the stream. If no data is immediately available, it waits up to ReadTimeoutMs milliseconds for data to arrive. The data is appended to sb.
		*m: readsbasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.67. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReadSb method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: readstring		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Read as much data as is immediately available on the stream. If no data is immediately available, it waits up to ReadTimeoutMs milliseconds for data to arrive. The data is returned as a string.
		*m: readstringasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReadString method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: readtimeoutms_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream ReadTimeoutMs property.
		*m: readtimeoutms_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ReadTimeoutMs property.
		*m: readtocrlf		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Reads the stream until a CRLF is received. If no data is immediately available, it waits up to ReadTimeoutMs milliseconds for data to arrive. The data is returned as a string.
		*m: readtocrlfasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReadToCRLF method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: readuntilmatch		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Reads the stream until the string indicated by matchStr is received. If no data is immediately available, it waits up to ReadTimeoutMs milliseconds for data to arrive. The data is returned as a string.
		*m: readuntilmatchasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Creates an asynchronous task to call the ReadUntilMatch method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: reset		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Resets the stream. If a source or sink is open, then it is closed. Properties such as EndOfStream and IsWriteClose are reset to default values.
		*m: runstream		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Runs the stream to completion.
		*m: runstreamasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Creates an asynchronous task to call the RunStream method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: setsinkstream		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Sets the stream's sink to strm. Any data written to this stream's sink will become available to strm on its source. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setsourcebytes		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Sets the stream's source to the contents of sourceData. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setsourcestream		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Sets the stream's source to be the sink of strm. Any data written to strm's sink will become available on this stream's source. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: setsourcestring		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Sets the stream's source to the contents of srcStr. The charset indicates the character encoding to be used for the byte representation of the srcStr. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: sinkfileappend_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream SinkFileAppend property.
		*m: sinkfileappend_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SinkFileAppend property.
		*m: sinkfile_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream SinkFile property.
		*m: sinkfile_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SinkFile property.
		*m: sourcefilepartsize_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream SourceFilePartSize property.
		*m: sourcefilepartsize_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SourceFilePartSize property.
		*m: sourcefilepart_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream SourceFilePart property.
		*m: sourcefilepart_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SourceFilePart property.
		*m: sourcefile_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream SourceFile property.
		*m: sourcefile_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the SourceFile property.
		*m: stringbom_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream StringBOM property.
		*m: stringbom_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the StringBOM property.
		*m: stringcharset_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream StringCharset property.
		*m: stringcharset_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the StringCharset property.
		*m: todecimalstr		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Some programming languages do not support 64-bit integers. The following properties are implemented as 64-bit ints: Length, NumReceived, NumSent.
		*m: verboselogging_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream VerboseLogging property.
		*m: verboselogging_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the VerboseLogging property.
		*m: writebd		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.67. Writes the contents of binData to the stream. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: writebdasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.67. Creates an asynchronous task to call the WriteBd method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: writebyte		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Writes a single byte to the stream. The byteVal must have a value from 0 to 255. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: writebyteasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Creates an asynchronous task to call the WriteByte method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.).
		*m: writebytes		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Writes binary bytes to a stream. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: writebytesasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Creates an asynchronous task to call the WriteBytes method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: writebytesenc		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Writes binary bytes to a stream. The byte data is passed in encoded string form, where the encoding can be "base64", "hex", or any of the supported binary encodings listed at the link below.
		*m: writebytesencasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Creates an asynchronous task to call the WriteBytesENC method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: writeclose		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Indicates that no more data will be written to the stream. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: writefailreason_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream WriteFailReason property.
		*m: writefailreason_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the WriteFailReason property.
		*m: writesb		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.67. Writes the contents of sb to the stream. The actual bytes written are the byte representation of the string as indicated by the StringCharset property.
		*m: writesbasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.67. Creates an asynchronous task to call the WriteSb method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: writestring		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Writes a string to a stream. The actual bytes written are the byte representation of the string as indicated by the StringCharset property.
		*m: writestringasync		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Creates an asynchronous task to call the WriteString method with the arguments provided. (Async methods are available starting in Chilkat v9.5.0.52.) Note: Async method event callbacks happen in the background thread.
		*m: writetimeoutms_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream WriteTimeouitMs property.
		*m: writetimeoutms_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the WriteTimeoutMs property.
		*p: abortcurrent		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. When set to 1, causes the currently running method to abort. Methods that always finish quickly (i.e.have no length file operations or network communications) are not affected.
		*p: canread		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. 1 if the stream supports reading. Otherwise 0. Note: A stream that supports reading, which has already reached the end-of-stream, will still have a CanRead value of 1.
		*p: canwrite		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. 1 if the stream supports writing. Otherwise 0. Note: A stream that supports writing, which has already been closed for write, will still have a CanWrite value of 1.
		*p: dataavailable		&& 1 if it is known for sure that data is ready and waiting to be read. 0 if it is not known for sure.
		*p: debuglogfilepath		&& If set to a file path, causes each Chilkat method or property call to automatically append it's LastErrorText to the specified log file.
		*p: defaultchunksize		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. The default internal chunk size for reading or writing. The default value is 65536. If this property is set to 0, it will cause the default chunk size (65536) to be used.
		*p: endofstream		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. 1 if the end-of-stream has already been reached. When the stream has already ended, all calls to Read* methods will return 0 with the ReadFailReason set to 3 (already at end-of-stream).
		*p: heartbeatms		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.97. The time interval, in milliseconds, between AbortCheck event callbacks. The heartbeat provides a means for an application to monitor a method call that has event callbacks, and to abort it while in progress.
		*p: iswriteclosed		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. 1 if the stream is closed for writing. Once closed, no more data may be written to the stream.
		*p: lastbinaryresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The binary data returned by the last (binary data returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepBinaryResult is set to 1.
		*p: lasterrorhtml		&& Provides information in HTML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrortext		&& Provides information in plain-text format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrorxml		&& Provides information in XML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lastmethodsuccess		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Indicate whether the last method call succeeded or failed. A value of 1 indicates success, a value of 0 indicates failure. This property is automatically set for method calls. It is not modified by property accesses.
		*p: laststringresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The string return value of the last (string returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepStringResult is set to 1.
		*p: laststringresultlen		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.53. The length, in characters, of the string contained in the LastStringResult property.
		*p: length		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. The length (in bytes) of the stream's source. If unknown, then this property will have a value of -1. This property may be set by the application if it knows in advance the length of the stream.
		*p: length32		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.58. The length (in bytes) of the stream's source. If unknown, then this property will have a value of -1. This property may be set by the application if it knows in advance the length of the stream.
		*p: numreceived		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. The number of bytes received by the stream.
		*p: numsent		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. The number of bytes sent by the stream.
		*p: readfailreason		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. This property is automatically set when a Read* method is called. It indicates the reason for failure.
		*p: readtimeoutms		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. The maximum number of seconds to wait while reading. The default value is 30 seconds (i.e. 30000ms). A value of 0 indicates a poll. (A polling read is to return with a timeout if no data is immediately available.)
		*p: sinkfile		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Sets the sink to the path of a file. The file does not need to exist at the time of setting this property. The sink file will be automatically opened on demand, when the stream is first written.
		*p: sinkfileappend		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.83. If 1, the stream appends to the SinkFile rather than truncating and re-writing the sink file. The default value is 0.
		*p: sourcefile		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Sets the source to the path of a file. The file does not need to exist at the time of setting this property. The source file will be automatically opened on demand, when the stream is first read.
		*p: sourcefilepart		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.59. If the source is a file, then this property can be used to stream one part of the file. The SourceFilePartSize property defines the size (in bytes) of each part.
		*p: sourcefilepartsize		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.59. If the source is a file, then this property, in conjunction with the SourceFilePart property, can be used to stream a single part of the file.
		*p: stringbom		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. If 1, then include the BOM when creating a string source via SetSourceString where the charset is utf-8, utf-16, etc. (The term "BOM" stands for Byte Order Mark, also known as the preamble.)
		*p: stringcharset		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. Indicates the expected character encoding, such as utf-8, windows-1256, utf-16, etc. for methods that read text such as: ReadString, ReadToCRLF, ReadUntilMatch.
		*p: verboselogging		&& If set to 1, then the contents of LastErrorText (or LastErrorXml, or LastErrorHtml) may contain more verbose information. The default value is 0. Verbose logging should only be used for debugging.
		*p: writefailreason		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. This property is automatically set when a Write* method is called. It indicates the reason for failure.
		*p: writetimeoutms		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.56. The maximum number of seconds to wait while writing. The default value is 30 seconds (i.e. 30000ms). A value of 0 indicates to return immediately if it is not possible to write to the sink immediately.
	*</DefinedPropArrayMethod>

	*<PropValue>
		abortcurrent = 0
		canread = 1
		canwrite = 1
		cchilkatclass = Stream
		dataavailable = 0
		debuglogfilepath = 
		defaultchunksize = 65536
		endofstream = 0
		heartbeatms = 0
		iinstancepatch = 56
		iswriteclosed = 0
		lastbinaryresult = .NULL.
		lasterrorhtml = 
		lasterrortext = 
		lasterrorxml = 
		lastmethodsuccess = 1
		laststringresult = 
		laststringresultlen = 0
		length = 0
		length32 = 0
		Name = "stream"
		numreceived = 0
		numsent = 0
		readfailreason = 0
		readtimeoutms = 30000
		sinkfile = 
		sinkfileappend = 0
		sourcefile = 
		sourcefilepart = 0
		sourcefilepartsize = 0
		stringbom = 0
		stringcharset = utf-8
		verboselogging = 0
		writefailreason = 0
		writetimeoutms = 30000
	*</PropValue>
	
	HIDDEN PROCEDURE abortcurrent_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Stream AbortCurrent property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            AbortCurrent_Access
		* Purpose:           Access method used to retrieve 
		*                    the Chilkat Stream AbortCurrent property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           THIS.AbortCurrent
		* Date Added:        06/13/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.58
		**
		** When set to 1, causes the currently running method to abort. 
		** Methods that always finish quickly (i.e.have no length file operations or network communications) 
		** are not affected. If no method is running, then this property is automatically 
		** reset to 0 when the next method is called. When the abort occurs, 
		** this property is reset to 0. Both synchronous and asynchronous method calls can be aborted. 
		** (A synchronous method call could be aborted by setting this property from a separate thread.)
		**
		
		LOCAL liStackLevel AS Integer, lcMethod AS Character, ;
		lcProperty AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_Stack[1, 1], la_IntroducedInBuild[3, 1]
		
		STORE [] TO m.lcMethod, m.lcProperty, m.lcMethodToCall, m.la_Stack, m.la_IntroducedInBuild
		
		liStackLevel = ASTACKINFO(la_Stack)
		
		lcMethod = m.la_Stack(m.liStackLevel, 3)
		lcMethod = PROPER(SUBSTRC(m.lcMethod, AT_C([.], m.lcMethod) + 1))
		lcProperty = LEFTC(m.lcMethod, LENC(m.lcMethod) - 7)
		
		lcMethodToCall = [LongBit]
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 9
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 5
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 58
		
		THIS.CallAccessObject(m.lcMethodToCall, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN EVALUATE([THIS.] + m.lcProperty)
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE abortcurrent_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the AbortCurrent property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            AbortCurrent_Assign
