	PROCEDURE markdowntohtml		&& Introduced in version 11.2.0. This method converts the Markdown content of this object to HTML, storing the result in sbHtml. It supports both streaming and full document conversion. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            MarkdownToHTML
		* Purpose:           This method converts the Markdown content of this object to HTML.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        toChilkatJSON, a Chilkat JSON object.
		*                    toChilkatStringBuilder, a Chilkat StringBuilder object.
		* Returns:           Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		* Date Added:        11/04/2025
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 11.2.0.
		**
		** This method converts the Markdown content of this object to HTML, storing the result in sbHtml.
		** It supports both streaming and full document conversion. Options specifies conversion options, 
		** including a key streaming option. In streaming mode, generated HTML is appended to sbHtml. 
		** In non-streaming mode, sbHtml is fully replaced by the generated HTML. 
		** For further details, see the examples linked below.
		** 
		** In streaming mode, only complete markdown lines are converted to HTML 
		** and removed from this object, leaving just the final partial line, if present. 
		** If this object contains only a partial markdown line, no HTML is emitted.
		** 
		** Starting in v11.3.0 ...
		**
		** "emitJavascript": true can be included in options to emit Javascript function calls instead of HTML. 
		** This is used to update the response in an embedded browser in real-time. 
		** See Real-Time Streaming AI Responses to Embedded Browsers in Desktop Apps
		**
		** "streamingShell": true is used to convert an empty string to an HTML shell to be used 
		** as the starting point before applying Javascript function calls. See Preparing the HTML Shell
		**
		** "theme": "html_theme_name" can be included when creating the HTML shell to select 
		** a predefined theme or when converting Markdown to HTML in non-streaming mode. The available themes are:
		**
		**   ChatGPT — A style that is similar to the ChatGPT application.
		**   cleanWin — A clean style for Windows applications.
		**   cleanMac — A clean style for MacOS applications.
		**   raw — No HTML styles, header, or body begin/end elements are emitted. 
		**   Only the Markdown to HTML generated elements are emitted.
		** 
		** If no theme is is included, then default HTML docType/root/body/header elements 
		** are emitted unless various parts are overridden by docType, rootElement, head, bodyStart, bodyEnd, and bodyExtra.
		**
		** "usesPrism": true can be included when creating the HTML shell (or when converting 
		** Markdown to HTML in non-streaming mode) to include PRISM code highlighting.
		**
		** "prism": { "theme": "prism_theme_name" } Is optional and can be used to specify 
		** the prism theme when usesPrism is true. Possible values are:
		**
		**     tomorrow
		**     default
		**     coy
		**     dark
		**     funky
		**     okaidia
		**     solarizedlight
		**     twilight
		**
		** "prism": { "version": "version_number" } Is optional can can be used to specify the prism version, 
		** such as "1.29.0" when usesPrism is true. If not specified, then "1.29.0" is used.
		**
		** If no theme is specified, then any or all of the following HTML document parts can be explicitly specified:
		**
		**    "docType": "doctype_element" The DOCTYPE element. The default is "<!DOCTYPE html>"
		**    "rootElement": "root_element" The html element. The default is "<html>"
		**    "head": "head_section" The HTML fragment for the HTML head section. 
		**     The default is "<head><meta charset="utf-8" /></head>".
		**    Note: If usesPrism is true, then prism related links will be inserted just before the </head>.
		**    "bodyStart": "html_fragment" The HTML fragment to begin the body section. The default is "<body><div id="content">"
		**    "bodyEnd": "html_fragment" The HTML fragment to end the body section. 
		**    The default is "</div><!-- end-of-content-div --></body>"
		**    "noContentDiv": true If set, the default bodyStart and bodyEnd do not include the "<div id="content">" 
		**    and "</div><!-- end-of-content-div -->"
		**    "copyButton": true In non-streaming mode, can optionally be set to include HTML for adding a copy button. 
		**    THe copy button is added by default in streaming mode.
		**    "ChatGPT": { "max-width": "css_length"; } Is optional can can be used to specify the max width 
		**    of the body text if the theme is ChatGPT. The css_length is a length using CSS length units, 
		**    such as "72ch", "40em", "800px", etc.
		**
		** Enhanced for version 11.3.0: Improved markdown to HTML conversion.
		**
		** Enhanced for version 11.4.0: Added support for image links. For example, markdown formatted like this: 
		** ![foo bar](/path/to/train.jpg "title" ) will convert to an HTML img tag like this: 
		** <img src="/path/to/train.jpg" alt="foo bar" title="title" />
		**
		** Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		** 
		
		LPARAMETERS toChilkatJSON AS CHILKAT_JSONOBJECT_COM_CALL, ;
		toChilkatStringBuilder AS CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, loParkParameterJson AS [iParkParameter OF ChilkatVFP.VCX], ;
		loChilkatJSON AS CHILKAT_JSONOBJECT_COM_CALL, liReturn AS Integer, luReturn AS Unknown
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterJson, m.loChilkatJSON
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(11, 2, 0)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      loParkParameterJson = ;
		      NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], .ClassLibrary, [], m.toChilkatJSON)
		
		      loChilkatJSON = m.loParkParameterJson.GetObject()
		
		      loParkParameterStringBuilder = ;
		      NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], .ClassLibrary, [], m.toChilkatJSON)
		
		      loChilkatStringBuilder = m.loParkParameterJson.GetObject()
		
		      TRY
		
		        STORE m.loChilkatObject.MarkdownToHTML(m.loChilkatJSON, ;
		        m.loChilkatStringBuilder) TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		      toChilkatJSON = ;
		      m.loParkParameterJson.SetObject(m.toChilkatJSON, m.loChilkatJSON)
		
		      toChilkatStringBuilder = ;
		      m.loParkParameterJson.SetObject(m.toChilkatStringBuilder, m.loChilkatStringBuilder)
		    
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		  luReturn = .BitToLogical(m.liReturn)
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterJson, m.loChilkatJSON, ;
		m.loParkParameterStringBuilder, m.loChilkatStringBuilder
		
		RETURN m.luReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL)
		  toChilkatJSON = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_JSONOBJECT_COM_CALL)
		  loParkParameterJson = NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], [ChilkatVFP.VCX])
		  loChilkatJSON = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_JSONOBJECT_COM_CALL)
		  toChilkatStringBuilder = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL)
		  loParkParameterStringBuilder = NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], [ChilkatVFP.VCX])
		  loChilkatStringBuilder = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE maskquotedstrings		&& Introduced in version 11.2.0. This function masks the content inside single and/or double-quoted strings by replacing it with a specified mask character (maskChar). The content of each masked quoted string is saved to maskedStrings.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            MaskQuotedStrings
		* Purpose:           This function masks the content inside single and/or double-quoted strings 
		*                    by replacing it with a specified mask character (maskChar).
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcMaskCharacter, the quoted mask character.
		*                    tiQuoteType, determines which types of quoted strings are masked.
		*                    toChilkatStringTable, a Chilkat StringTable object.
		* Returns:           Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		* Date Added:        10/31/2025
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 11.2.0
		**
		** Searches the content of this object for substrings that match a regular expression pattern 
		** and returns the matches in json. Returns the number of matches or -1 for failure. 
		** iTimeOutMs is the maximum number of milliseconds of processing allowed before giving up. 
		** Pass 0 for an infinite amount of time. Failure information is also returned in json.
		** 
		
		LPARAMETERS tcMaskCharacter AS Character, tiQuoteType AS Integer, ;
		toChilkatStringTable AS CHILKAT_STRINGTABLE_COM_CALL
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_STRINGTABLE_COM_CALL, ;
		loParkParameterStringTable AS [iParkParameter OF ChilkatVFP.VCX], ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, loChilkatStringTable AS CHILKAT_STRINGTABLE_COM_CALL, ;
		liReturn AS Integer, luReturn AS Unknown, loException AS Exception
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterStringTable, m.loChilkatStringTable
		STORE 0 TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(11, 2, 0)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      loParkParameterStringTable = ;
		      NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], .ClassLibrary, [], m.toChilkatStringTable)
		
		      loChilkatStringTable = m.loParkParameterStringTable.GetObject()
		
		      TRY
		
		        STORE m.loChilkatObject.MaskQuotedStrings(m.tcMaskCharacter, ;
		        m.tiQuoteType, m.loChilkatStringTable) TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		      toChilkatStringTable = ;
		      m.loParkParameterStringTable.SetObject(m.toChilkatStringTable, m.loChilkatStringTable)
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		  luReturn = .BitToLogical(m.liReturn)
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterStringTable, m.loChilkatStringTable
		
		RETURN m.lUReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_STRINGTABLE_COM_CALL)
		  toChilkatStringTable = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_STRINGTABLE_COM_CALL)
		  loParkParameterStringTable = NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], [ChilkatVFP.VCX])
		  loChilkatStringTable = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_STRINGTABLE_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE obfuscate		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.80. Obfuscates the string. (The Unobfuscate method can be called to reverse the obfuscation to restore the original string.)
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            Obfuscate
		* Purpose:           Obfuscates the string.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcString, the string to Obfuscate
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        03/09/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.80.
		**
		** Obfuscates the string. 
		** (The Unobfuscate method can be called to reverse the obfuscation 
		** to restore the original string.)
		**
		** The Chilkat string obfuscation algorithm works by taking the utf-8 bytes of the string, 
		** base64 encoding it, and then scrambling the letters of the base64 encoded string. 
		** It is deterministic in that the same string will always obfuscate to the same result. 
		** It is NOT a secure way of encrypting a string. 
		** It is only meant to be a simple means of transforming a string into something unintelligible.
		** 
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 80
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        m.loChilkatObject.Obfuscate()
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

