DEFINE CLASS task AS ibasechilkat OF "chilkatvfp.vcx" 		&& Represents a single task to be run in a background thread.
 	*< CLASSDATA: Baseclass="custom" Timestamp="" Scale="Pixels" Uniqueid="" />

	#INCLUDE "foxpro.h"
	*<DefinedPropArrayMethod>
		*m: cancel		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Marks an asynchronous task for cancellation.
		*m: clearprogresslog		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Removes all entries from the progress info log.
		*m: copyresultbytes		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Returns the binary bytes result of the task. The bytes are copied to the caller. Returns a zero-length byte array (as a Variant) on failure. An empty array will have a UBound of -1 meaning 0 elements.
		*m: debuglogfilepath_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task DebugLogFilePath property.
		*m: debuglogfilepath_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the DebugLogFilePath property.
		*m: finished_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task Fishished property.
		*m: finished_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Finished property.
		*m: getresultbool		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Returns the boolean result of the task.
		*m: getresultbytes		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Returns the binary bytes result of the task. The bytes are transferred to the caller, not copied. Call CopyResultBytes instead to copy the result bytes.
		*m: getresultint		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Returns the integer result of the task.
		*m: getresultstring		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Returns the string result of the task. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: heartbeatms_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task HeartbeatMs property.
		*m: heartbeatms_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the HeartbeatMs property.
		*m: inert_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task Inert property.
		*m: inert_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Inert property.
		*m: keepprogresslog_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task KeepProgressLog property.
		*m: keepprogresslog_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the KeepProgressLog property.
		*m: lastbinaryresult_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task LastBinaryResult property.
		*m: lastbinaryresult_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastBinaryResult property.
		*m: lasterrorhtml_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task LastErrorHTML property.
		*m: lasterrorhtml_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastErrorHTML property.
		*m: lasterrortext_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task LastErroText property.
		*m: lasterrortext_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastErrorText property.
		*m: lasterrorxml_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task LastErrorXML property.
		*m: lasterrorxml_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastErrorXML property.
		*m: lastmethodsuccess_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task LastMethodSuccess property.
		*m: lastmethodsuccess_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastMethodSuccess property.
		*m: laststringresultlen_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task LastStringResultLen property.
		*m: laststringresultlen_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastStringResultLen property.
		*m: laststringresult_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task LastStringResult property.
		*m: laststringresult_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the LastStringResult property.
		*m: live_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task Live property.
		*m: live_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Live property.
		*m: percentdone_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task PercentDone property.
		*m: percentdone_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the PercentDone property.
		*m: progressinfoname		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Returns the name of the Nth progress info event logged. The 1st entry is at index 0. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: progressinfovalue		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Returns the value of the Nth progress info event logged. The 1st entry is at index 0. Returns Nothing on failure.
		*m: progresslogsize_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task ProgressLogSize property.
		*m: progresslogsize_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ProgressLogSize property.
		*m: removeprogressinfo		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Removes the Nth progress info log entry.
		*m: resulterrortext_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task ReslutErrorText property.
		*m: resulterrortext_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ResultErrorText property.
		*m: resulttype_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task ResultType property.
		*m: resulttype_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the ResultType property.
		*m: run		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Queues the task to run on the internal Chilkat thread pool. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: runsynchronously		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Runs the task synchronously. Then this method returns after the task has been run. Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		*m: sleepms		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Convenience method to force the calling thread to sleep for a number of milliseconds. (This does not cause the task's background thread to sleep.)
		*m: statusint_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task StatusInt property.
		*m: statusint_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the StatusInt property.
		*m: status_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task Status property.
		*m: status_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Status property.
		*m: taskid_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task TaskID property.
		*m: taskid_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TaskID property.
		*m: tasksuccess_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task TaskSucess property.
		*m: tasksuccess_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the TaskSuccess property.
		*m: userdata_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task UserData property.
		*m: userdata_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the UserData property.
		*m: verboselogging_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat Task VerboseLogging property.
		*m: verboselogging_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the VerboseLogging property.
		*m: wait		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Waits for the task to complete. Returns when task has completed, or after maxWaitMs milliseconds have elapsed. (A maxWaitMs value of 0 is to wait indefinitely.)
		*p: debuglogfilepath		&& If set to a file path, causes each Chilkat method or property call to automatically append it's LastErrorText to the specified log file.
		*p: finished		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. 1 if the task status is "canceled", "aborted", or "completed".
		*p: heartbeatms		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The number of milliseconds between each AbortCheck event callback. The AbortCheck callback allows an application to abort the Wait method. If HeartbeatMs is 0 (the default), no AbortCheck event callbacks will fire.
		*p: inert		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. 1 if the task status is "empty" or "loaded". When a task is inert, it has been loaded but is not scheduled to run yet.
		*p: keepprogresslog		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Determines if the in-memory progress info event log is kept. The default value is 0 and therefore no log is kept. To enable progress info logging, set this property equal to 1 (prior to running the task).
		*p: lastbinaryresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The binary data returned by the last (binary data returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepBinaryResult is set to 1.
		*p: lasterrorhtml		&& Provides information in HTML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrortext		&& Provides information in plain-text format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lasterrorxml		&& Provides information in XML format about the last method/property called. If a method call returns a value indicating failure, or behaves unexpectedly, examine this property to get more information.
		*p: lastmethodsuccess		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Indicate whether the last method call succeeded or failed. A value of 1 indicates success, a value of 0 indicates failure. This property is automatically set for method calls.
		*p: laststringresult		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The string return value of the last (string returning) method called. Only available if Chilkat.Global.KeepStringResult is set to 1.
		*p: laststringresultlen		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.53. The length, in characters, of the string contained in the LastStringResult property.
		*p: live		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. 1 if the task status is "queued" or "running". When a task is live, it is either already running, or is on the thread pool thread's queue waiting for a thread to become available.
		*p: percentdone		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Indicates the percent completion while the task is running. The percent completed information is only available in cases where it is possible to know the percentage completed.
		*p: progresslogsize		&& What would normally be a ProgressInfo event callback (assuming Chilkat supports event callbacks for this language) is instead saved to an in-memory progress log that can be examined and pruned while the task is still running.
		*p: resulterrortext		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The LastErrorText for the task's asynchronous method.
		*p: resulttype		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Indicates the data type of the task's result. This property is only available after the task has completed. Possible values are "bool", "int", "string", "bytes", "object", and "void".
		*p: status		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The current status of the task.
		*p: statusint		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. The current status of the task as an integer value.
		*p: taskid		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. A unique integer ID assigned to this task. The purpose of this property is to help an application identify the task if a TaskCompleted event callback is used.
		*p: tasksuccess		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. This is the value of the LastMethodSuccess property of the underlying task object. This property is only valid for those methods where the LastMethodSuccess property would be valid had the method been called synchronousl
		*p: userdata		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. An application may use this property to attach some user-specific information with the task, which may be useful if a TaskCompleted event callback is used.
		*p: verboselogging		&& If set to 1, then the contents of LastErrorText (or LastErrorXml, or LastErrorHtml) may contain more verbose information. The default value is 0. Verbose logging should only be used for debugging.
	*</DefinedPropArrayMethod>

	*<PropValue>
		cchilkatclass = Task
		debuglogfilepath = 
		finished = 0
		heartbeatms = 0
		iinstancepatch = 52
		inert = 0
		keepprogresslog = 0
		lastbinaryresult = .NULL.
		lasterrorhtml = 
		lasterrortext = 
		lasterrorxml = 
		lastmethodsuccess = 1
		laststringresult = 
		laststringresultlen = 0
		live = 0
		Name = "task"
		percentdone = 0
		progresslogsize = 0
		resulterrortext = 
		resulttype = 
		status = 
		statusint = 0
		taskid = 0
		tasksuccess = 0
		userdata = 
		verboselogging = 0
	*</PropValue>
	
	PROCEDURE cancel		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Marks an asynchronous task for cancellation.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            Cancel
		* Purpose:           Marks an asynchronous task for cancellation.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        05/15/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.52
		**
		** Marks an asynchronous task for cancellation. 
		** The expected behavior depends on the current status of the task as described here:
		** 
		** "loaded" - If the task has been loaded but has not yet been queued 
		** to run in the thread pool, then there is nothing to do. 
		** (There is nothing to cancel because the task's Run method has not yet been called.) 
		** The task will remain in the "loaded" state.
		** 
		** "queued" - The task is marked for cancellation, is dequeued, and will not run. 
		** The task's status changes immediately to "canceled".
		** 
		** "running" - The already-running task is marked for cancellation. 
		** The task's status will eventually change to "aborted" when the asynchronous method returns. 
		** At that point in time, the ResultErrorText property will contain the "LastErrorText" 
		** of the method call. In the case where a task is marked for cancellation 
		** just at the time it's completing, the task status may instead change to "completed".
		** 
		** "canceled", "aborted", "completed" - In these cases the task has already finished, 
		** and there will be no change in status.
		** 
		** Cancel returns 1 if the task was in the "queued" or "running" state 
		** when it was marked for cancellation. Cancel returns 0 if the task was in any other state.
		** 
		** Important: Calling the Cancel method marks a task for cancellation. 
		** It sets a flag in memory that the running task will soon notice and then abort. 
		** It is important to realize that your application 
		** is likely calling Cancel from the main UI thread, 
		** whereas the asynchronous task is running in a background thread. 
		** If the task was in the "running" state when Cancel was called, 
		** it will still be in the "running" state when Cancel returns. 
		** It will take a short amount of time until the task actually aborts. 
		** This is because operating systems schedule threads in time slices, 
		** and the thread needs one or more time slices to notice the cancellation flag and abort. 
		** After calling Cancel, your application might wish to call 
		** the Wait method to wait until the task has actually aborted, 
		** or it could periodically check the task's status 
		** and then react once the status changes to "aborted".
		**
		** Fixed for version 64: This method was not working in the ActiveX.
		** Note: ChilkatVFP uses the ActiveX version of Chilkat.
		**
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_TASK_COM_CALL, loException AS Exception, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 52
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        m.loChilkatObject.Cancel()
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_TASK_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE chilkatchangelog
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ChilkatChangeLog
		* Purpose:           Documentation method used to hold 
		*                    the Chilkat class changes per release version.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        02/07/2024
		*==============================================================================
		
		#IF .F.
		
		TEXT
		
		** Version 65
		
		  ActiveX LastStringResultLen property incorrectly returned the size of the string in bytes (utf-16)
		  rather than in number of characters. This is fixed to return the number of characters.
		  (Note: this is a property that only exists in ActiveX classes, and is only useful
		  for certain programming languages such as SQL Server to help programs determine 
		  if temp tables are required.)
		
		** Version 64
		
		  Fixed: The Task.Cancel method was not working in the ActiveX.
		
		** Version 58
		
		  The Windows logged-on username is no longer automatically logged at the top of every LastErrorText.
		  (This was originally done to help w/ support issues so tht Chilkat might notice if the program runs
		  in the context of a Service or IIS, which could be a clue to the cause of certain problems.)
		
		  Added the AbortCurrent property to classes that can have event callbacks.
		
		** Version 53
		
		  The LastStringResultLen property is added to each Chilkat class.
		  This is helpful for certain programming languages such as DataFlex or SQL Server
		  where the size of the string returned may need to be known before using it.
		  Each Chilkat ActiveX object has its own LastStringResult and LastStringResultLen properties.
		  The KeepStringResult is a property of Chilkat.Global only.
		  (It may be confusing that Chilkat.Global also has a LastStringResult property —
		  but this is just like any other object.)
		
		  Therefore, your code would set Global.KeepStringResult once at the beginning of your code.
		
		  Let’s say you have an HttpResult object, and you want the BodyQP.
		  You would access the BodyQP, but ignore the string returned.
		  Then examine the HttpResult.LastStringResultLen, adjust your max string length (in DataFlex) if necessary,
		  and then get the cached string from HttpResult.LastStringResult.
		
		** Version 52
		
		  These new classes are part of the async functionality.
		
		ENDTEXT
		
		#ENDIF .F.
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE clearprogresslog		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.52. Removes all entries from the progress info log.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClearProgressLog
		* Purpose:           Marks an asynchronous task for ClearProgressLoglation.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
