	HIDDEN PROCEDURE behaviors_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat XMLDSigGen Behaviors property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            Behaviors_Access
		* Purpose:           Access method used to retrieve 
		*                    the Chilkat XMLDSigGen Behaviors property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           THIS.Behaviors
		* Date Added:        07/05/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.70
		**
		** A comma-separated list of keywords to specify special behaviors 
		** to work around potential oddities or special requirements needed 
		** for providing signatures to particular systems. 
		** This is an open-ended property where new behaviors can be implemented 
		** depending on the needs encountered by Chilkat customers. 
		** The possible behaviors are listed below.
		** 
		** AttributeSortingBug (introduced in v9.5.0.79) 
		** Tells Chilkat to produce a signature that duplicates 
		** a common XML canonicalization attribute sorting bug found 
		** in some XML signature implementations (such as JPK VAT signed XML documents 
		** for Polish government, i.e. mf.gov.pl, csioz.gov.pl, crd.gov.pl, etc). 
		** See XML Signature Canonicalization Bug for details.
		** 
		** Base64CrEntity Produce multi-line base64 for XML elements such as SignatureValue and X509Certificate, 
		** with each line ending in a CR hex entity, except for the last line. For example:
		**
		** <ds:X509Certificate>MIIFNTCCBB2gAwIBAgIQHozVnBl1lTsusAh26u6WZTANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQsFADCBlzELMAkGA1UE&#xD;
		** BhMCR0IxGzAZBgNVBAgTEkdyZWF0ZXIgTWFuY2hlc3RlcjEQMA4GA1UEBxMHU2FsZm9yZDEaMBgG&#xD;
		** A1UEChMRQ09NT0RPIENBIExpbWl0ZWQxPTA7BgNVBAMTNENPTU9ETyBSU0EgQ2xpZW50IEF1dGhl&#xD;
		...
		** sp3FRlACVeb1Qlytr4vgc5FlCqn0rMtjlF4=
		** </ds:X509Certificate>
		** 
		** Base64Cr13Entity Produce multi-line base64 for XML elements such as 
		** SignatureValue and X509Certificate, with each line ending in a CR decimal entity, 
		** except for the last line. For example:
		**
		** <ds:X509Certificate>MIIFNTCCBB2gAwIBAgIQHozVnBl1lTsusAh26u6WZTANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQsFADCBlzELMAkGA1UE&#13;
		** BhMCR0IxGzAZBgNVBAgTEkdyZWF0ZXIgTWFuY2hlc3RlcjEQMA4GA1UEBxMHU2FsZm9yZDEaMBgG&#13;
		** A1UEChMRQ09NT0RPIENBIExpbWl0ZWQxPTA7BgNVBAMTNENPTU9ETyBSU0EgQ2xpZW50IEF1dGhl&#13;
		** ...
		** sp3FRlACVeb1Qlytr4vgc5FlCqn0rMtjlF4=
		** </ds:X509Certificate>
		** 
		** Base64Multiline Produce multi-line base64 for XML elements such as SignatureValue and X509Certificate. 
		** For example:
		** 
		** <ds:X509Certificate>MIIFNTCCBB2gAwIBAgIQHozVnBl1lTsusAh26u6WZTANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQsFADCBlzELMAkGA1UE
		** BhMCR0IxGzAZBgNVBAgTEkdyZWF0ZXIgTWFuY2hlc3RlcjEQMA4GA1UEBxMHU2FsZm9yZDEaMBgG
		** A1UEChMRQ09NT0RPIENBIExpbWl0ZWQxPTA7BgNVBAMTNENPTU9ETyBSU0EgQ2xpZW50IEF1dGhl
		** 
		** ...
		** sp3FRlACVeb1Qlytr4vgc5FlCqn0rMtjlF4=
		** </ds:X509Certificate>
		**
		** ForceAddEnvelopedSignatureTransform The 
		** "<Transform Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#enveloped-signature" /> " 
		** is normally only added when the Signature is contained within the XML fragment 
		** that is signed. The meaning of this tranformation is to tell the verifier 
		** to remove the Signature from the data prior to canonicalizing. 
		** If the Signature is not contained within the XML fragment 
		** that was signed, then the signature was not enveloped. 
		** There would be no need to remove the Signature because the Signature 
		** is not contained in the XML fragment being verified. 
		** However... some brain-dead verifiying systems require this Transform 
		** to be present regardless of whether it makes sense. 
		** This behavior will cause Chilkat to add the Transform regardless.
		** 
		** NoEnvelopedSignatureTransform (introduced in v9.5.0.82) Prevents the 
		** "<Transform Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#enveloped-signature" /> " 
		** from being added in all cases.
		** 
		** EnvelopedTransformFirst (introduced in v9.5.0.87) 
		** Forces the http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#enveloped-signature to be listed 
		** first when there are multiple transforms for a reference.
		** 
		** ebXmlTransform (introduced in v9.5.0.73) Causes the following tranform 
		** to be added for ebXml messages:
		**   <Transform Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/TR/1999/REC-xpath-19991116">
		**       <XPath xmlns:SOAP-ENV="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/">not(ancestor-or-self::node()[@SOAP-ENV:actor="urn:oasis:names:tc:ebxml-msg:actor:nextMSH"]
		**         | ancestor-or-self::node()[@SOAP-ENV:actor="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/actor/next"])</XPath>
		**   </Transform>
		** 
		** TransformSignatureXPath (introduced in v9.5.0.75) Causes the following tranform to be added:
		**   <ds:Transform Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/TR/1999/REC-xpath-19991116">
		**      <ds:XPath>not(ancestor-or-self::ds:Signature)</ds:XPath>
		**   </ds:Transform>
		** 
		** CompactSignedXml (introduced in v9.5.0.73) The passed-in XML to be signed is first reformatted 
		** to a compact representation by removing all CR's, LF's, and unnecessary whitespace 
		** so that the XML to be signed is on a single line. The resulting XML (with signature) 
		** is also entirely contained on a single line. (If an XML declarator is present, 
		** then it will remain on it's own line.)
		** 
		** IndentedSignature (introduced in v9.5.0.73) Causes the XML Signature to be produced 
		** on multiple lines with indentation for easier human readability. 
		** The CompactSignedXml behavior takes precedence over this behavior.
		** 
		** FullLocalSigningTime (introduced in v9.5.0.76) Causes the signing time to be formatted like this: 
		** 2017-05-20T19:16:05.649+01:00.nnn, where the ".nnn" is added to indicate milliseconds.
		** 
		** LocalSigningTime (introduced in v9.5.0.76) Causes the signing time to be formatted 
		** using a local time (with a timezone offset such as "+01:00" rather than "Z" to signify GMT).
		** 
		** NoReplaceSigningTime Don't replace the <SigningTime> content with a timestamp of the current date/time. 
		** Instead keep the current value provided by the application.
		** 
		** NoTimestampBias Exclude the timestamp bias from the generated <SigningTime>
		**
		** DnReverseOrder (introduced in v9.5.0.77) Causes DN's (certificate Distinguished Names) 
		** to be written in reverse order. Reverse order leads with "CN", 
		** such as "CN=..., O=..., OU=..., C=...", whereas normal order ends with "CN", 
		** such as "C=..., OU=..., O=..., CN=..."
		** 
		** IssuerSerialHex (introduced in v9.5.0.77) Causes the issuer serial number located 
		** in SignedProperties.SignedSignatureProperties.SigningCertificate to be emitted 
		** as uppercase hex instead of decimal. (Also, when signing XML for e-dokumenty.mf.gov.pl, 
		** Chilkat automatically recognizes it and uses IssuerSerialHex.)
		** 
		** IssuerSerialHexLower (introduced in v9.5.0.77) Causes the issuer serial number located 
		** in SignedProperties.SignedSignatureProperties.SigningCertificate to be emitted 
		** as lowercase hex instead of decimal.
		** 
		** SigningTimeAdjust-<numSeconds> (introduced in v9.5.0.80) When Chilkat automatically fills 
		** in the value for a SigningTime, it will use the current system date/time. 
		** This behavior can be used to adjust the generate time to numSeconds in the past. 
		** For example: "SigningTimeAdjust-60" will generate a signing time 60 seconds prior to the current time.
		** 
		** SigningTimeAdjust+<numSeconds> (introduced in v9.5.0.88) When Chilkat automatically fills 
		** in the value for a SigningTime, it will use the current system date/time. 
		** This behavior can be used to adjust the generate time to numSeconds in the future. 
		** For example: "SigningTimeAdjust+60" will generate a signing time 60 seconds past the current time.
		** 
		** UBLDocumentSignatures Causes an XPath "ancestor-or-self" Transform to be added for the 1st reference. 
		** See the example at UBL XAdES Enveloped Signature
		** 
		** SignExistingSignatures This keyword can be used when applying a 2nd or greater signature 
		** and the new signature will encompass one or more existing signatures. 
		** The default behavior is that existing signatures are not included 
		** in the canonicalization/digest before signing. 
		** Adding this keyword will cause existing signatures to be included in the canonicalization/digest.
		**
		** Note: The AttributeSortingBug keyword was being ignored until version 95.
		** 
		
		LOCAL liStackLevel AS Integer, lcMethod AS Character, ;
		lcProperty AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_Stack[1, 1], la_IntroducedInBuild[3, 1]
		
		STORE [] TO m.lcMethod, m.lcProperty, m.lcMethodToCall, m.la_Stack, m.la_IntroducedInBuild
		
		liStackLevel = ASTACKINFO(la_Stack)
		
		lcMethod = m.la_Stack(m.liStackLevel, 3)
		lcMethod = PROPER(SUBSTRC(m.lcMethod, AT_C([.], m.lcMethod) + 1))
		lcProperty = LEFTC(m.lcMethod, LENC(m.lcMethod) - 7)
		
		lcMethodToCall = [String]
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 9
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 5
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 70
		
		THIS.CallAccessObject(m.lcMethodToCall, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN EVALUATE([THIS.] + m.lcProperty)
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE behaviors_assign		&& Assign method used to hold a reference to the Behaviors property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            Behaviors_Assign
		* Purpose:           Assign method used to hold a reference to the Behaviors property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcValue, character value used to hold 
		*                    a reference to the Behaviors property.
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        07/05/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		LPARAMETERS tcValue AS Character
		
		LOCAL lcValidationMethod AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_IntroducedInBuild[3, 1]
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 9
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 5
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 70
		
		lcValidationMethod = [Behaviors]
		lcMethodToCall = [String]
		
		THIS.CallAssignObject(m.tcValue, m.lcMethodToCall, m.lcValidationMethod, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE chilkatchangelog
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ChilkatChangeLog
		* Purpose:           Documentation method used to hold 
		*                    the Chilkat class changes per release version.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        02/03/2024
		*==============================================================================
		
		#IF .F.
		
		TEXT
		
		** Version 11.5.0
		
		 Fixed a problem with handling the 
		 <XPath xmlns=http://www.w3.org/2002/06/xmldsig-filter2 Filter=”intersect”> transform.
		
		** Version 11.4.0
		
		  CreateXmlDSigSb, CreateXmlDSig — If both an enveloped-signature transform and a c14n transform 
		  exist in a single reference, then it will be ensured that the enveloped-signature transform 
		  precedes the c14n transform.
		
		** Version 11.2.0
		
		  Added base62 encoding as an additional encoding choice recognized throughout Chilkat.
		
		** Version 11.1.0
		
		  Added the SigLocationIdx property.
		
		** Version 10.1.2
		
		  In v10.0.0 Chilkat started automatically using and fixing for SigningCertificateV2 
		  for cases where the xmlns:xades=”http://uri.etsi.org/01903/v1.3.2#” (and also v1.4.1 and v1.4.2), 
		  which is technically correct. However many govt validators, specifically Poland, Saudia Arabia, 
		  and others, reject XML signatures using SigningCertificateV2. 
		 
		  Chilkat backed out this “fix” and will revisit the issue in the future.
		
		** Version 10.1
		
		  Fixed the ability to use X509Data+KeyValue or KeyValue for the KeyInfo when
		  non-accessible key is used for signing.
		
		** Version 10.0
		
		  Fixed a problem having to do with sending OCSP requests for ECDSA based certificates.
		
		** Version 99
		
		  Added “Base45” to the set of binary encodings supported by Chilkat. 
		  “base45” can now be used in any Chilkat function or property 
		  where a binary encoding such as “base64”, “hex”, “base58”, etc., can be used.
		
		** Version 96
		
		  Added the “NoTimestampBias” keyword to emit signing times without the timezone bias.
		  For example, “2023-08-06T15:36:29”. This is needed for certain picky Turkish government validators.
		
		** Version 95
		
		  The “AttributeSortingBug” Behavior was getting ignored.
		  This caused signed XML documents to be rejected by some Polish government services
		  where it is necessary to reproduce a bug in XML canonicalization
		  in order for signed documents to be accepted.
		
		  Chilkat is working better with several Brazilian government servers.
		  (Such that the XML digital signatures produced by Chilkat are accepted
		  by the Brazilian government servers. The difficulty was in getting the settings just right.)
		
		  Fixed OCSP requests for ECDSA certificates. This problem also caused PDF signatures
		  using ECDSA cerificates to not be LTV-enabled.
		
		** Version 94
		
		  Chilkat improved OCSP requests (used in various parts of the Chilkat API)
		  to satisfy some servers that are more picky about certain parts
		  of the OCSP protocol which should be optional.
		
		  Fixed some problems relating to creating signed XML invoices for SII Chile.
		
		  Added intelligence for XmlDSigGen to automatically detect when signing for
		  SRI – SISTEMA DE COMPROBANTES ELECTRONICOS (Ecuador) to produce output in the needed format.
		
		** Version 91
		
		  No longer automatically adds the Id attribute to the Signature element.
		  This caused problems with certain servers that verify XML signatures, such as SII en Chile.
		  (Technically it should NOT cause any problems — the problems are really a deficiency on the validation side.
		  The presence of an Id attribute in the Signature element should NOT cause a failure.)
		
		** Version 90
		
		  Added the AddObjectRef2 and AddSameDocRef2 methods to allow
		  for a more precise specification of the transforms to be applied when signing.
		
		  Added the ability to include an EncapsulatedTimeStamp when signing.
		  The SetTsa method was added to provide the URL for the timestamping authority.
		
		** Version 85
		
		  Fixed problem when X509Type property includes “SubjectName”
		  AND the signing certificate has a subject name that includes the ‘&’ char.
		
		** Version 83
		
		  Improved support for ECDSA certs.
		
		** Version 80
		
		  Added “SigningTimeAdjust” to the list of Behaviors.
		 
		** Version 79
		
		  Fixed: References to elements that are empty (have no children) caused
		  a “Did not find same-document Reference Id” error when signing.
		
		  Encoding: Added ascii85 encoding/decoding to the list of supported binary encoding algorithms.
		  “ascii85” can be used anywhere in the Chilkat API where an encoding
		  such as “base64”, “hex”, “base58”, etc. is used.
		
		  Added the “AttributeSortingBug” Behavior to allow an application
		  to duplicate a bug found in other software implementations.
		
		** Version 77
		
		  Added the “IssuerSerialHex” and “IssuerSerialHexLower” behaviors (to the Behaviors property)
		  to emit hex issuer serial numbers instead of decimal
		  in the SignedProperties.SignedSignatureProperties.SigningCertificate.
		  Also, when signing content for “e-dokumenty.mf.gov.pl”, Chilkat will automatically recognize
		  that IssuerSerialHex is required and will do it automatically.
		
		  Fixed a bug in XML canonicalization. This problem occurred when the default namespace
		  is defined at the root node, and exclusive canonicalization (EXCL_C14N) is used,
		  and a fragment is canonicalized where no usage of the default namespace exists
		  and non-qualified attribute names were used.
		  (It is a situation that is not common and therefore was not noticed for quite some time.)
		
		  When the SigLocation points to an empty element tag (a tag that is self-closed),
		  Chilkat would insert the signature after the closed tag.
		  Now it correctly expands the tag so that the signature is placed within.
		
		** Version 76
		
		  Added automatic internal behaviors to produce signatures as needed by www.cioz.gov.pl.
		  For example, if the XML data indicates www.cioz.gov.pl,
		  then Chilkat produce signatures in the particular way that is required.
		
		  Added the “FullLocalSigningTime” and “LocalSigningTime” keywords to the Behaviors property.
		
		** Version 75
		
		  Many improvements and fixes to XML digital signature generation and verification…
		
		  Added the “TransformSignatureXPath” keyword to the Behaviors property.
		
		  Added the SignedInfoId property.
		
		  Added the KeyInfoId property.
		
		  Added the SetRefIdAttr method.
		
		  Added the “hexlower” encoding. “hexlower” may be used instead of “hex”
		  to get the hexadecimal encoding using lowercase a-f (“hex” produces uppercase A-F).
		
		** Version 73
		
		  Now capable of using non-exportable private keys on Windows,
		  such as for A3 certificates where the private key is on a hardware token.
		
		  Added the “X509Data+KeyValue” option for the KeyInfoType property.
		
		  Fixed: The X509SerialNumber in the X509IssuerSerial needed to be in decimal, not hex.
		
		** Version 71
		
		  Added support for XML canonicalization WithComments algorithms.
		
		** Version 70
		
		  Added the IncNamespacePrefix and IncNamespaceUri properties.
		
		  Added a special behavior for the prefixList argument of the AddSameDocRef method.
		  The keyword “_EMPTY_” may be passed to force the generation of an InclusiveNamespaces element
		  with an empty PrefixList under the Transform element.
		  See the online reference documentation for details.
		
		  Added the Behaviors property to account for special needs.
		  See the online reference documentation for details.
		
		** Version 69
		
		  Chilkat introduces two new classes for creating and verifying XML Digital Signatures:
		  XmlDSig (for verification) and XmlDSigGen for generating XML signatures.
		  More examples will be available soon.
		
		ENDTEXT
		
		#ENDIF .F.
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE constructsignedinfo		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.74. This method will construct and return the canonicalized SignedInfo XML. The digests of each Reference are computed and included in the SignedInfo.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ConstructSignedInfo
		* Purpose:           This method will construct and return the canonicalized SignedInfo XML. 
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        toChilkatStringBuilder, a Chilkat String Builder object.
		* Returns:           The canonicalized SignedInfo XML.
		* Date Added:        07/05/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.74
		**
		** This method will construct and return the canonicalized SignedInfo XML. 
		** The digests of each Reference are computed and included in the SignedInfo. 
		** This method is provided for certain special circumstances 
		** where one wants to get the exact canonicalized SignedInfo 
		** that would be signed using the private key.
		** 
		** Note: Properties such as SigLocation, SigningAlg, etc. 
		** and references must be set exactly as if an XML signature 
		** was to be actually generated because they determine the content of the SignedInfo.
		** 
		** Note, the sbXml is not signed by this method. It is not modified.
		** 
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS toChilkatStringBuilder AS CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_XMLDSIGGEN_COM_CALL, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		loException AS Exception, lcSignedInfoXML AS Character
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		lcSignedInfoXML = []
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 74
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        lcSignedInfoXML = ;
		        m.loChilkatObject.ConstructSignedInfo(loChilkatStringBuilder)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcSignedInfoXML
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_XMLDSIGGEN_COM_CALL)
		  toChilkatStringBuilder = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE createxmldsig		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.69. Creates an XML Digital Signature. The application passes in the XML to be signed, and the signed XML is returned.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            CreateXMLDSig
		* Purpose:           Creates an XML Digital Signature.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        tcXML, a Chilkat String Builder object.
		* Returns:           The canonicalized SignedInfo XML.
		* Date Added:        07/05/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.69
		**
		** Creates an XML Digital Signature. 
		** The application passes in the XML to be signed, and the signed XML is returned. 
		** If creating an enveloping signature where the Signature element is the root, 
		** then the inXml may be the empty string.
		** 
		** Chilkat v9.5.0.76 or greater is required for XML signatures for www.csioz.gov.pl
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 11.4.0: If both an enveloped-signature transform 
		** and a c14n transform exist in a single reference, then it will be ensured that the 
		** enveloped-signature transform precedes the c14n transform.
		** 
		** Returns Nothing on failure
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS tcXML AS Character
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_XMLDSIGGEN_COM_CALL, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		loException AS Exception, lcSignedXML AS Character
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		lcSignedXML = []
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 69
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      TRY
		
		        lcSignedXML = m.loChilkatObject.CreateXMLDSig(m.tcXML)
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException
		
		RETURN m.lcSignedXML
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_XMLDSIGGEN_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	PROCEDURE createxmldsigsb		&& Introduced in version 9.5.0.69. Creates an XML Digital Signature. The application passes the XML to be signed in sbXml, and it is replaced with the signed XML if successful. (Thus, sbXml is both an input and output argument.)
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            CreateXMLDSigSb
		* Purpose:           Creates an XML Digital Signature.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        toChilkatStringBuilder, a Chilkat String Builder object.
		* Returns:           Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		* Date Added:        07/05/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		**
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.69
		**
		** Creates an XML Digital Signature. The application passes the XML to be signed 
		** in sbXml, and it is replaced with the signed XML if successful. 
		** (Thus, sbXml is both an input and output argument.) 
		** Note: If creating an enveloping signature where the Signature element 
		** is to be the root element, then the passed-in sbXml may be empty.
		**
		** Enhancement for Version 11.4.0: If both an enveloped-signature transform 
		** and a c14n transform exist in a single reference, then it will be ensured that the 
		** enveloped-signature transform precedes the c14n transform.
		** 
		** Returns 1 for success, 0 for failure.
		**
		
		LPARAMETERS toChilkatStringBuilder AS CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL
		
		LOCAL loChilkatObject AS CHILKAT_XMLDSIGGEN_COM_CALL, ;
		llImplemented AS Logical, liIntroducedInBuild AS Integer, ;
		loParkParameterStringBuilder AS [iParkParameter OF ChilkatVFP.VCX], ;
		loChilkatStringBuilder AS CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL, ;
		loException AS Exception, liReturn AS Integer, luReturn AS Unknown
		
		STORE 0 TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn, m.liIntroducedInBuild
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterStringBuilder, m.loChilkatStringBuilder
		
		llImplemented = .F.
		liIntroducedInBuild = 69
		
		WITH THIS
		
		  llImplemented = .IsPEMImplemented(9, 5, m.liIntroducedInBuild)
		
		  ** Method implemented test
		  IF m.llImplemented
		
		    loChilkatObject = .oChilkat
		
		    ** Have a good object test
		    IF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		
		      loParkParameterStringBuilder = ;
		      NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], .ClassLibrary, [], m.toChilkatStringBuilder)
		
		      loChilkatStringBuilder = m.loParkParameterStringBuilder.GetObject()
		
		      TRY
		
		        STORE m.loChilkatObject.CreateXMLDSigSb(m.loChilkatStringBuilder) ;
		        TO m.liReturn, m.luReturn
		
		      CATCH TO m.loException
		
		        .CallToChilkatError(m.loException, THIS)
		
		      ENDTRY
		
		      toChilkatStringBuilder = m.loParkParameterStringBuilder.SetObject(;
		      m.toChilkatStringBuilder, m.loChilkatStringBuilder)
		
		    ELSE
		
		      .MissingObjectError(THIS)
		
		    ENDIF VARTYPE(m.loChilkatObject) == T_OBJECT ;
		    AND (NOT ISNULL(m.loChilkatObject))
		    ** End have a good object test
		
		  ENDIF m.llImplemented
		  ** End method implemented test
		
		  luReturn = .BitToLogical(m.liReturn)
		
		ENDWITH
		
		STORE NULL TO m.loChilkatObject, m.loException, ;
		m.loParkParameterStringBuilder, m.loChilkatStringBuilder
		
		RETURN m.luReturn
		
		** Design time IntelliSense test
		#IF .F.
		
		  loChilkatObject = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_XMLDSIGGEN_COM_CALL)
		  toChilkatStringBuilder = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL)
		  loParkParameterStringBuilder = NEWOBJECT([iParkParameter], [ChilkatVFP.VCX])
		  loChilkatStringBuilder = NEWOBJECT(CHILKAT_STRINGBUILDER_COM_CALL)
		  loException = NEWOBJECT([Exception])
		
		#ENDIF .F.
		** End design time IntelliSense test
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE customkeyinfoxml_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat XMLDSigGen CustomKeyInfoXML property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            CustomKeyInfoXML_Access
		* Purpose:           Access method used to retrieve 
		*                    the Chilkat XMLDSigGen CustomKeyInfoXML property.
