	HIDDEN PROCEDURE siglocation_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat XMLDSigGen SigLocation property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            SigLocation_Access
		* Purpose:           Access method used to retrieve 
		*                    the Chilkat XMLDSigGen SigLocation property.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           THIS.SigLocation
		* Date Added:        07/05/2022
		*==============================================================================
		
		** 
		** Introduced in version 9.5.0.69
		**
		** Indicates where the Signature is to be located within the XML that is signed. 
		** This is a path to the position in the XML where the Signature will be inserted, 
		** using Chilkat path syntax (using vertical bar characters to delimit tag names). 
		** If the Signature element is to be the root of XML document, 
		** then set this property equal to the empty string.
		** 
		** For example, if we have the following SOAP XML and wish to insert the Signature at the indicated location, then the SigLocation property should be set to "SOAP-ENV:Envelope|SOAP-ENV:Header|wsse:Security".
		** 
		**   <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
		**   <SOAP-ENV:Envelope xmlns:SOAP-ENV="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/">
		**       <SOAP-ENV:Header>
		**     <wsse:Security xmlns:wsse="http://docs.oasis-open.org/wss/2004/01/oasis-200401-wss-wssecurity-secext-1.0.xsd" SOAP-ENV:mustUnderstand="1">
		**       ** The XML Signature is to be inserted here **
		**     </wsse:Security>
		**       </SOAP-ENV:Header>
		**   ...
		**   </SOAP-ENV:Envelope>
		**
		** Fix for version 77: When this method points to an empty element tag (a tag that is self-closed), 
		** Chilkat would insert the signature after the closed tag. Now it correctly expands the tag 
		** so that the signature is placed within.
		** 
		
		LOCAL liStackLevel AS Integer, lcMethod AS Character, ;
		lcProperty AS Character, lcMethodToCall AS Character
		
		LOCAL ARRAY la_Stack[1, 1], la_IntroducedInBuild[3, 1]
		
		STORE [] TO m.lcMethod, m.lcProperty, m.lcMethodToCall, m.la_Stack, m.la_IntroducedInBuild
		
		liStackLevel = ASTACKINFO(la_Stack)
		
		lcMethod = m.la_Stack(m.liStackLevel, 3)
		lcMethod = PROPER(SUBSTRC(m.lcMethod, AT_C([.], m.lcMethod) + 1))
		lcProperty = LEFTC(m.lcMethod, LENC(m.lcMethod) - 7)
		
		lcMethodToCall = [String]
		
		la_IntroducedInBuild[1] = 9
		la_IntroducedInBuild[2] = 5
		la_IntroducedInBuild[3] = 69
		
		THIS.CallAccessObject(m.lcMethodToCall, @m.la_IntroducedInBuild)
		
		RETURN EVALUATE([THIS.] + m.lcProperty)
	ENDPROC

