	PROCEDURE chilkatchangelog
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ChilkatChangeLog
		* Purpose:           Documentation method used to hold 
		*                    the Chilkat class changes per release version.
		* Author:            Bill Anderson
		* Notice:            Copyright (c) 2022 - 2026 The Anderson Files LLC, All Rights Reserved.
		* Parameters:        
		* Returns:           
		* Date Added:        02/03/2024
		*==============================================================================
		
		#IF .F.
		
		TEXT
		
		** Version 11.5.0
		
		  Fixed the AppendZip method.
		
		** Version 11.2.0
		
		  Added base62 encoding as an additional encoding choice recognized throughout Chilkat.
		
		** Version 11.0.0
		
		  Removed the UnlockComponent method.
		
		  Removed the IsUnlocked method.
		
		  Added the AddBd, AddEmpty, AddEncoded, AddFile, AddSb, AddString, 
		  EntryAt, EntryByID, EntryMatching and EntryOf methods.
		
		  Decremented the AppendBd, AppendData, AppendDataEncoded, AppendNew,
		  AppendOneFileOrDir, APpendOneFileOrDirAsync, AppendSb, AppendString,
		  AppendString2, FirstEntry, FirstMatchingEntry, GetByEntryID, 
		  GetEntryByIndex, GetEntryByName and GetExclusions methods.
		
		** Version 10.0.0
		
		  Fixed: When unzipping on Windows, filenames beginning with “.” would unzip with the “.” removed.  
		  Thus, “.xyz”  would become the file named “xyz”.
		
		  Added the AppendSb method.
		
		  Added the MinDate and MaxDate properties.
		
		  The following methods and properties are now decremented:
		
		  AppendBase64
		  AppendCompressed
		  AddEmbedded
		  AppendHex
		  AppendMultiple
		  OpenMyEmbedded
		  RemoveEmbedded
		  ReplaceEmbedded  
		  TextFlag (property)
		
		** Version 99
		
		  Added “Base45” to the set of binary encodings supported by Chilkat. 
		  “base45” can now be used in any Chilkat function or property 
		  where a binary encoding such as “base64”, “hex”, “base58”, etc., can be used.
		
		** Version 98
		
		  Fixed a problem with the QuickAppend method, which only occurred on non-Windows systems.
		
		** Version 96
		
		  Added the MaxUncompressSize property. An application can set this property
		  to prevent unzipping any files larger than a max size uncompressed.
		
		  Added the GetMaxUncompressedSize method. After opening a .zip,
		  the application can call this method to return the size of the file contained
		  within the Zip that has the largest uncompressed size.
		
		** Version 94
		
		  Fixed a problem when trying to include non-us-ascii chars in the Zip file comment.
		
		** Version 92
		
		  Fixed: When zipping files on Windows, the file archive attribute
		  was not maintained w/ the file entry created within the zip.
		
		** Version 87
		
		  Fixed ZIP64 problems encountered when opening a ZIP64 file, removing entries, and rewriting.
		
		** Version 79
		
		  Encoding: Added ascii85 encoding/decoding to the list of supported binary encoding algorithms.
		  “ascii85” can be used anywhere in the Chilkat API where an encoding such as “base64”, “hex”, “base58”, etc. is used.
		
		  Fixed: The UnzipTree method did not remove the base64 compressed content from the XML element after unzipping.
		
		** Version 78
		
		  Fixed internal problem mainly involving emoji chars.
		  The actual problem had to do with internal utf-8 to utf-16 conversion
		  when surrogate pairs are present
		  (and emoji chars are the typical chars where surrogate pairs occur).
		
		** Version 75
		
		  Added the “hexlower” encoding. “hexlower” may be used instead of “hex”
		  to get the hexadecimal encoding using lowercase a-f (“hex” produces uppercase A-F).
		
		  Fixed rare problems involved with rewriting zip archives, when the “move from temp zip to target” fails.
		
		** Version 73
		
		  Added the PwdProtCharset property.
		
		** Version 70
		
		  Fixed the ability to create zips using any of PPMD, LZMA, and Bzip2 compression.
		
		  Fixed the AppendString2 method to not include the utf-8 preamble when the charset argument is “utf-8”.
		
		** Version 69
		
		  Fixed the ZipAppendOneFileOrDir method for the case when a UNC path is passed.
		
		** Version 67
		
		  Added the “base64_mime” to the list of possible encodings.
		  This is the same as “base64”, but causes the base64 to be emitted
		  in lines just like it would be found in MIME or in a PEM.
		
		** Version 66
		
		  Added the Zip.OpenBd and Zip.WriteBd methods
		  to open from a BinData object, and to write to a BinData object.
		
		** Version 65
		
		  Added the “eda” encoding for UN/EDIFACT Syntax Level A.
		  See https://www.example-code.com/foxpro/edifact_eda_syntax_level_A_encoding.asp
		  Also see: https://cknotes.com/chilkat-binary-encoding-list/
		
		  ActiveX LastStringResultLen property incorrectly returned the size of the string in bytes (utf-16)
		  rather than in number of characters. This is fixed to return the number of characters.
		  (Note: this is a property that only exists in ActiveX classes, and is only useful
		  for certain programming languages such as SQL Server to help programs determine
		  if temp tables are required.)
		
		** Version 59
		
		  Added the AppendDataEncoded method.
		
		  Fixed a problem w/ encrypted zips for Unicode C++ (CkZipW) on Mac OS X.
		  The issue has to do with the fact that wchar_t is 4 bytes per char (on Mac OS X)
		  as opposed to 2 bytes per char.
		
		** Version 58
		
		  The Windows logged-on username is no longer automatically logged at the top of every LastErrorText.
		  (This was originally done to help w/ support issues so tht Chilkat might notice if the program runs
		  in the context of a Service or IIS, which could be a clue to the cause of certain problems.)
		
		  Added the AbortCurrent property to classes that can have event callbacks.
		
		** Version 56
		
		  Memory leak fixed.
		
		** Version 55
		
		  Fixed a problem with OpenZipAsync where the 1st call would succeed, but subsequent calls would fail.
		
		** Version 54
		
		  Fixed: Error in rewriting a ZIP64 zip (larger then 4GB or having more than 65536 files).
		  There was an error when a large zip was opened, potentially modified, and rewritten.
		
		** Version 53
		
		  The LastStringResultLen property is added to each Chilkat class.
		  This is helpful for certain programming languages such as DataFlex or SQL Server
		  where the size of the string returned may need to be known before using it
		  Each Chilkat ActiveX object has its own LastStringResult and LastStringResultLen properties.
		  The KeepStringResult is a property of Chilkat.Global only.
		  (It may be confusing that Chilkat.Global also has a LastStringResult property —
		  but this is just like any other object.)
		
		  Therefore, your code would set Global.KeepStringResult once at the beginning of your code.
		
		  Let’s say you have an HttpResult object, and you want the BodyQP.
		  You would access the BodyQP, but ignore the string returned.
		  Then examine the HttpResult.LastStringResultLen, adjust your max string length (in DataFlex) if necessary,
		  and then get the cached string from HttpResult.LastStringResult.
		
		  The WriteExe method was fixed for cases where a contained file is extremely large.
		
		** Version 52
		
		  Added asynchronous functionality for all qualifying methods
		  across all programming languages, operating systems, and architectures.
		  Each Chilkat method that can potentially be time-consuming or involve network communications,
		  now has a corresponding asynchronous version of the method with the name ending in “Async”.
		
		  Added the LastMethodSuccess property.
		
		** Version 49
		
		  Added PercentDoneScale property to FTP2, Http, Tar, Zip, SFtp, MailMan, Imap, Upload.
		
		  Fixed problem where backslashes in paths were not automatically getting converted to forward slashes.
		
		** Version 48
		
		  For files skipped because of access-denied or file-not-found,
		  the FileZipped event fired when it should not have.
		  This was fixed, and in addition a ProgressInfo event was added for each occurance,
		  using the names “fileAccessDenied” and “fileNotFound”.
		  (Each Progress info event has two params: a name and value where the name identifies the event,
		  and the value contains information specific to the event.)
		
		  AppendFilesEx w/ ArchiveOnly=true omitted directory entries,
		  which was unnoticed when the directory contained files because the files still get added
		  and unzip software automatically re-creates directories when unzipping as needed.
		  However, this is noticed for empty directories because the empty directory entries were not added to the .zip.
		
		** Version 44
		
		  Added the ExtractExe method to Chilkat.Zip.
		
		  New: New self-extracting EXE config params are available.
		  These have to do with the information that would be seen in Windows Explorer for the .exe file:
		  CompanyName, FileDescription, InternalName, LegalCopyright, OriginalFilename, and ProductName.
		  Each can be set via the zip.SetExeConfigParam method.
		  For example: zip.SetExeConfigParam(“CompanyName”,”Acme Software, Inc.”);
		
		** Version 40
		
		  Review the online reference documentation for new methods or properties
		  for Ftp2, TrustedRoots, Rsa, Mime, Cert, Email, Imap, MailMan, Crypt2,
		  Http, Zip, Pfx, XmlCertVault, CertChain, and Upload.
		  New entries are clearly marked by the version in which they are introduced.
		
		** Version 38
		
		  Fixed a minor issue with writing AES encrypted Zips — the CRC written to the local file header
		  and central directory record within the zip format was the correct CRC, but it is preferred to write a 0.
		  This caused no actual problem, but it now conforms to what is preferred for AES encrypted zip archives.
		
		ENDTEXT
		
		#ENDIF .F.
	ENDPROC

	HIDDEN PROCEDURE cleararchiveattribute_access		&& Access method used to retrieve the Chilkat ZIP ClearArchiveAttribute property.
		*==============================================================================
		* Method:            ClearArchiveAttribute_Access
		* Purpose:           Set this to 1 to clear the FILE_ATTRIBUTE_ARCHIVE 
